window.DETAILS = {"cars":{"asphalt-acura-arx-06-gtp":{"hp":"667","kg":"1030","lbs":"2271","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Acura AR24e 2.4L V6 twin-turbocharged","year":"2023","wiki_type":"LMDh / GTP","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"Another LMDh / GTP car on the service, the Acura ARX-06 is one of Acura's racing thoroughbreds designed and built to take on BMW, Cadillac, Ferrari, and Porsche. The car features many innovations, technology, and impressive performance figures guaranteed to make it one to watch out for on raceday. To start off, the car has a carbon fiber monocoque chassis and a double wishbone with pushrod suspension front and rear with Penske dampers giving the car ample durability, toughness, and a comfortable handling model that will be well-suited for many drivers alike. Other features on the car include a FIA-specified roll cage structure, carbon fiber driver's seat shell, six-point safety harness, fresh air intake system, and on-board fire suppression system for max safety for the driver. With an IMSA-specified XTrac six-speed, sequential, paddle-operated transmission and a engine producing over 650 hp, this makes the Acura ARX-06 a LMDh / GTP car ready for the battlegrounds of raceday war.","wiki_title":"Acura ARX-06 LMDh / GTP","kg_per_hp":"1.54","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-acura-nsx-gt3-evo-22":{"hp":"520","kg":"1320","lbs":"2910","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"3.5L Twin-Turbocharged DOHC V6 ICE","year":"2022","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Another GT3 addition to a very healthy field, Acura's NSX GT3 Evo 22 storms onto the racing scene to compete against Audi, BMW, Chevrolet, Ferrari, Ford, Lamborghini, McLaren, Mercedes-Benz, and Porsche. Featuring a powerful 3.5L Twin-Turbocharged DOHC V6 ICE engine making just over 500 horsepower, while it has less power than a number of its counterparts, it seems adequate for its weight, fuel mileage, and acceleration time. The car also features the latest in GT3 racing technology like an aluminum monocoque with a steel roof structure, a short-long arm double wishbone and multilink with outboard coilover spring suspension, Brembo piston with steel rotors and ABS braking, and a 6 speed sequential transmission makes the car worthy of an opponent for its hardened veteran adversaries.","wiki_title":"Acura NSX GT3 Evo 22","kg_per_hp":"2.54","released":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-arca-chevrolet-ss":{"hp":"700","kg":"1554","lbs":"3425","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"ARCA Ilmor 396 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2025","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The newest ARCA Chevrolet vehicle to hit the iRacing scene, the ARCA Chevrolet SS is definitely a high speed oval racer for many racing tracks from tight short ovals to the big superspeedways. The car features General racing tires, a Holley 4150HP Series carburetor, Five star composite laminate blend body, a steel tubeframe chassis, and the usual 4 speed manual transmission with no clutch needed to shift to the higher gears from 2 to 4. With a beefy 700 horsepower coming from its ARCA Ilmor 396 cubic inch V8 engine, the car is loud and proud to thrill ARCA fans alike for many racedays to come.","wiki_title":"ARCA Chevrolet SS","kg_per_hp":"2.22","released":"2025-03-10"},"asphalt-arca-ford-mustang":{"hp":"700","kg":"1554","lbs":"3425","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"ARCA Ilmor 396 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2025","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Featuring the same features as its Chevrolet and Toyota rivals, the ARCA Ford Mustang is a nice alternative to those that are neither Chevrolet or Toyota fans. Between the exterior look of the cars, there isn't a whole lot in terms of differences. With that the car features the same General racing tires, a Holley 4150HP Series carburetor, Five star composite laminate blend body, a steel tubeframe chassis, and the usual 4 speed manual transmission including the ARCA Ilmore 396 Cubic Inch V8 engine giving this pony express a lot of muscle needed to race against its most fiercest competitors.","wiki_title":"ARCA Ford Mustang","kg_per_hp":"2.22","released":"2025-03-10"},"asphalt-arca-menards-chevrolet-impala-legacy":{"hp":"650","kg":"1497","lbs":"3300","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Chevrolet Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2009","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"With speeds topping out at almost 205 mph and 650 horsepower under the hood, this Impala is ready for action out on the track. The older Gen 4 variant of this classic NASCAR design is still used today in the ARCA Meanrds Series. Its Chevy Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8 makes it one of the most powerful Oval Racecars to date. Though the weight is at around 3300 lbs and acceleration to 60 mph in just under 4 seconds, the drivers, fans, and sponsors can truly agree that this vehicle is one of the best oval racers in the world. Many people flock to the races that these cars visit to see what kind of action, fun, and entertainment has in store waiting for them.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) NASCAR ARCA Menards Chevrolet Impala","kg_per_hp":"2.30"},"asphalt-arca-toyota-camry":{"hp":"700","kg":"1554","lbs":"3425","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"ARCA Ilmor 396 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2025","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With different exterior looks compared to its Ford or Chevrolet ARCA car rivals, the ARCA Toyota Camry is still a fine choice for anyone picking an ARCA vehicle for raceday. Once again, the car has the same features as the other two options with the same General racing tires, a Holley 4150HP Series carburetor, Five star composite laminate blend body, a steel tubeframe chassis, and the usual 4 speed manual transmission including the ARCA Ilmore 396 Cubic Inch V8 engine makes the ARCA Toyota Camry one of the most modern oval racing vehicles in America today.","wiki_title":"ARCA Toyota Camry","kg_per_hp":"2.22","released":"2025-03-10"},"asphalt-aston-martin-dbr9-gt1":{"hp":"608","kg":"1170","lbs":"2579","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"V12 DOHC with 4 valves per cylinder","year":"2015","wiki_type":"GT1","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Speed and Power are matched in the form of the DBR9 GT1. The car is designed for Le Mans series racing and a tough breed to beat. The V12 DOHC engine produces over 600 horsepower giving the car weight under 3000 lbs and fast acceleration at the 3 second mark. The aluminium frame with carbon fibre panels lowers the cars weight while its double wishbone with adjustable Koni dampers give the car a more flexible feel. With Eibach springs for its suspension, it shows other racing cars in the GT1 category that this Brit Car is worth staying around.","wiki_title":"Aston Martin DBR9 GT1","kg_per_hp":"1.92"},"asphalt-aston-martin-valkyrie-amr-lmh":{"hp":"671","kg":"1016","lbs":"2240","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"6.5 Liter Naturally Aspirated V12","year":"2025","wiki_type":"LMDh","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The Aston Martin Valkyrie AMR-LMH is the 4th and newest Aston Martin car to join iRacing. The addition of this car also marks the 17th vehicle from the United Kingdom and now the nation has a high speed LMDh vehicle to call its own. The car is powered by a 6.5 Liter Naturally Aspirated V12 engine making 671 horsepower propelling it easily past 200 mph. The other features of the car include a Xtrac 7 speed transmission, a Multimatic Carbon Tub chassis, a double wishbone suspension, 6 pot Alcon caliper brakes, and Michelin tires giving the car a very modern and technologically advanced feel like no other.","wiki_title":"Aston Martin Valkyrie AMR-LMH","kg_per_hp":"1.51","released":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-aston-martin-vantage-evo-gt3":{"hp":"535","kg":"1330","lbs":"2932","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"4.0L DOHC V8 ICE Twin-Turbocharged","year":"2024","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"iRacing's newest Aston Martin on the service since the Vantage GT4, the Vantage GT3 EVO features the usual refinements that GT3 drivers have expected over the years. The car is powered by 4.0L DOHC V8 ICE Twin-Turbocharged engine delivering over 530 horsepower and a 6 speed sequential transmission. Other refinements of the car include a large 28 gallon or 106 liter fuel tank, an aluminum monocoque chassis with bonded and bolted steel safety cage, a short-long arm double wishbone with outboard coilover springs and dampers on the suspension, and Alcon brakes with 6-piston action on the front and 4-piston action in the rear with steel rotors and ABS making this Aston Martin one of the most advanced GT3 cars competing today.","wiki_title":"Aston Martin Vantage GT3 EVO","kg_per_hp":"2.49","released":"2025-09-08"},"asphalt-aston-martin-vantage-gt4":{"hp":"450","kg":"1465","lbs":"3230","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"4.7L V8","year":"2022","wiki_type":"GT4","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"More GT4 cars for the diehard GT4 fans, the Aston Martin Vantage does that and deliver. With a 450 hp 4.7L V8 engine under the hood the car packs the punch as it cruises effortlessly up to 170 mph. The car itself has a 27.8 gallon fuel tank for long range endurance racing and a 3200+ lb total weight for maximum punishment out on the racetrack. The gearbox is a 6-speed manual sequential with flappy paddles connected to a mechanical self-locking differential while also having front and rear indepenent coilover suspension and Ohlins own ILX 2-way adjustable dampers giving the car the agility and handling it needs. With over 425 ft lbs of torque, this car has the muscle to take it to Porsche, BMW, and Audi for any GT4 race.","wiki_title":"Aston Martin Vantage GT4","kg_per_hp":"3.26","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-audi-90-gto":{"hp":"710","kg":"1206","lbs":"2659","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Inline Five Cylinders, Indirect","year":"1989","wiki_type":"IMSA GT","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The Audi 90 GTO is one of the classic IMSA cars of its time that showcased power, speed, and handling to the track. It’s Inline Five Cylinder engine is no slouch and drivers know it. The Inline Five Cylinder Turbocharged engine is well known for being the Audi Quattro S1 Pikes Peak power of choice. Its 6 speed gearbox makes acceleration a breeze to go through. It's standard steel roof and tubular frame isn't very technologically advanced but for the late 1980's, its one hyper performance of a racing car that should never be overlooked.","wiki_title":"Audi 90 GTO","kg_per_hp":"1.70"},"asphalt-audi-r18":{"hp":"1246","kg":"875","lbs":"1929","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"4WD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Audi 4.0 Liter V6 turobdiesel and Electric motor-generator","year":"2018","wiki_type":"LMP1","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A LMP1 Rival to Porsche, this Audi R18 is throwing all its power onto the pavement to show who’s #1 at Le Mans. This car is truly a screamer. The car features a Double a-arm suspension at both ends and the front uses a pushrod-actuated heave element, anti-roll bar, and roll damper. The rear suspension uses a pullrod-actuated heave element, anti-roll bar, torsion bars, and roll damper. The six-speed paddle actuated, semi-automatic transmission allows no mis-shifts at all and allows upshifts and downshifts a breeze.The carbon discs with monobloc calipers and an electronic control for brake balance uses a re-generating hybrid system to keep the car balanced and smooth on the race track. With a powerful diesel engine for the rear wheels and an electric motor generator for the front wheels, this car and its 17.6 gallon fuel tank proves to be quite the brute force of a racecar Audi set out to create.","wiki_title":"Audi R18 e-Tron Quattro","kg_per_hp":"0.70","released":"2018-03-05"},"asphalt-audi-r8-lms-legacy":{"hp":"576","kg":"1270","lbs":"2799","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"90 degree V10, DOHC, 4 valves per cylinder","year":"2016","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"When power comes to shove, the Audi R8 LMS can get the job done for GT and Sports Cars alike. Its DOHC V10 engine gives it vast power while keeping the tires to the asphalt. The Electro hydraulically activated 3-plate race clutch and its double wishbone with coil springs and adjustable dampers give this car unmatched tech like no other. Based on the designs and looks of the first Audi R8 Le Mans Quattro of 2006 and later 2010, it has transferred to this magnificent car for racing enthusiasts to enjoy.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Audi R8 LMS GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.20"},"asphalt-audi-r8-lms-evo-ii-gt3":{"hp":"585","kg":"1235","lbs":"2723","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Naturally Aspirated 5.2L V10","year":"2022","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"One of Audi's newest GT3 racers comes to iRacing in the form of the R8 LMS EVO II. The car is a 585 horsepower fire-breathing dragon that gives its naturally aspirated 5.2L V10 engine the punch it deserves. The car also has over 550 nm of torque for bursting acceleration and even features a sequential, pneumatically six-speed performance transmission for optimal gear shifting. With a new aerodynamics package that generates more downforce on the rear wing, a new intake system, and four-way adjustable dampers in the suspension, the car itself has the performance and technology to deal even with the most fiercest GT3 competitors out on the track.","wiki_title":"Audi R8 LMS EVO II GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.11","released":"2023-12-05"},"asphalt-audi-rs-3-lms-gen2-tcr":{"hp":"340","kg":"1300","lbs":"2866","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"4 Cylinder 2.0 Liter Turbocharged","year":"2021","wiki_type":"Touring Car","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The new Audi RS3 LMS Gen2 TCR seems to be the TCR answer out on the circuit. The car may have 10 less horsepower compared to its previous generation but it still remains a fierce competitor on any track in any touring car series. A 6 speed sequential transmission combined with a Audi RS3 motorsports adapted body shell with a full carbon fiber bodywork for its chassis gives it great flexibility and acceleration for its 4 cylinder 2.0 liter turbocharged engine. Other features include a strut front multilink rear suspension, Alon 6 piston front caliper and 2 piston rear brakes and Michelin tires gives the car all the usual touring car refinements and technology that's expected but improved upon compared to its previous generation.","wiki_title":"Audi RS3 LMS Gen2 TCR","kg_per_hp":"3.82","released":"2019-09-04"},"asphalt-audi-rs3-lms-tcr-legacy":{"hp":"350","kg":"1215","lbs":"2673","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Turbocharged 4-Cylinder","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Touring Car","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"One of the newest brutes to iRacing, the Audi RS3 LMS TCR is ready to tear up the racetrack for spectacular fun. A very sturdy vehicle makes it a truly reliable spectacle for all race fans. The car features McPherson suspension for easy adjustability on the toe, camber, and even the height with multi-link accessibility. A VAQ electro-hydraulic and its 3 modes keep the differential nice and smooth through the cars weight distribution giving it an even keel. With 6-piston caliper brakes for maximum stopping power, this Audi RS3 LMS TCR is ready for any brutal TCR race come shine, night, cloudy, or even rainy weather.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Audi RS3 LMS TCR","kg_per_hp":"3.47"},"asphalt-bmw-m-hybrid-v8":{"hp":"640","kg":"1030","lbs":"2270","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"V-shaped P66/3 Otto four-stroke twin-turbocharged V8","year":"2023","wiki_type":"LMDh (racing in IMSA's GTP class)","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The first LMDh car to hit the iRacing racing scene, the BMW M Hybrid V8 EVO LMDh / GTP is truly a remarkable racecar in both performance, technology, and economy. Starting off, the car features a V-shaped P66/3 Otto four-stroke twin-turbocharged V8 with a Front-mounted separate motor generator single-speed reducer for a juicy 640 horses of power. The car has cast aluminum cylinder block and cylinder head construction for durability and strength to keep the car intact at all times. The car also has high-pressure direct injection at 350 bar for mean effective pressure and a dry sump oil system for superb lubrication and with a 7 speed transmission gives this car plenty of acceleration during any race event to leave its competition in the dust.","wiki_title":"BMW M Hybrid V8 EVO LMDh / GTP","kg_per_hp":"1.61","released":"2022-12-06","updated":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-bmw-m2-cs-racing-f87-2020":{"hp":"365","kg":"1544","lbs":"3405","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.0L Inline 6-Cylinder, 4 Valve","year":"2024","wiki_type":"CSR","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"Something a bit different, the BMW M2 CS Racing (F87) - 2020 is quite a different car altogether for the base content side of iRacing. Mainly being used as a gap between rookie content and the GT4 and TCR cars, the car features a 3.0 Liter Inline 6-Cylinder, 4 valve engine capable of making around 365 horsepower with a 7 Speed BMW DSG transmission. The car has a steel body with aluminum and carbon for its chassis, a strut and multilink system for its suspension, Alcon piston brakes, and Michelin Pilot Sport GT tires giving the car a balanced feel between its handling, braking, and the power that it delivers to the track. With the car being an entry-level racer, this vehicle is sure to be quite a fan favorite.","wiki_title":"BMW M2 CS Racing (F87) - 2020","kg_per_hp":"4.23"},"asphalt-bmw-m2-racing-g87":{"hp":"313","kg":"1575","lbs":"3472","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Turbocharged 2.0 Liter B48B220O1 Inline 4","year":"2026","wiki_type":"CSR","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The newest update from Bavaria, the BMW M2 CS Racing (G87) is a landmark upgrade from the previous F87 model. One of BMW's latest cars for road racing, the new G87 features racecar technology that makes it popular among many drivers and fans alike. Some new technological advancements include a 7 Speed ZF Automatic Gearbox, a Turbocharged 2.0 L B48B20O1 Inline 4 engine, a Steel unibody chassis, MacPherson strut front and multi-link rear suspension, BMW 6 piston front, 1 piston rear with iron rotor brakes, and Goodyear tires that gives the car the grip and handling that it desires making this new G87 model quite a technologically advanced car indeed.","wiki_title":"BMW M2 CS Racing (G87)","kg_per_hp":"5.03","released":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-bmw-m4-f82-gt4-2018":{"hp":"431","kg":"1430","lbs":"3153","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Twin-Turbo 3.0-Liter Inline-Six","year":"2018","wiki_type":"GT4","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The M4 F82 GT4 is BMW’s latest design in power and maximum aerodynamics in the GT4 field. With competing makers from Porsche, McLaren, Audi, and others, BMW has definitely got a car with a lot of punch. The car features a Twin-Turbo 3.0-Liter Inline-Six engine for max horsepower output of 431 horses. A 33.6 gallon fuel tank for maximum endurance, weight of over 3100 lbs to stick the car to the road, and also a 0-60 mph time of 3.7 seconds makes the BMW M4 GT4 quite a spectacle of a racecar,","wiki_title":"(Legacy) BMW M4 F82 GT4 - 2018","kg_per_hp":"3.32","released":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-bmw-m4-g82-gt4-evo":{"hp":"530","kg":"1532","lbs":"3377","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.0 Liter ICE Turbo Charged Inline 6 Cylinder","year":"2024","wiki_type":"GT4","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The newest GT4 on the block, the BMW M4 G82 GT4 Evo is ready to hit the racing scene taking on the Porsche, Aston Martin, McLaren, and Mercedes-Benz equivalents. Replacing the previous F82 model, this car comes packed with new racecar features and has over 500 hp thanks to its 3.0 Liter ICE Turbo Charged Inline 6 Cylinder engine. The car does weigh slightly heavier than its older F82 counterpart but no matter what, the acceleration has been slightly improved from a 3.7 second time to a new 3.3 second time. A slightly larger fuel tank to improve its range and a 7 speed semi-automatic transmission with stamped steel chassis and carbon fiber components and strut front multilink suspension AP Racing 6 piston caliper brakes makes this car a true technical GT4 car in a long line of innovation history.","wiki_title":"BMW M4 G82 GT4 Evo","kg_per_hp":"2.89","released":"2024-09-03"},"asphalt-bmw-m4-gt3-evo":{"hp":"503","kg":"1430","lbs":"2833","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Water-Cooled Turbocharged Inline 6","year":"2021","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"BMW's newest EVO GT3 racer, the M4 EVO GT3 combines modern technology with cutting edge power and speed. The vehicle itself is powered by a Water-Cooled Turbocharged Inline 6 that makes just over 500 horsepower. One of the many features on the car include the ever popular Brembo racing calipers for max stopping and braking power. Its suspension is double A-arms with coilovers on the front and rear with KW 4-way adjustable dampers and also blade-adjustable front and rear anti-roll bars for the best stability and handling on the circuit. The transmission is a 6-speed sequential transaxle gearbox with also a valvetrain that is a DOHC and a direct fuel injection fuel feed. With also dry sump lubrication and even a weight of just over 2800 lbs, this car is ready to go for any driver that knows how to get the most out of any GT3 machinery.","wiki_title":"BMW M4 EVO GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.84","updated":"2025-09-08"},"asphalt-bmw-m8-gte":{"hp":"560","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1197","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"2640","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"BMW P63/1 V8 Twin-Turbocharged","year":"2019","wiki_type":"GTE","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The new M8 GTE, is BMW’s answer to the GTE world. With over 500 horsepower at the disposal and top speeds over 180 mph, this new Beemer will take the fight to Ford, Porsche, Ferrari and more to secure dominance in an already crowded racing field. The car also features Brembo racing caliper brakes for maximum stopping during anytime a wreck occurs in front of it. The vehicle is also installed with Front and rear Double A-arms with coil over suspension with cartridge type dampers to ensure a safe ride over bumps on various racetracks. Michelin tires are supplied on the car to ensure maximum grip and traction whenever needed and finally, the 6-speed transaxle sequential gearbox ensures no misshifts are allowed whatsoever. This gives the car a more friendly appearance in both operation and usage out on the track.","wiki_title":"BMW M8 GTE","kg_per_hp":"2.14","released":"2019-03-04"},"asphalt-bmw-z4-gt3-legacy":{"hp":"515","kg":"1200","lbs":"2646","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"V8 with Aluminum Cylinder Block","year":"2014","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Pure German engineering is displayed in the form of the Z4 GT3. BMW’s V8 engine gives it over 500 hp with unmatched handling ability. The car is one of BMW’s pride in the racing world. Based on the roadgoing BMW Z4, this GT3 version has been upgraded to include more sophistaced aero, winglets, and front fenders to provide even more additional downforce. The MacPherson axle with pushrods and wishbone give the car a ride quality like no other, tailored for its own racing driver. The H&R Coil Springs help the suspension while its two proprietary lubricants keep the car running until the race is over.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) BMW Z4 GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.33"},"asphalt-cadillac-cts-v-racecar":{"hp":"460","kg":"1452","lbs":"3200","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"6.2L V8 with aluminum block and heads","year":"2012","wiki_type":"GT and Prototype","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A 6.2L V8 and over 450 horsepower make the CTS-V Racecar a true GT style racer. Its top speed of almost 190 mph makes it a true racer when always driving on road courses all across the entire world. With a rear wing to provide more downforce for the back end of the car, it still remains a powerful beast today. While the racing modifications have improved its worth to the track, this CTS-V Racecar today has been blown away by newer, more tech-savvy cars of the future for safer but still more dynamic racing.","wiki_title":"Cadillac CTS-V Racecar","kg_per_hp":"3.16"},"asphalt-cadillac-v-series-r-gtp":{"hp":"670","kg":"1030","lbs":"2271","drivetrain":"4WD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Cadillac LMC55R 5.5L V8 NA DOHC","year":"2023","wiki_type":"LMDh / GTP","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest LMDh/ GTP car to join the iRacing service, the new Cadillac V-Series.R is the main competitor to BMW's M Hybrid V8 LMDh/ GTP car making these 2 fierce beasts requiring new techniques and skills that are needed in order to tame them. The car comes with all the latest innovations and technology associated with LMDh / GTP cars and even some other features of its own. The car has a 7-Speed Sequential gearbox with a dry sump for its lubrication system and a Rear-mounted 50KW spec MGU for some extra boost for qualifying, overtake, build, no deploy, or attack modes, a feature also seen on a few other cars that are on the iRacing service. The Xtrac P1359 7-speed carbon-fibre plastics reinforced pneumatically actuated transmission makes the car a breeze to shift through the gears, both upshifting and downshifting, which gives the vehicle to struck a cord with even more iRacing service members.","wiki_title":"Cadillac V-Series.R LMDh / GTP","kg_per_hp":"1.54","released":"2023-06-05"},"asphalt-caterham-420r":{"hp":"195","kg":"635","lbs":"1400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"2.0 Litre Ford Duratec Naturally Aspirated Inline 4","year":"2026","wiki_type":"Caterham 420R","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The Caterham 420R is the other Caterham car that iRacing has brought to the service and boats 65 more horsepower compared to its less powerful Academy cousin with 195 hp compared to 130 hp. The car is powered by a 2.0 Litre Ford Duratec Naturally Aspirated Inline 4 engine and has a SADEV 6 speed sequential transmission. The car has similar features to its Academy alternate which includes a Tube frame with aluminum skin, a double wishbone and de-dion suspension, and 4 piston AP Racing calipers with iron discs. The car has Nova tires so the car is light and nimble on its wheels but still powerful enough to challenge a MX-5 and even a Formula Ford car for both speed and acceleration making it quite a formidable adversary as a racecar for climbing up the racing hierarchy.","wiki_title":"Caterham 420R","kg_per_hp":"3.26","released":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-caterham-academy":{"hp":"130","kg":"635","lbs":"1400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"1.3 Litre Horse HR13 Turbocharged Inline 4","year":"2026","wiki_type":"Caterham Academy","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The Caterham Academy car is iRacing's first entry for Caterham vehicles as the car comes in a double package with it and the 420R. The Academy car itself comes with its own set of features which includes a 6 Speed H-Pattern transmission, a Tube frame with aluminum skin Chassis, a Double wishbone front with de-dion rear axle suspension, Toyo Tires, and 2 piston AP racing sliding calipers on iron discs making this car a very modern Caterham vehicle for raceday, trackday, or even a simple day out on the road just to cruise about.","wiki_title":"Caterham Academy","kg_per_hp":"4.88","released":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-chevrolet-corvette-c6-r-gt1":{"hp":"590","kg":"1100","lbs":"2425","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"LSR7 6980cc V8 Naturally Aspirated","year":"2009","wiki_type":"GT1","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With a LSR7 6980cc V8 engine, the Corvette C6.R GT1 has a speed prepared for Le Mans style racing come rain, shine, or cloudy weather. Being based on its roadgoing counterpart, Pratt and Miller engineering designed and developed the car for high levels of intense racing around the globe. Featuring CNC Ported Cylinder heads, Titanium Valves with a Steel forged crankshaft, the car and its modifications gave the overall vehicle 6% less drag than the standard roadgoing vehicle.","wiki_title":"Chevrolet Corvette C6.R GT1","kg_per_hp":"1.86"},"asphalt-chevrolet-corvette-c7-daytona-prototype":{"hp":"788","kg":"1039","lbs":"2291","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"5.5 Liter, normally aspirated V8","year":"2015","wiki_type":"Prototype","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"A 5.5 Liter V8 gives the C7 Daytona Prototype the king of the Prototype racing out there. With its steel tube frame being made in consolidation with Dallara, the car and its double wishbone, push-rod actuated coil springs give it a smooth but firm ride around the race track. The sequential semi-automatic 6 speed transmission makes changing up and down gears a breeze to go through ensuring drivers to never allow a misshift or put in the wrong gear. Having 4 constructors championships and 3 drivers championships over its lifetime, its one of the most successful Daytona Prototype cars in the motorsport world of racing.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Chevrolet Corvette C7 Daytona Prototype","kg_per_hp":"1.32"},"asphalt-chevrolet-corvette-c8-r-gte":{"hp":"500","kg":"1240","lbs":"2733","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Naturally Aspirated 5.5 Liter V8","year":"2020","wiki_type":"GTE","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The latest Corvette GTE monster that has now been unveiled to the racing world, the Chevrolet Corvette C8.R GTE is the newest GTE competitor in the iRacing field. Now taking the fight to BMW, Porsche, Ferrari, and Ford this fire breathing American muscle car is ready to crush its competition. Using a naturally aspirated 5.5 liter V8 that produces 500 horsepower and revving up to 7200 rpm, the car also features a six speed sequential transmission to ensure the smoothest of any upshift or downshift. The car also has a very quick acceleration 0-60 mph (0-100 kmh) time of 3.2 seconds giving it a middle range between the Porsche's quick 2.9 seconds and BMW's semi-quick 3.5 seconds. With a weight of 2,733 pounds, the car is a true midweight and its competition surely knows it. Michelin tires give it the superb traction and grip it needs to blast through any corners which makes this car a worthy adversary.","wiki_title":"Chevrolet Corvette C8.R GTE","kg_per_hp":"2.48","released":"2020-09-08"},"asphalt-chevrolet-corvette-z06-gt3-r":{"hp":"600","kg":"1240","lbs":"2733","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"5.5 Liter Naturally Aspirated Flat-Plane Crankshaft DOHC V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With the 2023 season behind them, Chevrolet looked forwards to a new beginning for the 2024 season with the Corvette Z06 GT3.R for its competition racecar. This vehicle itself, still under the Corvette Racing program, still carries the Corvette Racing traits that has been in circulation for decades. With a 5.5 Liter Naturally Aspirated Flat-Plane Crankshaft DOHC V8 engine and a Xtrac 6 speed gearbox, the car has the ample power and torque needed to power its way through straights and out of the bends on any racetrack even though its a bit heavier than some of its older cousins. Double Wishbone suspension and a fully homologated FIA safety cage and crash safety systems makes it a technological right-up-to-date thoroughbred with the addition of even Quick-fill Fuel Fill and AP Racing Calipers and even optimized driveline systems makes this car a true marvel in its own right.","wiki_title":"Chevrolet Corvette Z06 GT3.R","kg_per_hp":"2.07","released":"2024-06-03"},"asphalt-dallara-f3":{"hp":"220","kg":"550","lbs":"1213","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Naturally","year":"2018","wiki_type":"Formula 3 Car","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With new technology, Dallara brings out their latest Formula racing monster, the F312 F3. This new car combines performance and economy to create a open wheeled racecar like no other. Being a beginner F1 car, it will be the envy of Renault’s Formula 3.5. The chassis is made from a carbon fiber monocoque giving strong rigidity and strengthness when taking in hits out on the track. It also features a Hewland 6-speed sequential transmission to minimize driver error when upshifting or downshifting. With a Naturally Aspirated Inline 4-Cylinder engine with 220 horsepower and weight of just over 1200 lbs, this car can really show some of the others what it can do.","wiki_title":"Dallara F312 F3","kg_per_hp":"2.50","released":"2018-12-03"},"asphalt-dallara-il-15":{"hp":"450","kg":"644","lbs":"1420","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"2.0L Inline-4 Cylinder Turbocharged","year":"2015","wiki_type":"Indy NXT","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A rocket car with acceleration and speed to boast, the IL-15 is a open wheel car that is sure to turn some heads from its 450 horsepower 2.0L Inline-4 Cylinder Turbocharged engine. The 6 speed sequential transmission coupled with a carbon fiber tub chassis thats also throughout its bodywork and both front and rear wings give it lightweight properties to give some cars a run for their money. Other features on this car include a double wishbone suspension on the front and rear with pushrods and a rocker activated inboard damper system with PFC style brakes with 6-piston action on the front and rear with iron rotors. With Firestone tires, this IL-15 can show what it can do not on just the straights but also in the turns too.","wiki_title":"Dallara IL-15","kg_per_hp":"1.43","released":"2025-09-08"},"asphalt-dallara-ir-01":{"hp":"900","kg":"832","lbs":"1834","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.0 Liter Naturally Aspirated V10","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Grand Prix","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A new high speed monster for the road racing aficionados, the Dallara IR-01 encapsulates power, speed, handling, and much more like no any open wheel racecar ever before. The power from its 3.0 liter naturally aspirated V10 makes this car squeal loud and proud to the tune of F1 cars of the mid 2000's. With a high speed of 245 mph (394 kmh) and an acceleration time that only rivals that of the Nissan GTP ZX-T, this car is truly a monster. Drivers that want to master this vehicle have a lot of work ahead of them but it will surely pay off in the end when their victories come to fruition. While the car itself can go much faster, its final drive ratio disbands it from going any faster, likely for a number of safety reasons.","wiki_title":"Dallara IR-01","kg_per_hp":"0.92","released":"2020-12-08"},"asphalt-dallara-ir18":{"hp":"700","kg":"735","lbs":"1590","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"2.2 Liter, 134.3 cu in V6, turbocharged","year":"2018","wiki_type":"Road and Oval IndyCar","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The newest Indycar entry offered, the Indycar IR18 is a vast improvement over its DW12 counterpart. With a slim design look and a smaller rear wing, this car was designed to cut through the air like a missile. This car is an untamed monster to any that drives it. The car features a Double A-arm, pushrod, with third spring and anti-roll bar on both the front and rear to create a perfect and balanced suspension. The sequential six speed, paddle actuated, semi-automatic transmission ensures that a misshift is impossible to perform no matter who is driving the car. With PFC carbon disc brakes with monobloc aluminum calipers, this car is ready to do many laps around the track without breaking a single sweat.","wiki_title":"Dallara IR18","kg_per_hp":"1.05","released":"2018-03-05","updated":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-dallara-p217":{"hp":"608","kg":"930","lbs":"2050","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Gibson GK-428 4.2 liter V8","year":"2020","wiki_type":"LMP2","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"A fast new Dallara for the road racing experience, the Dallara P217 LMP2 is a perfect blend of LMP1 acceleration with GTE dependability. While not having much more power than their slower GTE counterparts, the new Dallara P217 LMP2 makes up for that with less weight, better aerodynamics, better downforce, and less drag to give it the straight line acceleration it deserves. Featuring a Gibson GK-428 4.2 liter V8 engine producing 608 horsepower and an acceleration 0-60 mph (0-100 kmh) time of 3.1 seconds, this car and its Michelin tires and Brembo carbon disc brakes make this car reliable, sturdy, fast, and fun for any road racer. The car also features double wishbone independent pushrod on its suspension and a chassis made entirely out of carbon-fibre with a monocoque design with aluminium honeycomb and zylon side panels that makes this car a technological dream. Finally, its Xtrac P1159F 6 speed sequential semi-automatic paddle-shift transmission makes the shifting very smooth, precise, and very effecient. This Dallara can stir up any competition that comes its way.","wiki_title":"Dallara P217 LMP2","kg_per_hp":"1.53","released":"2020-09-08"},"dirt-dirt-legends-ford-34-coupe":{"hp":"122","kg":"500","lbs":"1100","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Yamaha 1250CC","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"A true beginners Dirt Introduction car, the Dirt Legends Ford ‘34 Coupe gives drivers what it feels like to drive on the loose stuff. Skill is the key to master this car. As the dirt version of its Legends Ford '34 Coupe counterpart, this vehicle is the perfect entry for Dirt Ovals and to learn the basics on dirt track racing. Being part of the 600 Racing family, this dirt version of the Legends Ford '34 Coupe, drivers will enjoy the fun and thrill of this classic vehicle.","wiki_title":"Dirt Legends Ford '34 Coupe","kg_per_hp":"4.10"},"dirt-dirt-street-stock":{"hp":"425","kg":"1395","lbs":"3075","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"350 Cubic Inch Chevrolet","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"With its 350 Cubic Inch, 425 hp Chevrolet, the Dirt Street Stock is one different machine. Because of its high weight, it requires braking into the turns but trying not to hit the wall or spinning out. Built by the JR Motorsports group who also put together the rookie Street Stock vehicle, the small wing but high dirt car speeds it attains still remains a challenge to dirt track drivers today.","wiki_title":"Dirt Street Stock","kg_per_hp":"3.28"},"asphalt-euro-nascar-v8gp":{"hp":"400","kg":"1330","lbs":"2932","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"5.7 Liter V8 Small Block","year":"2026","wiki_type":"EuroNASCAR","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The new Euro NASCAR V8GP is the first outside of America racing series that gets big focus in the world of simracing. While most NASCAR cars on iRacing are mainly focused on modifieds, trucks, O'Reilly, or Cup series that is mainly centered in North America. the Euro NASCAR V8GP takes its focus abroad over on the continent of Europe. The car features a 5.7 Liter V8 Small Block engine, a 5 speed sequential transmission, a tube frame chassis, a front independent with live rear axle suspension, and 4 pot caliber brakes gives this car a modern technological feel without making it too old school.","wiki_title":"Euro NASCAR V8GP","kg_per_hp":"3.33"},"asphalt-ferrari-296-challenge":{"hp":"700","kg":"1330","lbs":"2932","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"V6 120 degree turbo dry sump 2992 cc","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Challenge","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A new type of Ferrari racing, the 296 Challenge is definitely one of the most formidable road racing cars around the globe today. From the illustrious F355 Challenge to the impeccable F430 Challenge and more, the new 296 Challenge and the series it participates in today seems to be carrying that Ferrari Challenge torch bright. With that said, the new Ferrari 296 Challenge car features modern Ferrari refinements including a 7 speed F1 dual clutch transmission, Pirelli tires, front disc and rear disc brakes, and a V6 120 degree turbo dry sump 2992 cc engine making 700 horsepower gives this car quite the punch despite the car being in a D Class license series.","wiki_title":"Ferrari 296 Challenge","kg_per_hp":"1.90","released":"2025-06-10"},"asphalt-ferrari-296-gt3":{"hp":"600","kg":"1350","lbs":"2976","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Ferrari F163CE V6 GDI Turbo","year":"2023","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Newest GT3 racer to come to iRacing as of September 2023, the Ferrari 296 GT3 is the newest of Ferrari's GT3 racing machines ready to tear up the track on raceday. The car comes with many features, components and more, one of them being its engine, a Ferrari F163CE V6 GDI Turbo packing 600 horsepower. Other features include a Transversal sequential gearbox with an 6 speed e-clutch actuator transmission and a double wishbone, tubular steel suspension arm with aluminum uprights and even adjustable dampers. This gives the car ample suspension, durability, toughness, and a smooth transition for shifting through the gears. The last feature on this car to point out is that it also has brake calipers with the fronts having 6 pistons and the rear having 4 pistons helping the car to slow down or stop whenever its needed. No matter what though, this Ferrari 296 GT3 is ready to race.","wiki_title":"Ferrari 296 GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.25","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-ferrari-488-gt3-legacy":{"hp":"552","kg":"1270","lbs":"2804","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.9 liter Twin-Turbo V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"An improvement in GT3 racing, the Ferrari 488 is a racer that brings shame to others and glory for itself. Coming from Italy and with over 400 horsepower, this car drives like a dream. Based on the road going Ferrari 488 car, the GT3 version comes with a 6-speed dual clutch with carbon-ceramic brakes to increase stopping distances to a bare minimum. With disc sizes 9% smaller than the previous 458, this car stops quicker and brakes harder like no other. With under body vortex generators to reduce air pressure, this car is a true scientific achievement in the racing world.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Ferrari 488 GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.30"},"asphalt-ferrari-488-gt3-evo-2020":{"hp":"600","kg":"1260","lbs":"2778","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.9 liter Twin-Turbo V8 VVT","year":"2021","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Gleaming on to the track in fresh, bright Rosso Corsa paint, the new Ferrari 488 GT3 EVO is probably one of the most sophisticated and technologically advanced GT3 cars on the road racing circuit. The 600 horses that are delivered to this beast comes from a 3.9 liter twin-turbo V8 VVT powered engine that knows how to lay the power down with its mid-engine RWD layout for any balanced feel for any driver. A weight of 1260 kg keeps the car light enough to speed off the line but its not too heavy to bog it down. The grip from its Pirelli F-Zero racing tires makes it unparalleled among many other cars in its class and gives the car very good traction on any racetrack. The vehicle finally features a Fabricated steel-double wishbone with multi-links to give it added handling to an already powerful vehicle.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Ferrari 488 GT3 EVO","kg_per_hp":"2.10","released":"2021-09-07"},"asphalt-ferrari-488-gte":{"hp":"483","kg":"1260","lbs":"2778","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.9 liter Twin-Turbo V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"GTE","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A thoroughbred, the 488 GTE is Ferrari’s latest Sports Car and GT Car racer it has to offer. Its engine spitting over 450 hp brings drivers a whole new flavor to the road course racing world. A more tuned up version of its GT3 counterpart, the GTE version (GTLM for North America) brings in scalloped side air intakes and increased radiator cooling. The car itself has 50% more downforce than the 458 while reducing aerodynamic drag at the same time. With a new Aero Pillar that deflects air under the car's flat body makes this car one of the most advanced racecars in the world of motorsport.","wiki_title":"Ferrari 488 GTE","kg_per_hp":"2.61"},"asphalt-ferrari-499p":{"hp":"680","kg":"1120","lbs":"2469","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Ferrari F163 Twin-Turbo V6 Hybrid","year":"2024","wiki_type":"LMDh / GTP","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest LMDh / GTP to hit the iRacing scene of an ever-growing list of prototype race cars, Ferrari's 499P LMDh / GTP seems to be quite the answer in providing iRacers with a 5th option in the LMDh / GTP field competing alongside Acura, BMW, Cadillac, and Porsche. The car features a Ferrari F163 Twin-Turbo V6 Hybrid with a Front-Mounted 200KW spec MGU electric motor giving it the power it needs to power through corners and speed down straightaways. Other features of the car include a carbon composite monocoque chassis, a double wishbone with pushrod activation suspension, a 6 piston caliper carbon rotor braking system and with Michelin tires and a 7 speed sequential paddle shift transmission makes this Ferrari a very technologically advanced car.","wiki_title":"Ferrari 499P LMDh / GTP","kg_per_hp":"1.65","released":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-fia-f4":{"hp":"160","kg":"570","lbs":"1257","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"2.0L Inline-4 Cylinder","year":"2022","wiki_type":"F4","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"Tatuus' F4-T021 has entered the sim in the presence with help from iRacing.com Motorsport Simulations also known as the Formula iR-04. With a 2.0L inline-4 cylinder engine making 160 hp, the car may not be very powerful but with its weight of 1257 lbs, it can comfortably get up to 150 mph. Other features on the car include a dry sump lubrication, water and air cooler cooling system, 6 speed sequential paddle shift gearbox, front and rear double wishbone suspension, and 2 piston Brembo brake calipers. All of this technology and with adjustable front and rear wings, this car is definitely sure to be a fan favorite on iRacing.","wiki_title":"Tatuus F4-T021","kg_per_hp":"3.56"},"asphalt-ford-gt-gt2":{"hp":"500","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1237","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"2727","lbs_src":"sheet","kg_per_hp":"2.47"},"asphalt-ford-gt-gt3":{"hp":"558","kg":"1200","lbs":"2644","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"5 liter Ford DOHC, 32 Valve","year":"2011","wiki_type":"GT","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A new lead design for GT3 racing, the GT GT3 from Ford gives over 550 horsepower like no other. 30 gallons of fuel makes it a true racer in 24 hour racing. Basically a downgraded version from its Ford GT counterpart, it is still a fast GT3 car for asphalt road races alike. While still using the same 6 speed transmission as the Ford GT, the car remains a formidable racing car to many alike. Not as flashy and fancy as the new Ford GT GTE, no matter what though, this GT3 variant is still alive and kicking.","wiki_title":"Ford GT GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.15"},"asphalt-ford-gte":{"hp":"530","kg":"1245","lbs":"2745","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.5 Liter DOHC Ecoboost V6","year":"2017","wiki_type":"GTE","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Ready to take on the Ferrari 488 GTE and other GTE cars alike, the new Ford GT GTE remains a popular road course figure as it won the Le Mans LM GTE Pro Class in June of 2016. Its power and speed are no laughing matter when driving this eccentric racecar. With Ford announcing the new Ford GT GTE for the 2016 24 Hours of Le Mans, it was Ford Chip Ganassi Racing that campaigned in that years IMSA WeatherTech SportsCar Championship and also the FIA World Endurance Championship. When the 2017 24 Hours of Le Mans was over, the #67 car finished runner up at that year's 24 Hours of Le Mans in the GTE Pro Class while in the previous year it finished 7th and 9th. The car has been improved since then and is now ready for any 24 Hours of Le Mans race.","wiki_title":"Ford GT GTE","kg_per_hp":"2.35"},"asphalt-ford-mustang-fr500s":{"hp":"330","kg":"1633","lbs":"3600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Aluminum 4.6 Liter V8","year":"2010","wiki_type":"GT and Prototype","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"A 330 horsepower Mustang FR500S gives road racing a whole new meaning to Ford. Its top speed of 158 mph makes it easy to control. Based on the Mustang FR500 road going variant, the S model of the Mustang FR500 was designed by Ford Racing and Miller Motorsports for the Ford Racing Mustang Challenge series. It features aerodynamic parts like any other Mustang but with DOT approved racing BF Goodrich g-Force R1 tires for good grip, good handling, and improved stability. Now homologated for the SCCA World Challenge GTS Class, this car has been a great tool in the Ford Racing lineup where ever it goes to.","wiki_title":"Ford Mustang FR500S","kg_per_hp":"4.95","updated":"2022-12-06"},"asphalt-ford-mustang-gt3":{"hp":"558","kg":"1289","lbs":"2842","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Ford Coyote 5.4 Liter Naturally Aspirated V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The newest generation of Ford's road racing fleet, the Mustang GT3 powered by its Coyote 5.4 Liter Naturally Aspirated V8 built by Multimatic for IMSA and FIA racing alike, this car is ready for many seasons worth of competition at any road course. This vehicle itself marks the first time since 1997 that a Mustang will compete at the Circuit des 24 Heures du Mans, a 27 year gap. With past Le Mans drivers now a part of the Ford factory IMSA program, this car seems to be quite a winner indeed. The car features double wishbone with Multimatic DSSV dampers for its suspension, Alcon brakes, a carbon propshaft, a four plate Ap racing clutch, and a Xtrac Six Speed transaxle with ESA shift transmission giving this car a lot of technological innovation to show off to many racing fans around the globe to both the casual and the hardcore.","wiki_title":"Ford Mustang GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.31","released":"2024-06-03"},"asphalt-ford-mustang-gt4":{"hp":"500","kg":"1470","lbs":"3241","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"5.0L Coyote V8 Naturally Aspirated","year":"2023","wiki_type":"GT4","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The newest GT4 in iRacing and also the first American GT4 in the sim, the Ford Mustang GT4 is the 6th GT4 to come to iRacing and is definitely full of features. The engine is a 5.0L Coyote V8 Naturally Aspirated giving it a loud and proud 500 horsepower. The car also comes with a 6 speed sequential transmission and its chassis is a unibody with natural fiber composites. Other features of this car include a MacPherson strut front, multi-link rear suspension and Brembo brakes with 6-piston action on the front and 4-piston action on the rear with iron rotors and ABS giving it ample braking power and Michelin tires giving the car grip to plow through its competition on raceday.","wiki_title":"Ford Mustang GT4","kg_per_hp":"2.94","released":"2025-09-08"},"asphalt-formula-renault-2-0":{"hp":"213","kg":"506","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"1116","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"1998 cc, 4 cylinder, 16 valve,","year":"2016","wiki_type":"Open Wheel","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"To start off a young driver’s F1 career, the Formula Renault 2.0 is the way to go. It’s power, speed, and aerodynamics give the car grip like no other F1 starter car. With a torsion bar, push-rod, twin strut suspension, this car gets around the corners with plenty of ease and with very little difficulty. The tires themselves are both Michelin branded and are a good racing treat to use come rain or shine. With the wheels having a single piece magnesium, this car and its agility makes it one of the most prominent open wheeler cars that any asphalt road race driver can use. __NOEDITSECTION__","wiki_title":"Formula Renault 2.0","kg_per_hp":"2.38"},"asphalt-formula-vee-classic":{"hp":"85","kg":"374","lbs":"825","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Volkswagen Type 3 1200cc","year":"2021","wiki_type":"Formula Vee","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The new Formula Vee from Sheane's Formula Vee - Classic is definitely one of the most fun and interesting cars to drive. While it only has a piffling 85 horsepower, this car can still reach 100 mph. It has a Volkswagen type 3 1200cc engine with external oil coolers and oil filters for max cooling. The car also has a 4 speed h-shifter transmission with hydraulic linkage for its clutch. The brakes are also hydraulic with disc brakes in the front and drum brakes in the back. The steering is rack and pinion giving the car good handling on any short road course. This vehicle will definitely be one of the popular vehicles in iRacing as it is now the 2nd option for a rookie to begin their road racing career.","wiki_title":"Sheane Formula Vee - Classic","kg_per_hp":"4.40"},"asphalt-formula-vee-conqueror":{"hp":"85","kg":"374","lbs":"825","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Volkswagen Type 3 1200cc","year":"2026","wiki_type":"Formula Vee","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The new Formula Vee - Conqueror is one of two new Formula Vee cars to come to iRacing to complement the Sheane Formula Vee - Classic. The features between it and the others are pretty much identical except the body shape. Regardless, the car is powered by a Volkswagen Type 3 (1200 cc) engine that is air cooled with external oil coolers and oil filters, a stock Volkswagen transmission that is 4 speed, coil and distributor ignition, a stock Volkswagen with hydraulic linkage Clutch, hydraulic brakes with discs on the front and drums on the back, and the usual rack and pinion steering column giving this formula vee car a worthy competitor to the 2 other formula vee's come any raceday, rain or shine.","wiki_title":"AHS Motorsport Formula Vee - Conqueror","kg_per_hp":"4.40","released":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-formula-vee-cutlass":{"hp":"85","kg":"374","lbs":"825","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Volkswagen Type 3 1200cc","year":"2026","wiki_type":"Formula Vee","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The new Formula Vee - Cutlass from Sabre Racing Cars is one of two new Formula Vee additions to iRacing to complement the Sheane Formula Vee - Classic car. The engine is the same Volkswagen Type 3 (1200cc) air cooled engine but still features a coil and distributor ignition, a stock Volkswagen with hydraulic linkage clutch, hydraulic with disc front brakes and rear drum brakes, and a rack and pinion steering column making the cutlass model of the formula vee a well-improved model with some very nice refinements.","wiki_title":"Sabre Racing Cars Formula Vee - Cutlass","kg_per_hp":"4.40","released":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-gen-4-grand-national":{"hp":"650","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch (5.8 Litre) Pushrod V8","year":"2009","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The Gen 4 Grand National car borrows aspects of the Impala SS that NASCAR's Nationwide Series used in 2009 with it being reflected in iRacing as a whole. Besides that the car is powered by a 650 horsepower 358 Cubic Inch Pushrod V8 giving it the beefy power that it desires. Other features of the car include a steel tube frame, a 4 speed transmission, and A-arm front with truck arm rear suspension designed for use with coil-bind spring setups with sway bars and spring rates with adjustable ride heights and track bar heights giving the car any oval suspension flexibility for any raceday. The car's fuel tank in real life can be filled with unleaded or leaded gasoline (petrol), and has a 12:1 carburetor compression ratio with a naturally aspirated size of 390 cubic foot per minute. This makes this car a true beast on any oval racetrack.","wiki_title":"Gen 4 Grand National","kg_per_hp":"2.37","released":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-global-mazda-mx-5-cup":{"hp":"155","kg":"892","lbs":"1967","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"SKYACTIV-G 2.0L DOHC 16-valve","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Beginner GT and Beginner Prototype","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"A beginner’s road course car, the Global MX-5 Cup has a balanced feel and a great way to start a road course career in a sim or in the real world. With the car being based on its road going Mazda MX-5 counterpart, its one of the greatest rookie asphalt road racers of its current time. With its invitational series today having 19 drivers from 8 different countries, this Mazda is a global star in its own right. Having its own series sanctioned from SCCA Pro racing to INDYCAR, the promotions are now controlled by Andersen Promotions that controls and runs promotions and sanctioning of many series for all to enjoy.","wiki_title":"Global Mazda MX-5 Cup","kg_per_hp":"5.75"},"asphalt-honda-civic-type-r":{"hp":"345","kg":"1265","lbs":"2783","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Turbocharged 4-Cylinder Inline","year":"2021","wiki_type":"Touring Car","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A new addition to the TCR circuit, the Honda Civic Type R with its V-TEC power is definitely one of the newest innovations taking the series by storm. The car itself with a weight over 2700 lbs make it quite the heavy hitter out there to anyone that oppose it. Other features of the car include McPherson strut coil springs and gas-filled dampers for thefront suspension and a multi-link axle with coil springs for the rear suspension along with the gas-filled dampers. Both front and rear suspension include the standard anti-roll bar and all of this leads to a car with a good acceleration time and a marginally good top speed giving the car plenty of power and grip.","wiki_title":"Honda Civic Type R TCR","kg_per_hp":"3.67","released":"2021-12-06"},"asphalt-hpd-arx-01c":{"hp":"487","kg":"825","lbs":"1819","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"LM-V8, ACO IMSA LMP2Power: 486.66 hp (480 bhp) (357.94 kw)","year":"2011","wiki_type":"Le Mans LMP2","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With its LM-V8 engine, this LMP2 ARX-01c tames Le Mans like no other LMP2 car on the circuit even to this date. Honda is well known for F1 and Le Mans racing. Previously known as the Acura ARX-01c before its change to the Honda HPD ARX-01c, the car features a double wishbone, coil spring suspension with anti-roll bars and dampers to provide maximum racing comfort. Its carbon fibre and aluminum monocoque chassis keeps the cars' weight to an absolute minimum. Using Castrol EDGE as its lubricant and Michelin and Dunlop as its main tires, the ARX-01c car is a LMP2 car that has long gone by.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Honda HPD ARX-01c","kg_per_hp":"1.69"},"asphalt-hyundai-elantra-n-tc":{"hp":"355","kg":"1265","lbs":"2783","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Turbocharged 4-Cylinder Inline","year":"2021","wiki_type":"Touring Car","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Hyundai's newest racecar for the touring car circuit, the Elantra CN7, is ready for the track to go up against Honda's Civic Type R and Audi's RS3 LMS. The car itself is loaded with tons of innovations and technological enhancements over quite a varied amount of areas. The car's transmission and gearbox is a 6 speed sequential with paddle shift and acerametallic twin-disc clutch with a multi-plate limited slip differential for ease of gear shifting. Other features include a McPherson strut with coil springs and gas-filled dampers with anti-roll bars on the front suspension with the 4-arm multi-link axle on the rear suspension. Other areas include electric powered steering and dual circuit hydraulic brakes for max handling and braking power. While the front brakes are six-piston calipers at 380mm, the rear brakes are two-piston calipers at 278mm. The fuel system is a 100 liter (26.42 gallon) fuel tank for long endurance racing and lastly with a OMP race seat with 6 point HANS compatiable harness with info pages for its interior. The car itself is ready to race for anyone that drives it.","wiki_title":"Hyundai Elantra CN7 TCR","kg_per_hp":"3.56","released":"2021-12-06"},"asphalt-hyundai-veloster-n-tc":{"hp":"350","kg":"1265","lbs":"2789","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Turbocharged 4-Cylinder Inline","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Touring Car","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Hyundai's 2nd vehicle in iRacing, the Veloster N TCR is definitely quite the beast. Also being the fastest TCR car to date, this car does boast the similar power, weight, engine, and same drive configuration as the other TCR cars but has its own party treats. The car itself has a 6 speed sequential paddle shift with cerametallic twin-disc clutch and a multi-plate limited slip differential with strut coil springs and gas filled chambers for delivering power and giving it good handling. It also has electrical power assisted rack and pinion steering for precision movement and modern brakes, brake calipers, fuel system, standard racing interior, and others. This car itself is ready to race.","wiki_title":"Hyundai Veloster N TCR","kg_per_hp":"3.61","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-indy-pro-2000-pm-18":{"hp":"275","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"500","lbs":"1102","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Mazda 2 Liter MZR-PM18A","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Indy Lights","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"Italian power in this small but nimble USF Pro 2000 PM18 for the Indy Lights series makes this car fun but also competitive. Using the Mazda 2.0 Liter for power, this car is ready for racing. The car features a Mazda 2 Liter MZR-PM18A engine which gives it 275 horsepower, this car and its 10.6 gallon fuel tank and 1102 lbs of weight is a true lightweight car that's definitely got a kick to its acceleration. Being only a little faster than the old Pro Mazda, this car also features more technological features that the older car didn't have.","wiki_title":"Tatuus USF Pro 2000 PM18","kg_per_hp":"1.82","released":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-kia-optima":{"hp":"380","kg":"1361","lbs":"3000","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"2.0 liter, four cylinder Turbo","year":"2013","wiki_type":"GT and Prototype","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"A Korean feat of engineering, the Optima GX deploys over 350 horsepower to the road like no other. Its speed of over 170 mph is in a class of its own in a racing world that races over 200 mph today. Based upon its road going Kia Optima counterpart, this very same vehicle is part of the 4th Generation of the Kia Optima known as the Kia Optima JF and related to the Hyundai Sonata LF model. Being the front wheel drive powered car in the iRacing field, this vehicle is surely in a class of its own.","wiki_title":"Kia Optima GX","kg_per_hp":"3.58"},"asphalt-lamborghini-huracan-gt3-evo":{"hp":"500","kg":"1285","lbs":"2833","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"5.2 Liter Naturally Aspirated V10","year":"2020","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The Lamborghini Huracán GT3 EVO is the newest GT3 car to hit the iRacing scene and has definitely a lot of potential to be a great car for the road racing GT3 community. With 500 horsepower coming from its 5.2 liter naturally aspirated V10 engine, this car is no slouch in delivering its power to the road and it has a really good acceleration time too. With a midweight of just under 3000 lbs and a fuel capacity of exactly 120 liters, this car can go long distances before needing another top-up of fuel. With a name and car like Lamborghini, its definitely gonna square off against the Ferrari 488 GT3 for dominance between the two well-known Italian car makes. While one of these cars will win the battle, it all comes down to which car will win the war.","wiki_title":"Lamborghini Huracán GT3 EVO","kg_per_hp":"2.57","released":"2020-12-08"},"asphalt-late-model-stock":{"hp":"500","kg":"1406","lbs":"3100","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"GM604 350 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2023","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Newest late model stock vehicle that has replaced the old Chevy Monte Carlo SS, the CARS Late Model Stock is a 500 hp V8 roaring beast for many short tracks and mile oval tracks throughout the southeast. The car has double arm suspension with coil over shocks and springs combined with a truck arm and track bar giving it the stability, agility, and proper turn-in needed to get around the tight short tracks and wider mile oval tracks with relative ease. The car also features a 4 speed manual transmission with 475 foot pounds of torque giving it some serious muscle out on the track.","wiki_title":"CARS Late Model Stock","kg_per_hp":"2.81","released":"2023-03-07"},"asphalt-legends-ford-34-coupe":{"hp":"122","kg":"500","lbs":"1100","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Yamaha 1250CC","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"One of iRacing’s oldest cars, the Ford ‘34 Coupe can deliver fun and excitement to Rookies and Pros alike. Its Yamaha engine powers the car quickly to compensate for its 1100 lb. weight. The car is based on '34 models of its heyday and it uses 595 Federal Tires for racedays on its schedule. With the weight being under 1 US Ton (2000 lbs, 907 kg), this tiny car remains a popular short-track racing vehicle to many people that go to those tracks. Not a very fast racecar but to the fans, action and good fun matters the most.","wiki_title":"Legends Ford '34 Coupe","kg_per_hp":"4.10"},"asphalt-ligier-js-p320":{"hp":"460","kg":"950","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"2094","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Nissan VK56 5.6 Liter V8","year":"2023","wiki_type":"LMP3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The 4th french car to the service and the 2nd french manufacturer to appear in iRacing, the Ligier JS P320 LMP3 is iRacing's first LMP3 racer. As any other racecar, this new LMP3 features many modern features that are standard and equipped on today's racecars. Besides its 450+ horsepower Nissan VK56 5.6 Liter V8 engine, the car is equipped with a variety of technologically advanced base features. Such features like Monocoque carbon chassis for lightweightness and durability, Double wishbone and Pushrod and spring-damper combination, Adjustable anti-roll bar system, 6-speed sequential gearbox Xtrac 1152 with aluminium casing, and even Hydraulic power-assisted steering cooled by the cars oil radiator makes this vehicle a very well-made product for a wide variety of road racing circuits that await for its visit.","wiki_title":"Ligier JS P320 LMP3","kg_per_hp":"2.07","released":"2023-06-05"},"asphalt-lotus-49":{"hp":"406","kg":"530","lbs":"1168","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"V8, 90 degree; four valves/cylinder; DOHC","year":"1967","wiki_type":"Classic Open Wheel","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With its DOHC V8 405 hp engine, the Lotus 49 represents a true icon of classic Formula One racing. Classic drivers like Jim Clark and Graham Hill graced the car with pristine glory and pride forever. The car features an aluminum monocoque chassis while using Firestone or Dunlop tires to keep this cars' weight down and to provide a smoother ride. Being most famously shown in its Gold and British Racing Green colors, the Lotus 49 started off as a troubled car for a few years but became one of the most fantastic Formula 1 cars of its time. With top speeds over 200 mph, drivers fought this car to stay alive.","wiki_title":"Lotus 49","kg_per_hp":"1.31"},"asphalt-lotus-79":{"hp":"475","kg":"575","lbs":"1268","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"32 valve DOHC Cosworth DFV V8","year":"1978","wiki_type":"Classic Open Wheel","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The Famous Lotus 79 constructed for the 1978 Formula One season is still titled as one of Formula One’s greatest cars. With it’s 32 valve DOHC Cosworth DFV V8 engine, its one heck of a beast. Being the first Formula 1 car to take maximum advantage of aerodynamics and startling ground effects, this car uses the same Aluminum Monocoque chassis as its previous Lotus 49 from the 60's. The car also uses a double wishbone suspension with inboard springs and dampers for the front and parallel top links, lower wishbone, twin radius arms for its rear suspension. Goodyear tires keep the cars' grip to a max sticking to the track come rain or shine. With famous drivers like Mario Andretti winning the 1978 Drivers Championship and Constructors Championship, this impressive car shows others what they were missing out on ever since debuting in its first race at the 1978 Belgian Grand Prix at Circuit Zolder.","wiki_title":"Lotus 79","kg_per_hp":"1.21"},"asphalt-mclaren-570s-gt4":{"hp":"462","kg":"1560","lbs":"3439","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.8 Liter Twin Turbo V8 M838TE","year":"2021","wiki_type":"GT4","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The newest GT4 car to hit the iRacing scene and a long awaited arrival, the Mclaren 570S GT4 has many things for it. The car is powered by a 3.8 Liter twin Turbo V8 M838TE engine that makes over 450 horsepower giving this car the acceleration and speed that it desires. The vehicle has a 7 speed SSG transmission for easy shifting through the gears and rides on a McLaren carbon fibre MonoCell II chassis with aluminium front and rear frames and crash structures for outstanding durability. Also the car has a body of aluminium and carbon panels to keep it lightweight and aerodynamics of both front splitter and rear spoiler for racecar handling on any road course. The car uses Pirelli racing 265/645 and 305/680 tires and a 110 liter fuel cell for endurance and long racing stints. For a car that seems to do plenty, this vehicle is definitely gonna be a favorite and will lead to many battles between the BMW and Porsche rivals.","wiki_title":"McLaren 570S GT4","kg_per_hp":"3.38"},"asphalt-mclaren-720s-gt3-evo":{"hp":"710","kg":"1283","lbs":"2829","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","gears":"6","gears_src":"sheet","engine":"Motorsport-prepared M840T 4.0 liter Twin-Turbocharged V8","year":"2023","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"New and innovative, the McLaren 720S GT3 Evo is ready to hit the road racing scene all across the world. With over 700 horsepower coming from its M840T 4.0 liter Twin-Turbocharged V8 engine, this gives the car an insane 0-60 time of just 2.8 seconds, faster than any other GT3 car out on the circuit today. With a mid-engine RWD layout, drivers will have to keep the car balanced as much as possible or risk spinning out. This machine also features a six-speed sequential transmission, adjustable dampers with coil-over springs, a carbon fiber MonoCage II chassis, FIA safety with rollcages, side-impact, foam, and a roof hatch extraction system giving the car the technology it demands. Other features of the car also include a lightweight carbon fiber composite body with a front splitter and floor assembly, dive planes, motorsport axles with single wheel retaining nuts, and the standard winged-headrest seat with six-point harness making the car a true technological masterpiece.","wiki_title":"McLaren 720S GT3 Evo","kg_per_hp":"1.81","released":"2024-09-03"},"asphalt-mclaren-mp4-12c-gt3-legacy":{"hp":"493","kg":"1434","lbs":"3161","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"V8 DOHC, spark-ignition 4-stroke","year":"2013","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With its V8 engine, the MP4-12C GT3 is a monster in GT racing. With a top speed of over 170 mph, it’s a powerful brute on the circuit. Based on the road going McLaren MP4-12C (later became the McLaren 12C respectively), this car is also related to the McLaren P1 and the McLaren 650S models as well. The body of the car uses carbon fibre to bring weight down to an absolute minimum and to provide better acceleration. The chassis known as the Carbon MonoCell is a very light weight system that makes the car very nimble on both straightaways and the turns. Having top speeds very close to the Porsche 911 GT3 Cup (991) and the Mercedes AMG GT3 vehicles, this car brings out the best in racers and simracers that drive this highly strung vehicle.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) McLaren MP4-12C GT3","kg_per_hp":"2.91"},"asphalt-mercedes-amg-gt3-legacy":{"hp":"500","kg":"1330","lbs":"2932","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"V8 Front Mid-Engine; DOHC 4 valves per cylinder","year":"2016","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Sinister but yet tame, the Mercedes-Benz AMG GT3 is the collaboration of Mercedes-Benz and AMG to make the road-going SLS a car to keep tabs on during race day. The characteristics of the car features lightweight body and chassis to keep weight down and acceleration up. Being a predecessor to the Mercedes-Benz 300SL and the Mercedes-Benz SLR McLaren, it is truly a monster on the track. Despite the Mercedes-Benz AMG GT being its successor, this car makes other race car drivers envy of the way it performs, drives, and how it handles.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Mercedes-Benz AMG GT3 - 2016","kg_per_hp":"2.66"},"asphalt-mercedes-amg-gt3-2020":{"hp":"550","kg":"1285","lbs":"2833","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"AMG 6.3 Liter V8 Naturally Aspirated","year":"2020","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Featuring new technology and a new mightier engine, the 2020 version of Merc's AMG GT3 has come to iRacing finally at last. With 550 horsepower from its AMG 6.3 Liter V8 Naturally Aspirated engine, the car has enough power for any GT3 driver. The vehicle has many other features as well including a Sequential AMG 6-gear racing transmission, motorsports electronics, multiple-adjustable ABS, AMG Traction Control, and many others. The wheels are AMG Alloys and the chassis is a double wishbone with configurable rebound and pressure dampers with configurable stabilizers. With a 28 gallon fuel endurance length tank, the car and its weight of just under 3000 lbs make the car quite the beast out on the track.","wiki_title":"Mercedes-Benz AMG GT3 - 2020","kg_per_hp":"2.34"},"asphalt-mercedes-amg-gt4":{"hp":"544","kg":"1390","lbs":"3064","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"AMG 4.0 Liter V8 BiturboPower: 544 hp (536.56 bhp) (400.111 kw)","year":"2020","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A newest GT4 to hit the iRacing GT4 scene, the Mercedes-Benz AMG GT4 is the newest entry for GT4 cars in iRacing. With a AMG 4.0 liter V8 biturbo engine, this makes the car output quite a whopping 544 horsepower. The vehicle is also equipped with a sequential AMG 6-gear racing transmission with motorsports electronics, multiple-adjustable ABS, and even AMG traction control making this car advanced in its technology. Other features of the car include a double wishbone chassis with configurable rebound and pressure dampers that feature configurable stabilizers. With a weight of just over 3000 pounds, the car can throw its weight around and survive making this vehicle quite a tank in its own right.","wiki_title":"Mercedes-Benz AMG GT4","kg_per_hp":"2.56","released":"2022-06-06"},"asphalt-mercedes-amg-w12-e-performance":{"hp":"1050","kg":"752","lbs":"1658","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Mercedes-Benz AMG F1 M12 E Performance 1.6 Liter V6","year":"2021","wiki_type":"Formula One","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest F1 car to come to iRacing after a long 6 years has finally arrived with the Mercedes-Benz AMG F1 W12 E Performance. This car itself having over 1,000 horsepower from its V6 engine delivers the power fast and hard to ensure its dominant place in the field. The car itself is chocked full of innovations, technology, and other cool tricks to make it stand out from other F1 cars. The moulded carbon fibre and honeycomb composite structure monocoque design ensure complete safety of the driver in the event of a crash. The bodywork is also carbon fibre composite and the cockpit features a removable drivers seat made of anatomically formed carbon composite with the OMP six-point driver safety harness and HANS system. Other safety structures include a cockpit survival cell incorporating impact-resistant construction and penetration panels with front impact structure, prescribed side impact structures, integrated rear impact structure, front and rear roll structures, and titanium driver protection structure to meet its highly safety standard requirements. The suspension on the car is carbon fibre wishbone and pushrod-activated for smooth rides over bumpy surfaces on any F1 track it goes to. The Carbone Industries carbon discs with Brembo brake calipers are the brakes that slow or stop this powerful beast of a car. FIA standard ECU and FIA homologated electronic and electrical system rely all the information to the driver that it can possibly deliver along with its McLaren Electronic System. The ATL Kevlar-reinforced rubber bladder fuel system makes its fuel tank safe in any serious crash. Finally the carbon plate clutch with the sequential semi auto-matic eight speed gearbox give the car both the acceleration and top speed it deserves. This makes this car a true beast out on the track.","wiki_title":"Mercedes-Benz AMG F1 W12 E Performance","kg_per_hp":"0.72","released":"2021-12-06"},"asphalt-mercedes-amg-w13-e-performance":{"hp":"1070","kg":"795","lbs":"1753","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Mercedes-AMG F1 M13 E Performance 1.6 liter direct injection turbocharged V6","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Formula One","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"Mercedes-Benz' newest F1 car for iRacing the AMG F1 W13 E Performance is loaded with technology and performance for 2022. The car features a Mercedes-AMG F1 M13 E Performance 1.6 liter direct injection turbocharged V6engine with a Motor Generator Unit Kinetic electric motor for over 1,000 horsepower. The car itself is a molded carbon fibre monocoque shell for light weight and strong durability with a carbon fibre bodywork for extra strength. The suspension are carbon fibre wishbone and pushroad-activated torsion springs for strong relative motion and even carbone industries carbon discs for its brakes gives the car ample braking power. With power-assissted steering, ECU electronics, MES instrumentation, ATL Kevlar-reinforced fuel system and a 8 speed sequential semi automatic hydraulic activated gearbox, this car is ready for raceday.","wiki_title":"Mercedes-Benz AMG F1 W13 E Performance","kg_per_hp":"0.74","released":"2022-12-06"},"asphalt-mini-stock":{"hp":"200","kg":"1066","lbs":"2350","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"2.3 Liter Inline 4 Cylinder 2V OHC","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Mini Stock","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Featuring the same technical specifications as its dirt oval counterpart, the mini stock is a fine small asphalt oval racecar for short oval and mile oval use and does it really well in local races across the country. With a 2.3 Liter Inline 4 Cylinder 2V OHC engine making 200 horsepower, OEM strut 4-link coil springs for its suspension, OEM disk and drum brakes, along with Hoosier racing tires and a Modified OEM frame with reinforced roll cage, the car is a near 1-to-1 exact of its dirt counterpart with the main difference is its main use for asphalt short track and mile oval racing. Nevertheless the similarities, the mini stock and its dirt counterpart are bound to be fan favorites. One thing to note is that the dirt mini stock counterpart revs up to 8,500 rpm's while the regular asphalt mini stock only revs up to 7,500 rpm's.","wiki_title":"Mini Stock","kg_per_hp":"5.33","released":"2024-09-03"},"asphalt-modified-sk":{"hp":"370","kg":"1179","lbs":"2600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 Degree V8","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"370 horsepower and open wheel racing, the SK Modified is one fast gerbil of a car. A top speed of over 140 mph makes it a quick bullet out on the racing circuit. Being a less powerful version of its Whelen Modified Tour counterpart, the SK Modified remains a quick and fast car. Even though it has 250 less hp and 15 less mph top speed than the Whelen Modified Tour counterpart, the car is still worth its weight and might around the track. Drivers are often started in the SK Modified before moving up to the Whelen Modified Tour car due to the fact that the Whelen Modified Tour car boasts over 600 horsepower and top speeds almost nearing 160 mph.","wiki_title":"Modified - SK","kg_per_hp":"3.19"},"asphalt-nascar-cup-series-chevrolet-camaro-zl1":{"hp":"750","kg":"0","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"0","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter EFI V8","year":"2018","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A new Gen 6 monster to devour the competition, Chevrolet brings out all the stops with their new Camaro ZL1 to take the fight to Ford and Toyota. With the car weighing 100 lbs less than its Chevy SS predecessor, this gives the car a 0-60 mph (0-100 kmh) acceleration improvement of 0.2 seconds from 2.9 to 2.7 seconds. The vehicle's chassis is the Mild-Steel with Full Rollcage for maximum car and driver protection. With 750 horsepower compared to its Chevy SS predecessor of over 850 hp, this means the car itself is a bit nerfed when it comes to power, acceleration and speed at the Superspeedways. With a 4 speed manual transmission for optimal gear selection and efficiency, a steel and carbon bodywork for maximum durability, and a SLA Front, truck arm rear suspension, this new thoroughbred is ready for any competition it meets out on the track.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Cup Series Chevrolet Camaro ZL1"},"asphalt-nascar-cup-series-ford-mustang":{"hp":"750","kg":"1497","lbs":"3300","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter EFI V8","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The new Monster Energy Ford car to take to the NASCAR circuit, this Mustang is ready to take on any car that comes its way. The past Fusion has been replaced by this new thoroughbred of a racecar that lays power down like no other NASCAR cup series racing machine. Featuring new aerodynamic and downforce technology the new Monster Energy Cup Ford Mustang remains one of the more exquisite NASCAR vehicles on the circuit today. Not all the much different from its previous Ford Fusion model, this one should feel quite similar to drive.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Cup Series Ford Mustang","kg_per_hp":"2.00","released":"2019-06-03"},"asphalt-nascar-cup-series-next-gen-chevrolet-camaro-zl1":{"hp":"670","kg":"1588","lbs":"3500","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter EFI V8","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest NASCAR next gen (or gen 7) cup cars have finally been launched to iRacing and they are definitely quite a different breed compared to the previous gen 6. One of the biggest changes is from the h-shifter 4 gear pattern to the sequential 5 gear pattern to make shifting up and down through the gears easier for the driver. The car features newly designed aero and downforce package and a redesigned side skirt which reduce the side force in the vehicle. Also included is a rear diffuser for the first time in a NASCAR cup series car. Some of the newest technological improvements on the car include a spec chassis, independent rear suspension, new wheel design, and a new refueling system similar to those used in the IMSA Series. The weight of the car is a bit heavier than its gen 6 predecessors but these cars are ready for the cup tracks of today and also yesteryear too.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Cup Series Next Gen Chevrolet Camaro ZL1","kg_per_hp":"2.37"},"asphalt-nascar-cup-series-next-gen-ford-mustang":{"hp":"670","kg":"1588","lbs":"3500","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter EFI V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest NASCAR next gen (or gen 7) cup cars have finally been launched to iRacing and they are definitely quite a different breed compared to the previous gen 6. One of the biggest changes is from the h-shifter 4 gear pattern to the sequential 5 gear pattern to make shifting up and down through the gears easier for the driver. The car features newly designed aero and downforce package and a redesigned side skirt which reduce the side force in the vehicle. Also included is a rear diffuser for the first time in a NASCAR cup series car. Some of the newest technological improvements on the car include a spec chassis, independent rear suspension, new wheel design, and a new refueling system similar to those used in the IMSA Series. The weight of the car is a bit heavier than its gen 6 predecessors but these cars are ready for the cup tracks of today and also yesteryear too.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Cup Series Next Gen Ford Mustang","kg_per_hp":"2.37"},"asphalt-nascar-cup-series-next-gen-toyota-camry":{"hp":"670","kg":"1588","lbs":"3500","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter EFI V8Power: 670 hp (660.8 bhp) (492.8 kw)","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest NASCAR next gen (or gen 7) cup cars have finally been launched to iRacing and they are definitely quite a different breed compared to the previous gen 6. One of the biggest changes is from the h-shifter 4 gear pattern to the sequential 5 gear pattern to make shifting up and down through the gears easier for the driver. The car features newly designed aero and downforce package and a redesigned side skirt which reduce the side force in the vehicle. Also included is a rear diffuser for the first time in a NASCAR cup series car. Some of the newest technological improvements on the car include a spec chassis, independent rear suspension, new wheel design, and a new refueling system similar to those used in the IMSA Series. The weight of the car is a bit heavier than its gen 6 predecessors but these cars are ready for the cup tracks of today and also yesteryear too.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Cup Series Next Gen Toyota Camry","kg_per_hp":"2.37"},"asphalt-nascar-cup-series-toyota-camry":{"hp":"875","kg":"1497","lbs":"3300","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter EFI V8","year":"2014","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"Power and grip for NASCAR vehicles are presented in the latest rendition of NASCAR’s Toyota Camry. Over 800 horsepower and speeds in excess of 190 mph gives this NASCAR speed a new nickname in the sport. Toyota has been with NASCAR ever since debuting in 2004 for the Camping World Series and 2007 for the Xfinity and Monster Energy series. Still using the same 5.9 liter pushrod V8 as the other NASCAR vehicles, the weight of 3300 lbs and the 2.9 0-60 mph acceleration time make it a fan favorite and a driver favorite for all to enjoy come qualifying, practice, and also racedays. When the might of this car comes around the track though, drivers still feel its presence and are aware of what they see in front or what they feel is coming behind them.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Cup Series Toyota Camry","kg_per_hp":"1.71"},"asphalt-nascar-gen-4-chevrolet-monte-carlo-2003":{"hp":"900","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"90 Degree Pushrod V8 358 Cubic Inch","year":"2003","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A classic NASCAR cup racer that brings a lot of nostalgia with it, the NASCAR Chevrolet Monte Carlo Gen 4 Cup car is definitely a vehicle that harkens back to NASCAR's golden era. The Gen 4 cars themselves lasting from 1992 to 2006 still have an everlasting impact on many racing fans young and old. The car has all of the NASCAR typical features like the classic 4 speed manual transmission, a 22 gallon fuel tank, standard NASCAR weight of 3400 lbs, a steel tube frame chassis and roll cage, and a double A-arm front and truck arm with panhard bar rear for its suspension gives the car that nostalgic 2003 feel.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Chevrolet Monte Carlo Gen 4 - 2003","kg_per_hp":"1.71","released":"2025-06-10"},"asphalt-nascar-gen-4-cup-legacy":{"kg":"0","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"0","lbs_src":"sheet"},"asphalt-nascar-gen-4-ford-taurus-2003":{"hp":"900","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"90 Degree Pushrod V8 358 Cubic Inch","year":"2003","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The main rival to the NASCAR Chevrolet Monte Carlo Gen 4, the NASCAR Ford Taurus Gen 4 is a worthy opponent as the two makes have battled each other through thick and thin ever since the beginning of NASCAR's days in 1949. With an intense rivalry lasting well over half a century by 2003 and three-quarters of a century by 2024, these two titans are still serious fighters today. Like the NASCAR Chevrolet Monte Carlo Gen 4, the features of this car are very similar featuring the same 900 horsepower with its 90 degree pushrod V8 358 Cubic Inch engine, 4 speed manual transmission, a 22 gallon fuel tank, the standard NASCAR Cup 3400 lbs weight, a steel tube frame chassis, and a double A-arm front and truck arm with panhard bar rear suspension although besides the many similarities, the Ford Taurus itself is a beast in its own right.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Ford Taurus Gen 4 - 2003","kg_per_hp":"1.71","released":"2025-06-10"},"asphalt-nascar-legends-buick-lesabre-1987":{"hp":"650","kg":"1678","lbs":"3700","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"1987","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The speediness of the Buick LeSabre has finally come to iRacing and it shows. With a car that shares many of the same characteristics as the other Gen 3 1987 vehicles in the sim, the car features a Borg Warner Super T-10 4 speed manual and independent front suspension with coil springs and anti-rollbar giving the car acceleration and handling. With a live axle truck arm and with power coming from its 358 cubic inch V8 engine, the car is ready to battle it out on the track once more against Chevrolet and Ford. Just remember that like the Chevrolet Monte Carlo and Ford Thunderbird, this car comes with no power steering.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Buick LeSabre Gen 3 - 1987","kg_per_hp":"2.58","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-nascar-legends-chevrolet-monte-carlo-1987":{"kg":"1678","lbs":"3700","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch Chevrolet V8","year":"1987","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A blast from the NASCAR racing past, this Gen 3 Monte Carlo from the 1987 season makes its entry into iRacing. While it may not be up to spec with today’s racecars, this car brings memories back for many people. With a powerful 358 Cubic Inch Chevy V8 blasting out 650 horsepower through its blow overs and a hefty weight of 3700 lbs, this car is also a handful to drive. This vehicle and its counterpart, the Ford Thunderbird, do not feature any power steering whatsoever so a pair of muscles might be necessary to wheel this beast around any oval racetrack.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Chevrolet Monte Carlo Gen 3 - 1987","released":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-nascar-legends-ford-thunderbird-1987":{"hp":"625","kg":"1678","lbs":"3700","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"351 Cubic Inch Ford V8Power: 625 hp","year":"1987","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"Another classic Gen 3 NASCAR from the 1987 season, the Thunderbird makes its entry into iRacing to compete with the 1987 Monte Carlo. Full of its own memories, this car is ready to whiz around any racetrack. This car and its 351 Cubic Inch Ford V8 weighing at 3700 lbs is ready for stiff and heavy competition against the Gen 3 NASCAR Chevrolet Monte Carlo on any track during any weekend of the year. While it may has less horsepower than its Chevy counterpart, it has a slightly higher power to weight ratio which gives it just a little more kick in its acceleration. The true test for sure is if anybody on iRacing can beat the 212.809 mph qualifying speed set by Bill Elliot at Talladega in 1987 with a lap time of 44.998 seconds.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Ford Thunderbird Gen 3 - 1987","kg_per_hp":"2.68","released":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-nascar-legends-pontiac-grand-prix-1987":{"hp":"650","kg":"1678","lbs":"3700","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"1987","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The new Pontiac Grand Prix - 1987 Gen 3 car is the 4th addition to iRacing's NASCAR gen 3 class cars from the 1987 season. The car while has similarities to the others like same fuel capacity, same weight, and similar acceleration time and configuration, this car still has some differences besides the badge on the car. For starters, the car has a Borg Warner super T-10 4-speed manual transmission, and the independent with coil springs and anti-rollbar with live axle truck arm suspension gives the car the typical gen 3 1987 technology and features that makes the Pontiac Grand Prix a blast from the past.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Pontiac Grand Prix Gen 3 - 1987","kg_per_hp":"2.58","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-nascar-o-reilly-chevrolet-camaro":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter Pushrod V8","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The new Camaro for the NASCAR’s XFINITY series, this new rendition of the car makes the competition all the more tougher and the action more spectacular. The new aerodynamic possibilities from the new Chevrolet Camaro means the car is a bit more fuel-efficient than its previous generations. This reduces drag slightly while also making more downforce on the car making it more stable. Inside the car, the interior is all but different for each model. On the Camaro, the gauges are in the center and also to the left. The car also itself features a strong metal body to keep its drivers safe from any nasty wrecks that happen during raceday.","wiki_title":"NASCAR XFINITY Chevrolet Camaro","kg_per_hp":"2.41","released":"2019-09-04"},"asphalt-nascar-o-reilly-ford-mustang":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter Pushrod V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Ford has brought out the new Mustang rendition to battle against the new Camaro and the new Supra. Time will tell if this will work to Ford’s advantage or not. The car follows the guidelines of the other XFINITY cars in its field with a 358 Cubic Inch V8 engine, 650 horsepower, and the standard 18.5 gallon fuel tank. With weight now under 3500 lbs, the car is a tad lighter giving slightly more acceleration. The vehicle's gauges itself are all on the center row to give maximum visibility to the driver no matter where the steering wheel input is. With top speeds over 180 mph and a very good 0-60 acceleration time, this new Mustang seems ready for the oval racing scene.","wiki_title":"NASCAR XFINITY Ford Mustang","kg_per_hp":"2.41","released":"2019-09-04"},"asphalt-nascar-o-reilly-toyota-supra":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch 5.8 Liter Pushrod V8","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The new Supra is one of the oddest looking NASCAR vehicles but one day may prove its dominance on the track. Same 358 Cubic Inch V8 engine with 650 hp as its other XFINITY counterparts, the XFINITY Toyota Supra may be one of the more interesting NASCAR shapes to enter into the modern era of NASCAR racing. With same 18.5 gallon fuel tank and 3450 lb weight as other XFINITY current gen vehicles, this Supra is ready to race alongside its fellow competitors. Like the Mustang, the gauges are in the center though it has one extra gauge to the right hand side. The oddball bit about the Supra's interior is that for gauge count, the Camaro and Mustang have 7 gauges while the Supra has 6 gauges making this car a truly unique racing machine.","wiki_title":"NASCAR XFINITY Toyota Supra","kg_per_hp":"2.41","released":"2019-09-04"},"asphalt-nascar-truck-chevrolet-silverado":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"0","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The new Silverado for the Craftsman Truck Series is truly a new advancement in technology. The downforce and aerodynamics of this vehicle is better than previous truck generations. Part of the new generation of NASCAR Truck series vehicles, this all-new model featuring new cutting edge technology both on the interior and exterior keeps the driver safe from any hard-hitting accident out on the track. The power, engine, fuel, and weight are the same from the previous incarnation of the truck series which makes this truck all the more easier to drive for even the inexperienced of drivers.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Craftsman Chevrolet Silverado - 2022","kg_per_hp":"2.41"},"asphalt-nascar-truck-ford-f150":{"kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 Degree V","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The 3rd brand of the NASCAR Craftsman Trucks has made its way into iRacing in the form of the F150. This new throroughbred is full of power, prestige, and excitement to keep fans glued to their seats. Finally adding the final truck that is part of NASCAR's Craftsman truck series, this modern truck racer can now finally race in iRacing competitions alongside its Chevrolet Silverado and Toyota Tundra enemies. Using the same engine, weight, and almost similar top speed as the others, this truck can be competitive if a driver knows how to wheel one of these powerful beasts that need a whole lot of taming.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Craftsman Ford F150","released":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-nascar-truck-ram":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Ilmor NT1 V8","year":"2026","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The new Ram 1500 for NASCAR's Craftsman truck series seems to be a call back to the days when Dodge used to be in the truck series until for a while it went down to 3 manufacturers between Chevrolet, Ford, and Toyota. For the Craftsman Truck Series, the 4 brand battle is now back with a new face but carries some familiar roots and history. The new Ram 1500 is powered by a 650 horsepower Ilmor NT1 V8 engine with a 4 speed manual transmission built on a mild-steel and full roll cage chassis, an SLA front and truck arm live axle rear suspension with multipot caliper brakes on both front and rear axles and the good ole Goodyear Eagle tires gives this Ram 1500 some technological improves to brag about.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Craftsman Ram 1500","kg_per_hp":"2.41","released":"2026-03-09"},"asphalt-nascar-truck-toyota-tundra":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 degree V","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The Tundra’s OEM Cast-Iron Block engine produces over 600 horsepower. Even though the restrictor plate limits the car to under 200 mph, its still a high-powered racing vehicle on the track. Based on its road going Tundra variant, the Tundra truck is the other choice when choosing a vehicle to run in any truck series race. With weight over 3400 lbs and acceleration just at around the 4 second mark, no matter who drives this untamed beast, they are gonna have a great time driving it around the NASCAR racetracks no matter how easy or how difficult the challenge may be.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Craftsman Toyota Tundra TRD Pro","kg_per_hp":"2.41"},"asphalt-nascar-whelen-tour-modified":{"hp":"612","kg":"1200","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"2645","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 Degree V8","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The new Whelen Modified is the true answer to modern open wheel oval racecars and this car is no exception. The power it lays down is truly amazing. The 600+ horsepower OEM Cast-Iron Block V8 engine produces an exquisite amount of torque making the car a quick accelerating beast. This ride itself needs whole new levels of taming even around the many short tracks that iRacing has today. With all new construction and many other technological advancements over the previous Whelen Modified model, the excitement that this new model will create will not go unnoticed by viewers, fans, and the drivers themselves.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Whelen Modified","kg_per_hp":"1.96"},"asphalt-nissan-gtp-zx-t":{"hp":"806","kg":"953","lbs":"2101","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"2966 cc, single overhead camshaft, V6","year":"1988","wiki_type":"IMSA Prototype","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Massive power and a 3,000 cc engine, the GTP ZX-T is one of the most fearsome cars on the racing circuit. With weight almost a ton, it has lightning fast acceleration of under 2 seconds. With its history starting back in 1984 when Nissan Motors started their long drive in the IMSA GT Championship, things first started off with the Lola T810 before gears shifted towards the GTP ZX-T with the T meaning \"Turbo\" thanks to its efficient turbocharger. Being the only car to crush the Porsche 962 by 11 seconds at Miami, this car showed its brute power and fast 0-60 2 second acceleration time makes other race cars truly fear it. With a narrow manufacturer championship defeat while winning the drivers championship in 1988, they came back in 1989 along with Geoff Brabham at the wheel crowning the Nissan GTP ZX-T in pure racing glory and triumph.","wiki_title":"Nissan GTP ZX-T","kg_per_hp":"1.18","released":"2026-03-09"},"asphalt-pontiac-solstice":{"hp":"177","kg":"1337","lbs":"2948","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"2.0 Liter Ecotec","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Beginner GT and Beginner Prototype","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Made for road course beginners, the Pontiac Solstice teaches drivers the art of driving a road course car. With a small 2.0 Liter Ecotec engine producing only 177 horsepower, this car weighing only 2948 lbs makes it quite nippy on its feet when driving it around the track. With a 0-60 acceleration time of just under 8 seconds and a fuel capacity of just 14 gallons, not many people know the whereabouts of this car and since all new iRacers that sign up for the first time receive this car, it gives many drivers a great learning curve to those that deal with it.","wiki_title":"Pontiac Solstice","kg_per_hp":"7.55"},"asphalt-pontiac-solstice-rookie":{"hp":"177","kg":"1337","lbs":"2948","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"2.0 Liter Ecotec","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Beginner GT and Beginner Prototype","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The Rookie version of the Pontiac Solstice, this car teaches rookie drivers how to handle the real car. With the same 2.0 liter Ecotec and 177 horsepower engine as its non-rookie counterpart, the road-going Solstice is truly quite a beginners dream choice. With 0-60 acceleration time of just under 8 seconds and weight of just under 3000 lbs, it can still be an iRacer rookie car choice when given the proper tools and the proper learning to deal with the car. It teaches young iRacers how to handle road course vehicles on the asphalt and teaches them how to reach maximum grip and how to keep the car on the track.","wiki_title":"Pontiac Solstice - Rookie","kg_per_hp":"7.55"},"asphalt-porsche-718-cayman-gt4-clubsport-mr":{"hp":"425","kg":"1320","lbs":"2910","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.8 Liter DOHC 24-valve Flat-Six","year":"2020","wiki_type":"GT4","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"One of Porsche’s newest racecars, the 718 Cayman GT4 Clubsport MR embodies everything that a Porsche should be. The speed, handling, and excitement that Porsche delivers is also shown in this very same racecar. The car features a 6 speed PDK dual-clutch automatic transmission for smooth transitions between upshifting and downshifting the gears. It also has ABS, traction control, and electronic stability control for ease of driving experience and skill to even the most novice of drivers. Also, the steering of the car is electrohydraulic power steering and also aluminum six piston brakes on the front and four piston brakes on the rear for maximum stopping and braking power. Finally, this Porsche features McPherson strut suspension on both front and rear for excellent rebounds over certain bumps on any racetrack that comes its way.","wiki_title":"Porsche 718 Cayman GT4 Clubsport MR","kg_per_hp":"3.11","released":"2020-03-02"},"asphalt-porsche-911-cup-992-2":{"hp":"520","kg":"1300","lbs":"2866","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Naturally Aspirated 4.0 Litre Flat-Six","year":"2025","wiki_type":"GT3 Cup","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Featuring a bit more weight but more power than its predecessor, the 911 GT3 Cup (992.1), the new 911 GT3 Cup (992.2) is still full of its own surprises. The car has a Naturally Aspirated 4.0 Litre Flat-Six engine making 520 hp and a fuel tank capacity of 29 gallons (110 liters). The has a quick 0-60 time of just over 3 seconds and features a 6-speed sequential transmission, a unibody chassis with recycled composites, and a double wishbone multi-link suspension making it quite a capable machine. With Brembo piston brakes with iron rotors and ABS and Michelin wheels, it seems to be that this is the 911 GT3 Cup car of the future.","wiki_title":"Porsche 911 GT3 Cup (992.2)","kg_per_hp":"2.50","released":"2025-12-08","updated":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-porsche-911-gt3-cup-991-legacy":{"hp":"485","kg":"1305","lbs":"2878","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"3,996 cc DOHC flat-6","year":"2017","wiki_type":"GT3 Cup","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Porsche and its 4,000 cc DOHC flat-6 engine gives drivers thrill, but also fine mechanics that gives the 911 GT3 Cup (991) superiority in the field of motor racing across the whole world. Based on the famous Porsche 911 road going model, it features revised aerodynamics, improved rollcage, new wheels, and a revised chassis. The transmission inside the car is a paddle shift, race-bred, pneumatically-activated six speed that makes this car geared heavily towards trackdays and racedays alike. Using lightweight materials with a stripped-out cabin to keep weight as low as possible, it truly is a technological advancement in the racing world.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Porsche 911 GT3 Cup (991)","kg_per_hp":"2.69"},"asphalt-porsche-911-gt3-cup-992-1-legacy":{"hp":"510","kg":"1260","lbs":"2778","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"DOHC Naturally-Aspirated Flat-6","year":"2021","wiki_type":"GT3 Cup","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The newest GT3 Cup to hit the GT Cup racing scene brings out the 911 GT3 Cup (992.1) from Porsche. Their newest and latest high-tech thoroughbred is gonna become a hot contender on the road racing circuit and the features it has will definitely bring this car to a spotlight worthy of fame and fortune. The modern day technological advancements on the car include power assisted rack and pinion for precision steering, aluminum six piston brakes on the front tires and four piston brakes on the rear tires, and double wishbone suspension on the front tires with multi-link suspension on the rear tires. Finally, its 6 speed semi-automatic gearbox gives the car ease of upshifting and downshifting for efficient throttle control.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Porsche 911 GT3 Cup (992.1)","kg_per_hp":"2.47","released":"2021-09-07"},"asphalt-porsche-911-gt3-r-legacy":{"hp":"520","kg":"1360","lbs":"2998","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Water-Cooled 4.0 Liter Flat-Six","year":"2021","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The Porsche 911 GT3 R is a cutting edge technically advanced vehicle from the giant automaker Porsche that is definitely a fan favorite to race today. It has a 520 horsepower water cooled 6-cylinder engine capable of delivering enough torque for the roaring beast. With a 31.7 gallon fuel tank and a weight of nearly 3000 lbs, this car can go the distance and throw itself around out on the racetrack. A 0-60 time of 2.8 seconds give it a fast acceleration and its mid-engine displacement keep the car balanced on the track. Other features of the car include Michelin 310/680-18 and 310/710-18 tires for very good gripping power, a 6-piston aluminum monobloc brake calipers for above average braking power, and a double wishbone and multilink suspension system with adjustable dampers and adjustable anti-roll bars for handling and stability. The car's transmission is a 6-speed constant-mesh sequential gearbox for smooth upshifts and downshifts and a direct fuel injection fuel feed with dry sump lubrication to keep it racing for hours on end making this car quite the vehicle to beat.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Porsche 911 GT3 R","kg_per_hp":"2.62","released":"2021-06-08"},"asphalt-porsche-911-gt3-r-992":{"hp":"565","kg":"1250","lbs":"2756","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Water-cooled six-cylinder boxer engine","year":"2023","wiki_type":"GT3","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A new GT3 beast for the road racing scene the Porsche 911 GT3 R (992) is the replacement for the previous 911 GT3 R model from 2021. While its only been two years between the two cars, the improvements made on this vehicle over the last have definitely shown. Such improves for the car include a Single mass flywheel, Four-valve technology, Direct fuel injection, Dry sump lubrication with oil/water heat exchanger, Carbon fiber intake manifold, and many more coming from its water-cooled six-cylinder boxer engine making over 560 hp. The car also comes with many other improvements on its two axles such as independent rear suspension, High-performance spherical bearings, Wheel hubs with center lock wheel nuts, Motorsport dampers, Damper potentiometers, Shim adjustment system and high performance braking power from its brake discs and its brake calipers making this car very technologically advanced for the road racing scene at any road course circuit.","wiki_title":"Porsche 911 GT3 R (992)","kg_per_hp":"2.21","released":"2023-06-05"},"asphalt-porsche-911-rsr":{"hp":"510","kg":"1235","lbs":"2723","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Water cooled six cylinder boxer","year":"2018","wiki_type":"GTE","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A breakthrough innovating in 911 Racing, the RSR GTE is the improved version of the GT3 Cup (991) and tuned to perfection by German Engineering. The cornering ability and the weight give the car a balanced feel throughout the entirety of the racing vehicle. Featuring AP racing caliper brakes for maximum stopping power, the car and its Michelin racing tires give it the grip it needs to battle any turn and any corner on the track. With Front and rear double A-arms with coilovers and a Multimatic Dynamic Suspensions Spool Valve (DSSV) adjustable cartridge-type dampers, featuring blade-adjustable front and rear anti-roll bar for its suspension the Porsche 911 RSR GTE is truly one of the most highly technological cars in the world.","wiki_title":"Porsche 911 RSR GTE","kg_per_hp":"2.42","released":"2018-06-04"},"asphalt-porsche-919":{"hp":"1157","kg":"875","lbs":"1929","drivetrain":"4WD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Porsche 2.0 Liter Direct-Injected Turbocharged V4 with lithium-ion battery","year":"2018","wiki_type":"LMP1","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A Le Mans LMP1 racer designed to give Audi’s R18 and Peugeot’s 908 a run for it’s money, the 919 by Porsche is a real competitor. It can seriously throw power down when needed to get the edge in competition. The car features a Double a-arm suspension at both ends while at the front it uses a pushrod-actuated heave element, anti-roll bar, and torsion bars suspension. The rear suspension of the car uses a pullrod-actuated heave element, anti-roll bar, and torsion bars as well. With a paddle-actuated, semi-automatic 7 speed transmission for smooth and easy gear changing, this car and its carbon disc brakes with monobloc calibers can speed past any other car that happens to be in its way not to mention the car has a 22 gallon fuel tank to stay out on the track a lot longer than others.","wiki_title":"Porsche 919 Hybrid","kg_per_hp":"0.76","released":"2018-03-05"},"asphalt-porsche-963-gtp":{"hp":"670","kg":"1030","lbs":"2271","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Porsche 9RD 4.6L V8 twin-turbocharged twin-supercharged 32-valve DOHC","year":"2023","wiki_type":"LMDh / GTP","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"With the LMDh / GTP field now at 5 cars, the Porsche 963 along with the Acura ARX-06 complete the roster for LMDh / GTP cars for the 2023 season. Although Alpine and Lamborghini are debuting their fiery beasts next year for the 2024 season, time will tell if those spec machines come to the iRacing platform. In the meantime, the Porsche 963 is a technological marvel of sophisticated design and implementation with many features packed inside. First off, the car has a carbon-fibre and aluminium honeycomb monocoque chassis for lightweight and durability out on the racetrack to give it the toughness that it needs. Another component of this car is the XTrac, single specification hybrid system 7 speed racing gearbox that gives the car the final push to over 200 mph (320 kmh). Combined with a powerful Porsche 9RD 4.6L V8 that is both twin-turbocharged and twin-supercharged gives this car over 650 horses of pure fiery firepower.","wiki_title":"Porsche 963 LMDh / GTP","kg_per_hp":"1.54","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-radical-sr10":{"hp":"431","kg":"725","lbs":"1598","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"RPE-Ford Turbocharged 2261cc","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Prototype","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The newest Radical to come to iRacing, the SR10 is definitely going to turn some heads. The car itself is packed with a ton of features and technology. The engine for the car is a RPE-Ford 2261cc engine with 380 ft lbs of torque and its turbocharged with direct injection with twin-independent variable cam timing and with drive-by-wire throttle linkage. The turbocharger for the car is a custom garrett turbocharger giving the car plenty of power and acceleration. The powertrain is a six-speed hewland sequential transaxle and the chassis is a lightweight spaceframe with safety cell and crash structure design. For the car's suspension, it features a fully adjustable nik-link system with front and rear unequal-length top and bottom wishbones and its lightweight fabricated to keep the weight down as much as possible. Finally the car has Radical four-pot caliper brakes with floating 48-vane disc brakes giving the car ample braking power. With the Radical center lock tires with cast aluminum wheels, this car is ready for any raceday no matter what day it is.","wiki_title":"Radical SR10","kg_per_hp":"1.68","released":"2022-06-06"},"asphalt-radical-sr8":{"hp":"380","kg":"650","lbs":"1433","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Powertec","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Prototype","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"With a 2.6 liter, 32 Valve V8, the Radical SR8 V8 throws 380 horsepower down to the road like no other. Its quick acceleration to 60 mph and top speed of 172 mph makes the SR8 a road course car feel quite snug. The car features a Powertec P-Tec 6 speed sequential manual transmission and weighs under 1500 lbs for fast acceleration to 60 mph that are under 3 seconds. Being one of Britain's finest beginner prototype cars, this car is well known for clocking one of the fastest times at Nurburging's famed Nordschleife with a 6:48.28 lap time until it was beaten in 2010 by a Pagani Zonda R. While Dominic Dobson drove this vehicle to victory at the 2015 Pikes Peak International Hill Climb, its no wonder why this car has been considered one of the very best in its business.","wiki_title":"Radical SR8 V8","kg_per_hp":"1.71"},"asphalt-ray-ff1600":{"hp":"116","kg":"504","lbs":"1111","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Ford Kent 1.6 Litre","year":"2023","wiki_type":"Formula Ford","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Featuring 116 hp from its 1.6 liter Ford Kent engine, the Formula Ford 1600 from Ray Race Cars is the newest open wheel road racing vehicle on the iRacing service. The car comes packed with a load of features that makes this low powered formula car quite an unique specimen for those that drive and race it. The car features twin side mounted water radiators for its cooling, adjustable suspension, AP racing caliper brakes, Avon tires, GKN assembly driveshaft, and a tubular steel welded chassis to keep its durability intact. The Hewland LD200 4 speed gearbox makes this car easy for many newcomers who want to focus more on the racing and not so much on gear selection.","wiki_title":"Ray Race Cars Formula Ford 1600","kg_per_hp":"4.34","released":"2023-03-07"},"asphalt-renault-clio-r-s-v":{"hp":"200","kg":"1032","lbs":"2275","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Renault HR13 4 cylinder 1330 cm3 Turbo","year":"2023","wiki_type":"Clio Cup","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The newest Renault in iRacing, this French car joins the new Clio Cup Series on iRacing with some of its own technological advancements and innovations. For starters, the car features a Renault HR13 4 cylinder Turbo engine making 200 hp with a Sequentially controlled dog clutch box with 5 gears and ZF differential for its transmission. The McPherson suspension keeps the car agile and nimble while its disc brakes give it ample braking power. Finally the Michelin tires gives it the grip and handling and its FIA GT3 fuel tank gives it enough fuel for some long distances making this car fun but also a cruise-like sunday drive when visiting some of its biggest venues on the schedule.","wiki_title":"Renault Clio R.S. V Cup","kg_per_hp":"5.16","released":"2023-03-07"},"asphalt-riley-mkxx-daytona-prototype-2008-legacy":{"hp":"500","kg":"1032","lbs":"2275","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Pontiac V8 Power: 500 hp (493.16 bhp) (367.75 kw)","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Prototype","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Ready for Road Course racing, the MkXX monsters the track like no other prototype machine in racing. Even though this car is not used any longer in Daytona Prototype racing, the MkXX was the product of a long awaited arrivals from Riley Technologies. With the company being founded in 2001 by Bob and Bill Riley, they have come quite a way's in the racing world. By 2008, they started racing in GTLM and GT3 cars to show how much they show their passion of motorsports. Without Riley Technologies, the Daytona Prototype that we know of today couldn't come to fruition without the help of both Bob and Bill Riley.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Riley MkXX Daytona Prototype - 2008","kg_per_hp":"2.06"},"asphalt-scca-spec-racer-ford":{"hp":"105","kg":"758","lbs":"1670","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"1.9 Liter Fuel-Injected SOHC 8 Valve Hemi","year":"2009","wiki_type":"Beginner GT and Beginner Prototype","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"A lightened racer, the Spec Racer Ford combines Solstice and Legends car attributes for a balanced feel. With a fuel capacity of 7 gallons and weight under 1700 lbs this Spec Racer Ford is quite a light car on its feet. Even though its 0-60 mph acceleration time is a rather slow 6.3 seconds, for many drivers thats quite alright with them. The car is built on a tube frame chassis with a fiberglass, 3-section body. The suspension is a front/rear rocket arm with coil-over shock/springs that contains a lower \"A\" arm with also dual externally adjustable anti-roll bars for maximum car handling, stability and also driver safety. Using Continental Tire radial-ply spec tires with dry and rain versions available, this car is ready for any racetrack that it goes to and always brings in a good crowd for all to enjoy.","wiki_title":"SCCA Spec Racer Ford","kg_per_hp":"7.22","updated":"2021-06-08"},"asphalt-silver-crown":{"hp":"819","kg":"726","lbs":"1600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"355 Cubic Inch","year":"2009","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"A monstrous power machine, the Silver Crown delivers all 800 horses on the track easily. With its 355 cubic inch, it never lacks power on any track that it runs at on the schedule. With a 75 gallon fuel tank and 1600 lbs this car can definitely go long distances very easily. With a 0-60 mph acceleration time of 2.1 seconds, this car is no slouch either. Many famous drivers over the years have raced in the Silver Crown racecar such as Tony Stewart, Jeff Gordon, J.J Yeley, Ryan Newman, A. J. Foyt, Al Unser, and also Mario Andretti. This car is one of those lightning quick machines that not all drivers can tame so easily. Great practice and skill is a very well respected attribute across all forms of racing but for this car, its really an attribute that is worth having.","wiki_title":"Silver Crown","kg_per_hp":"0.89"},"asphalt-skip-barber-formula-2000":{"hp":"150","kg":"567","lbs":"1250","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"20 SOHC 4-Cylinder","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Beginner Open Wheel","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"With a 150 horsepower engine, the Formula 2000 is the grassroots car for all open wheel race car drivers. Even though the fuel tank is small, this car can go great distances. Its 5.20 gallon fuel tank with its 1250 lb weight makes it a very nimble car to drive. With a 0-60 mph time of 4.5 seconds, this car is not a slowpoke but for its breed its quite a fun and average vehicle for all that drive it. Using BF Goodrich Tires for maximum grip and traction, drivers are quite thankful for these tires as they allow the car to stick to the track very well. With its 20 SOHC 4-Cylinder engine, its powerful enough to make this car do fantastic racing for all to see.","wiki_title":"Skip Barber Formula 2000","kg_per_hp":"3.78","updated":"2019-12-02"},"asphalt-srx":{"hp":"700","kg":"1474","lbs":"3250","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"396 Cubic Inch Ilmore V8Power: 700 hp (690.424 bhp) (514.849 kw)","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The SRX car has been one of the few independent oval racing series that turned some heads in only its few season outings and its stars and car are the reason why. Crafted by Tony Stewart and Ray Evernham, the SRX is an interesting beast unlike any oval racing machine out there. Its design looks a Ferrari F40 with oval racing bits bolted to it but that's where the resemblance and similarity ends. The car is powered by a 700 horsepower Ilmore 396 Cubic Inch V8 giving it the fast power it demands along with the usual 4 speed manual transmission making it more familiar with its star drivers of the past. A symmetrical tube frame plus its SLA axle coil over suspension gives the car flexibility, handling, and precision out on the track and giving it also some toughness and rigidity. Other things the car features are 4-piston PFC brakes along with a nearly 24 gallon fuel tank and Goodyear Radial tires for maximum grip and longevity to keep the car out on the racetrack longer.","wiki_title":"Fury Race Cars SRX","kg_per_hp":"2.11","released":"2024-03-05"},"asphalt-stock-car-pro-series-chevrolet-cruze":{"hp":"415","kg":"1385","lbs":"3053","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"6.8L Pushrod V8","year":"2022","wiki_type":"SCB","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The Chevrolet Cruze SCB is iRacing's newest car from South America along with its counterpart, the Toyota Corolla SCB. With a 3053 lb weight, 136.8 liter fuel tank, a 6.8L Pushrod V8, and 415 hp, this car has quite the powerful punch to give to its competitors. The car also has 410 ft lbs of torque for quick acceleration and a 6 speed sequential paddle shift gearbox with a limited slip differential. The suspension is front and rear double wishbone which gives the car handling, grip, and a comfortable ride for many racers to enjoy. For a car being in the Stock Car Brazil series. it really is quite the beast that many will have to tame throughout a race on any raceday.","wiki_title":"Chevrolet Cruze SCB","kg_per_hp":"3.34","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-stock-car-pro-series-toyota-corolla":{"hp":"415","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1385","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"3053","lbs_src":"sheet","kg_per_hp":"3.34","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-street-stock-casino-eagle":{"hp":"375","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"One of the two newest street stocks to hit the short track oval racing scene, the Casino M2 is a classic looking car but with modern safety standards and design. The car features the same power rating, engine, fuel capacity, and weight from the old Street Stock - Panther C1 but is on a fiberglass steel body with an OEM frame with an SLA floating leaf spring for its chassis and suspension and 4 pot caliper disk brakes. Besides the old and traditional 4 speed manual transmission, the grassroots that these cars are known for are still going strong even with the new generation of street stock racecars.","wiki_title":"Street Stock - Casino M2","kg_per_hp":"4.11"},"asphalt-super-formula-lights":{"hp":"275","kg":"584","lbs":"1287","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"1.6 Liter Toyota Yaris 3 Cylinder TGE33 Turbocharged","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Super Formula Lights","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The car that is the feeder series to the Super Formula Toyota and Honda cars on iRacing, Dallara's 324 Super Formula Lights car is brand spanking new and a successor to its previous 320 model. The car features a 1.6 Liter Toyota Yaris 3 Cylinder TGE33 Turbocharged making 275 horsepower giving it ample power and performance and it also features a Hewland 6 speed sequential transmission. The car features Dallara's own carbon monocoque chassis for lightness and durability with a double wishbone pushrod with inboard springs and dampers suspension for many adjustments in the garage. 4-piston Brembo brakes and even Kumho tires for grip and longevity makes this car one that drivers need to master in order to gain entry into more prestigious and faster open wheel racecars. Make sure to not underestimate the car or it may overestimate you.","wiki_title":"Dallara 324 Super Formula Lights","kg_per_hp":"2.12","released":"2024-03-05"},"asphalt-super-formula-sf23-honda":{"hp":"543","kg":"670","lbs":"1477","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Honda HR-417E 2.0L DOHC Inline-4","year":"2023","wiki_type":"Super Formula","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The newest SF23 Super Formula car that made its way into the iRacing 2023 Season 4 Patch 2 release notes comes the Honda SF23 Super Formula. This car incorporates pretty much of the same technology as its Toyota counterpart but it does have key differences that makes it stand out a bit more. First off, the car is powered by a Honda HR-417E 2.0L DOHC Inline-4 engine making 543 horsepower compared to the 570 horsepower of its Toyota counterpart. The car also weights a bit heavier too at 670 kg (1,4177.10 lbs) compared to the Toyota's 600 kg (1322 lbs). Besides that the car is a 6 speed paddle shift gearbox for smooth transitioning through the gears and also features electric power-assisted rack and pinion steering with Yokohama ADVAN radial dry slicks while its rain tires are treaded giving the car grip, handling, and ease of overall driving just like its Toyota counterpart.","wiki_title":"Honda SF23 Super Formula","kg_per_hp":"1.23","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-super-formula-sf23-toyota":{"hp":"570","kg":"600","lbs":"1322","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Toyota TRD-01F 2.0L Turbocharged DOHC Inline-4","year":"2023","wiki_type":"Super Formula","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The Toyota SF23 Super Formula is iRacing's first super formula spec vehicle in sim history. The car features a good variety of equipment, technology and others but the main ones will be featured for now. The SF23 Super Formula features a 570hp Toyota TRD-01F 2.0L Turbocharged DOHC Inline-4 engine for plenty of firepower come raceday. Other features of the car include a 6-speed paddle shift gearbox, direct fuel injection, electric power-assisted rack and pinion steering, and finally it has Yokohama ADVAN radial dry slicks and treaded rain tires for any dry or rainy condition. This makes the SF23 Super Formula very well suited to road courses not just in Asia but also in Europe, North America, Oceania, and more.","wiki_title":"Toyota SF23 Super Formula","kg_per_hp":"1.05","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-super-late-model":{"hp":"558","kg":"1270","lbs":"2800","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch, OEM Cast-Iron","year":"2013","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Speed and handling meet together in the Super Late Model. This 557 horsepower engine gives drivers a handful when out on the track. Being a higher powered version of the standard Asphalt Late Model, this vehicle with its 358 Cubic Inch OEM Cast Iron Block 90 Degree V8 engine makes it a true powerful beast. Its 22 gallon fuel tank with its 2800 lb weight makes it a rolling target on the track. Its 0-60 mph acceleration time of around 3.5 seconds makes it a quick oval car to those that drive it. Being part of the United States National Touring Series, this car has been truly one of the greatest oval cars that has ever graced the stock car asphalt oval name and tradition of its time.","wiki_title":"Super Late Model","kg_per_hp":"2.28","updated":"2021-03-09"},"asphalt-supercars-chevrolet-camaro-gen-3":{"hp":"600","kg":"1340","lbs":"2954","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"LS 5.7 Liter V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"V8 Supercar","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The newest generation of V8 Supercars hit the Australian racing scene and Chevrolet seems more than ready. Taking the spot of the dearly, never to-be-forgotten Holden brand, their first car in this century of V8 Supercars racing is the Camaro ZL1 V8 Gen 3. The car has a LS 5.7 Liter V8 engine making 600 horsepower. A composite boy on a tube frame chassis, double A-arm with coilover spring and anti-roll bar suspension, AP Racing piston disc brakes, Dunlop tires, and an Xtrac 6-speed sequential transmission gives this car plenty of speed and power whether its racing on the mountain at Bathurst, the beautiful coastal sights of Surfers Paradise, or even on the streets of Adelaide.","wiki_title":"Chevrolet Camaro ZL1 V8 Gen 3","kg_per_hp":"2.23","released":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-supercars-ford-mustang-gen-3":{"hp":"635","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1340","lbs":"2954","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Coyote 5.4 Liter V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"V8 Supercar","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Ford Australia's newest V8 Supercar comes in the form of the Mustang GT V8 Gen 3, the main rival to Chevrolet's V8 Supercar, the Camaro ZL1 V8 Gen 3. The features on this car is pretty much the same as its Chevrolet counterpart with a Xtrac 6-speed sequential, composite body on a tube frame chassis, front and rear double A-arm with coilover springs and anti-roll bar suspension, AP Racing piston disc brakes, and Dunlop Tires. The only main difference between the two cars, other than the badges and model names, are the engines that they use. The Chevrolet is an LS while the Ford is a Coyote that hopefully doesn't get too wily.","wiki_title":"Ford Mustang GT V8 Gen 3","kg_per_hp":"2.11","released":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-supercars-ford-mustang-gt-legacy":{"hp":"635","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1398","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"3081","lbs_src":"sheet","kg_per_hp":"2.20","released":"2019-12-02"},"asphalt-supercars-holden-zb-commodore-legacy":{"hp":"635","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1395","lbs":"3075","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"5.0 Liter Normally Aspirated V8","year":"2019","wiki_type":"V8 Supercar","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Holden’s new monster, the Commodore ZB is really quite the treat. Though this treat starts out sour and gets sweeter as drivers get used to it. Sharing the same engine as the Ford Mustang GT V8, the Holden itself is quite a very good car to anyone that can tame its immense power. Sharing the same Xtrac 1293 six-speed sequential transmission, Double wishbone suspension, and the same Dunlop SP Sport tires, the only difference between the two cars is truly who the driver behind the wheel is. This car also has some former roots since its actually an Opel based model.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Holden Commodore ZB V8","kg_per_hp":"2.20","released":"2019-12-02"},"asphalt-toyota-gr86":{"hp":"223","kg":"1359","lbs":"2996","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"2.4 Liter Flat 4 Cylinder","year":"2023","wiki_type":"Beginner GT","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"A new cup car for new competition, the Toyota GR86 Cup is the newest of Toyota's racing machines. Featuring a 223 hp 2.4 Liter Flat 4 Cylinder engine and SADEV 6-speed sequential gearbox, this car makes quick work of its gears with a very precise handling and driving feel. Other features of the car include a Bosch engine management, Alcon brakes, JRI adjustable shocks, and TGRNA-designed Macpherson struts for its suspension. With Continental tires for above average grip, this car is ready for the GR Cup North America series.","wiki_title":"Toyota GR86 Cup","kg_per_hp":"6.09","released":"2022-12-06","updated":"2025-12-08"},"asphalt-usf-2000":{"hp":"175","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"500","lbs":"1102","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Mazda 2 Liter MZR","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Indy Lights","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"A less powerful cousin than its PM18 counterpart, the USF17 2000 is also a great way to open-wheel racing without a whole lot of power. This results in close-racing action for many drivers. Using a less powerful version of the MZR engine than what the Indy Pro 2000 PM18 uses, this makes the USF17 2000 an easy car to learn and master to any novice driver on the iRacing sim. Since it has the same weight and fuel tank as its slightly more powerful cousin, that makes the USF17 2000 another starting car for the open-wheel enthusiasts climb to the likes of Formula 1 and IndyCar.","wiki_title":"Tatuus USF17 2000","kg_per_hp":"2.86","released":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-vw-jetta-tdi-cup":{"hp":"170","kg":"1379","lbs":"3041","drivetrain":"FWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"2 Liter, inline 4 cylinder TDi diesel","year":"2010","wiki_type":"Sports Car","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"A Inline 4 cylinder TDi diesel may not prove to be powerful, but its 170 horsepower is more than enough to give this car a top speed of over 130 mph and is competitive against the Mazda MX-5. The Jetta is a good start for sports cars and prototypes. Its 2 liter inline 4 cylinder TDi Diesel engine and its 3041 lbs makes it a throughbred of a racer. Its 14.5 gallon fuel tank and 0-60 mph acceleration time of just under 6 seconds makes it a true beginners car for any new coming road course racers. It also uses a twin shaft, dual clutch automatic transmission to ease upshifting and downshifting for all drivers. The car itself uses a Sachs race suspension and tires from Pirelli, which means that this particular car is a purpose built vehicle that knows that a diesel powered racer can still get the job done.","wiki_title":"Volkswagen Jetta TDi Cup","kg_per_hp":"8.11"},"asphalt-williams-toyota-fw31":{"hp":"740","kg":"605","lbs":"1334","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Toyota RVX-09 2.4 Liter V8","year":"2009","wiki_type":"Ex-Formula One","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"The F1 beast before the MP4-30, the FW31 is still a F1 lover’s dream with a V8 Toyota RVX-09 engine under the hood. 740 hp and a top speed of 215 mph makes the car a rocket. With a 35.28 gallon fuel tank and weight of 1334 lbs makes the car a true beast of a machine with a blistering 0-60 mph acceleration time of just under 4 seconds. The car uses a Carbon-aramid and honeycomb composite monocoque chassis to lower weight and to make the car even more flexible around the turns. Its front suspension features a carbon fibre double wishbone with pushrod activated springs and also zero keel geometry. The rear suspension of the car has a double wishbone, with push rod activated springs making the rear part of the car light and agile while keeping it firmly on the road. With a Williams 7-speed electro-hydraulically actuated to make gear changing very smooth and using Bridgestone Potenza tires for maximum grip and traction, this car is truly one of the most technologically advanced thoroughbreds of its time.","wiki_title":"Williams-Toyota FW31","kg_per_hp":"0.82"},"site-dallara-dw12":{"hp":"700","kg":"726","lbs":"1600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"2.2 Liter, 134.3 cu in V6,","year":"2014","wiki_type":"IndyCar","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Full of power and passion, the Dallara DW12 is Italy’s finest in IndyCar racing. Its 700 hp V6 turbocharged engine and its aerodynamics give the car insane grip. Named after Dan Wheldon, It has a carbon fiber monocoque chassis with a double A-arm pushrod suspension. This gives the car flexibility and makes it easily adjustable to suit to any track on the schedule. Using an Xtrac 1011 6 speed semi-automatic transmission and a Braille MLT7Ti Battery for extra oomph, this Dallara DW12 has the muscle of a NASCAR Gen 6 cup car with no fenders and less weight overall that counts for its high top speed.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Dallara DW12","kg_per_hp":"1.04"},"site-dallara-ir05-circa-2009":{"hp":"650","kg":"726","lbs":"1600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"3.5 Liter DOHC V8","year":"2005","wiki_type":"IndyCar","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"With its 3.5 liter DOHC V8 spewing out over 600 hp, the IndyCar Dallara from 2005 is light and quick. With a 0-60 time of just under 3 seconds, this car is ready for any race day situation that throws at it. The carbon brakes that this car uses in conjunction with its BBS and O.Z. Racing rims, weight and stopping power are greatly reduced. Firestone tires are still the main supplier of tires after a short period when Goodyear tires ruled the IndyCar Series for only 4 seasons. With safer methanol fuel, this older Indycar breed is still a champ for many of the drivers that piloted this car.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Dallara IR-05","kg_per_hp":"1.12"},"site-dirt-micro-sprint":{"hp":"120","kg":"354","lbs":"780","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Side Mounted 600cc 4-stroke motorcycle","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The winged brother to the dirt micro sprint car - non-winged variant, this car carries all the same features and technology and parts of its non-winged variant. 120 horses under its belt and weight of 780 lbs, this car accelerates off the line quickly and its competition knows it. The transmission, chassis, tires, suspension, fuel tank and engine and more are all carried over making the winged and non-winged dirt micro sprint cars a cost effective and much more cheaper way to get some fun out on any small, local dirt oval track no matter where you take it.","wiki_title":"Dirt Micro Sprint Car - Winged","kg_per_hp":"2.95","released":"2024-03-05"},"site-dirt-micro-sprint-non-winged":{"hp":"120","kg":"345","lbs":"760","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Side Mounted 600cc 4-stroke motorcycle","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Small, nimble, quick, and fun, the Dirt Micro Sprint Car Non-Winged is quite a versatile vehicle with 160 horses under its belt. With a low weight of 760 lbs, this car shoots of the line quickly and is no slouch too. Chain and sprocket transmission making repairs easy and efficient and a tublar space frame chassis makes the car flexible around the turns. A solid axle coil over torsion bar suspension gives it the give and bend that it demands. Other features of the car are 2-piston brakes and a substantial fuel tank so that it can last a whole heat or feature segment of a race without refueling.","wiki_title":"Dirt Micro Sprint Car - Non-Winged","kg_per_hp":"2.88","released":"2024-03-05"},"site-dirt-midget":{"hp":"400","kg":"408","lbs":"900","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Pushrod Inline 4-cylinder","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"With 400 horsepower underneath a car weighing under 1000 lbs, the Dirt Midgets show what little dirt cars can do when been given the right driver. These high speed temperamental speedsters are popular in the United States, Australia, and New Zealand. Known commonly as speedcars in the Australia continent, these cars are here today thanks to the brilliant work of Kurtis Kraft and Solar who build the earliest known examples. Fitted with roll cages and many other safety features, these cars spit out power and fun to create a whole new dementia of racing.","wiki_title":"Dirt Midget","kg_per_hp":"1.02","released":"2017-12-04"},"site-dirt-outlaw-micro-sprint-non-winged":{"hp":"167","kg":"345","lbs":"760","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Side Mounted 600cc 4-stroke motorcycle","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The more powerful variant of the regular micro sprint non-winged cars, the outlaw variants boasts an additional 47 horsepower for faster racing with even more stiff competition. The engine specs are the same along with the transmission, chassis, suspension, brakes, wheels, tires, and even the fuel tank and wheelbase giving the outlaw variants just a more powerful option for many iRacers on the service.","wiki_title":"Dirt Outlaw Micro Sprint Car - Non-Winged","kg_per_hp":"2.07"},"site-dirt-outlaw-micro-sprint-winged":{"hp":"167","kg":"354","lbs":"780","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Side Mounted 600cc 4-stroke motorcycle","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Just like the its regular micro sprint car - winged variant, the outlaw version totes 47 more horsepower with the same carry-over features including the engine, transmission, chassis, suspension, brakes, wheels, tires, and even the fuel tank and wheelbase making repairs quicker to perform and parts more easy to find. As always, these cars are just a slightly more powerful version of their less powerful micro sprint car - winged cousins.","wiki_title":"Dirt Outlaw Micro Sprint Car - Winged","kg_per_hp":"2.12"},"site-dirtcar-305-sprint-car":{"hp":"458","kg":"640","lbs":"1400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Stock Block, Push-Rod V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"An entry level dirt sprint car, this 305 has over 450 horsepower to learn drivers what it feels like to drive on the loose stuff. A speed over 100 mph makes it agile and fast for any track in the dirt schedule. First created and driven by Jim Cushman at the Columbus Motor Speedway in 1958, the car and its World of Outlaws series has been synonymous with dirt racing. Its 1 speed transmission gives high acceleration like no other machine today.","wiki_title":"Dirt 305 Sprint Car","kg_per_hp":"1.40"},"site-dirtcar-358-small-block-modified":{"hp":"510","kg":"1157","lbs":"2551","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"358 CID Naturally Aspirated V8","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The 358 Modified is definitely a new modified on the dirt oval racing scene and with over 500 horsepower it has the oomph to powerslide around any dirt oval racetrack. The car itself is a middle midweight of around 2500 or so pounds but does have a pretty good top speed and acceleration time for a dirt oval racecar. For a car with 24 gallons of fuel and a true beast in its own, the 358 modified is definitely a good learner car if one's dirt oval racing dreams is modified racing instead of late model or sprint car racing on the dirt oval scene.","wiki_title":"Dirt 358 Modified","kg_per_hp":"2.27"},"site-dirtcar-360-sprint-car":{"hp":"720","kg":"640","lbs":"1400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Stock Block, Push-Rod V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Over 700 horsepower and a top speed of 130 mph, the 360 pushes the driver to the limits in both turns and on the long straights. Skill is required to drive this monster. Carrying over the same transmission as the Dirt 305 Sprint Car, this high powered beast is another brilliant creation coming from Jim Cushman. First introduced after the Dirt 305 Sprint Car came on the scene, the Dirt 360 Sprint Car is still one of the most challenging dirt cars to drive.","wiki_title":"Dirt 360 Sprint Car","kg_per_hp":"0.89"},"site-dirtcar-limited-late-model":{"hp":"400","kg":"1021","lbs":"2250","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"350 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"With a 350 cubic inch V8 motor, the Limited Late Model is a beginners guide to driving late models on the loose stuff. Based on the asphalt Chevrolet Monte Carlo SS Late Model version, this Limited Late Model teaches drivers the basics and first steps on how to drive a Dirt Late Model. It's two speed transmission makes shifting through the gears and acceleration a painless act to perform. Not as fast as its Pro and Super counterparts, but this car can still be a handful to drive even put into the hands of an experienced driver.","wiki_title":"Dirt Limited Late Model","kg_per_hp":"2.55"},"site-dirtcar-pro-late-model":{"hp":"700","kg":"1021","lbs":"2250","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A 358 Cubic Inch motor that produces 700 horsepower, the Pro Late Model takes the world of Late Model Dirt Racing to the next level of competition. Built on the same chassis, suspension, and transmission of its Limited Late Model cousin, the Pro Late Model is the next step up for Dirt Late Model drivers. With 300 more horsepower and 20 more mph in top speed, these high speed devils can really show their muscle around the track.","wiki_title":"Dirt Pro Late Model","kg_per_hp":"1.46"},"site-fia-cross-car":{"hp":"120","lbs":"959","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Yamaha MT-09 890cc 3 Cylinder","year":"2025","wiki_type":"Off-Road Cross Car","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The new Ligier FIA Cross Car is iRacing's newest addition to the off-road racing scene. Tiny cars but lots of acceleration with little weight and powered by a Yamaha MT-09 890cc 3 cylinder engine making 120 horsepower. A weight of just over 950 lbs and a 0-60 mph time of around 4.5 seconds, this light and agile vehicle with its short wheelbase gives drivers plenty of memorable racing battles. The key to being successful besides the driving attitude would be the jumps as going to fast overshoots the jump and potentially overshooting up the corner entry but going too slow could mean not clearing the jump and not having optimal corner entry.","wiki_title":"Ligier FIA Cross Car","released":"2025-12-08"},"site-ford-fiesta-rs-wrc":{"hp":"600","kg":"1300","lbs":"2999","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Rallycross","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The ST GRC throws its power on the dirt and snow like no other rally car. It’s quick acceleration makes it’s a time punisher in the rally world. Sporting a reinforced multi-point roll cage and a 6-speed M-Sport transmission, it makes acceleration an easy task to accomplish. Using a combination of Michelin, Pirelli, and DMACK tires, the car shines when it tackles asphalt, gravel, dirt, snow and more. Drivers love the car as much as fans love seeing it perform out on the rallycross and rally tracks.","wiki_title":"Ford Fiesta ST GRC","kg_per_hp":"2.17","released":"2017-12-04"},"site-formula-renault-3-5":{"hp":"537","kg":"711","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"1567","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Naturally","year":"2018","wiki_type":"Open Wheel","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The Formula 3.5 is the next car to go when learning the overdrive feel of open wheel racecars. With more power and speed, skill starts to develop as drivers learn to master this new beast. The car uses a Carbon Fiber Monocoque chassis to keep weight down, acceleration high, and keeping its rigidity nice and firm out on the track. It also boasts a Recardo 6-speed sequential transmission so that upshifts and downshifts are quick and smooth. Featuring a Naturally Aspirated 90 Degree V8 with over 530 hp, weight of under 1600 lbs, and 0-60 mph in nearly 3 seconds, this fast racecar will need a lot of taming. The Michelin tires that it has will provide the car with plenty of traction and grip to keep you on the road and not on the grass.","wiki_title":"Formula Renault 3.5","kg_per_hp":"1.32","released":"2018-12-03"},"site-lucas-oil-off-road-pro-2-truck":{"hp":"700","kg":"0","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"0","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"410","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Offroad Trucks","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"With a big loud engine and heavy weight, this 2 Truck can throw a lot of its weight around on the track. Visiting a few selection of offroad dirt tracks, this one is an exclusive among many out there. Unlike other iRacing vehicles, this 2 Truck and its slightly faster 4 Truck cousin are the only iRacing vehicles that have the Shocks option in the garage menu due to the suspension featured on these beasts. The 410 Cubic Inch V8 that this monster is powered by is sure to be a popular screamer among fans and drivers. The 12 gallon fuel tank is nothing to write home about but the 4000 lb weight on this and the 4 Truck make them the heaviest vehicles in iRacing.","wiki_title":"PRO 2 Truck","released":"2019-06-03"},"site-lucas-oil-off-road-pro-4-truck":{"kg":"0","kg_src":"sheet","lbs":"0","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"410","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Offroad Trucks","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The 4 Truck is a mighty off-road vehicle that can take quite a beating. Of all the off-road vehicles, this thing knows how to tear up the track for some good action on the track. The same 410 Cubic Inch V8 powers this monster but up to 900 horsepower giving it mighty acceleration. Whilst the 2 truck is a 3 speed transmission, this one is a 6 speed sequential which does not allow a misshift both up and down. Both vehicles rev up to almost 8,000 rpm and sharing the same weight of 4000 lbs as the 2 truck, this 4 truck is also sure to be quite a sight for great racing action and fierce competition.","wiki_title":"PRO 4 Truck","released":"2019-06-03"},"site-lucas-oil-off-road-pro-2-lite-truck":{"hp":"400","kg":"1814","lbs":"4000","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"410 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2019","wiki_type":"Offroad Trucks","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The starter off-road truck for an off-road drivers career, the 2 Lite is one of the more fun off-road trucks ever made. Less powerful than its other cousins, it still makes it a very fun machine to drive. The Cubic Inch V8 engine that it possess makes it a very powerful beast though less powerful than its PRO 2 and PRO 4 relatives. Same weight of 4000 lbs and same fuel capacity of 12 gallons as its relatives, this 2 Lite is a great addition for those offroad truck fans looking to get their feet muddy in the loose stuff.","wiki_title":"PRO 2 Lite","kg_per_hp":"4.54","released":"2019-09-04"},"site-mazda-mx-5-cup-2010":{"hp":"172","kg":"1179","lbs":"2600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"2.0 L 170 bhp","year":"2010","wiki_type":"Beginner GT and Beginner Prototype","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Despite its small power and low top speed, the MX-5 2010 is a starter car for all fans and sim drivers alike. It has almost 13 gallons of fuel for semi-long distance racing. Ever starting its season back in 2006, the little Mazda MX-5 has been wowing the fans with road racing never before seen. As a production model, nobody imagined that an under powered vehicle could bring so much fandom and joy to all that enjoy motorsport racing. Being a cousin to its roadster and later Global MX-5 Cup variants, the MX-5 Cup of yesteryear still brings on quite a fantastic show.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Mazda MX-5 Cup - 2010","kg_per_hp":"6.85"},"site-mazda-mx-5-roadster-2010":{"hp":"172","kg":"1179","lbs":"2600","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"2.0 L 170 bhp","year":"2010","wiki_type":"Beginner GT and Beginner Prototype","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Same specs as it’s cup counterpart, the steering wheel is on the other side for an extra challenge. The roadster is a car like no other. Drivers themselves will feel a little uneasy at first since they will have to deal with right-side steering which is native to its Japanese culture that drives on the left side of the road. Being the Cup version, this Roadster version is a tad slower than the Cup car but it shows that little cars and indeed do big things.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Mazda MX-5 Cup Roadster - 2010","kg_per_hp":"6.85"},"site-mclaren-honda-mp4-30":{"hp":"700","kg":"702","lbs":"1548","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Honda RA615H Hybrid 1.6 Liter V6","year":"2015","wiki_type":"Formula One","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"F1 cars rule the open wheel circuit and the MP4-30 is one of its most modern designs. With 700 hp and a top speed over 210 mph, its no walk in the park to tame this monster. An improved variant of the McLaren MP4-29 and an inspiration for the current McLaren MP4 and MCL models, the car features a carbon-fibre composite survival cell chassis keeping both weight and acceleration under control. The car uses a Pushrod system with inboard torsion bars and dampers for the front and a Pullrod system with inboard torsion bars and dampers for the rear. The car itself uses Honda lithium-ion batteries for fast recharging, their lightweight durability, and ease of maintenance. Using Pirelli P Zero and Pirelli Cinturato tires in soft, medium and hard compounds to battle dry and wet conditions, this car remains a tough one to master but when mastered, it comes off as a victorious feeling.","wiki_title":"McLaren MP4-30","kg_per_hp":"1.00"},"site-mini-stock-dirt":{"hp":"200","kg":"1066","lbs":"2350","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"2.3 Liter Inline 4 Cylinder 2V OHC","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Mini Stock","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Is the small and nimble dirt mini stock the car for you? Well with 200 horsepower from its 2.3 Liter Inline 4 Cylinder 2V OHC engine and a weight of just over 2300 lbs, this small car can throw its weight around with its 5 speed manual transmission pretty well. Other features of the dirt mini stock include a modified OEM frame with reinforced roll cage for its chassis, OEM Strut and 4 link rear coil springs for its suspension, OEM disc and drum brakes, and with the addition of Hoosier racing tires for grip, the dirt mini stock is definitely a fun way to begin and learn closed wheel dirt oval racing competition for many dirt oval racing fans.","wiki_title":"Dirt Mini Stock","kg_per_hp":"5.33"},"site-nascar-chevrolet-ss-cup-car":{"hp":"875","kg":"1497","lbs":"3300","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Chevrolet Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2013","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A Chevy Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8 and over 800 horsepower, the Chevy SS is ready to devour the competition loud and proud. Its monstrous Chevy Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8 and its weight of just 3300 lbs make the car one of the fastest accelerating oval cars on the circuit. Acceleration to 60 mph at around 3 seconds and modern safety features makes the NASCAR Chevy SS Gen 6 one of the more known NASCAR vehicles still racing to this very day.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) NASCAR Cup Chevrolet SS - 2013","kg_per_hp":"1.71"},"site-nascar-cup-series-ford-fusion":{"hp":"875","kg":"1497","lbs":"3300","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Chevrolet Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2016","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Pro","bio":"A monster Ford ready for the track, this Fusion car is ready to take on both Camry and SS models on the NASCAR circuit. One of the Chevy SS competitors and the Ford Fusion and its Chevy Pushrod 358 Cubic Inch V8 give it the same 3300 lbs and 2.9 0-60 acceleration time as its Chevy SS rival. Drivers like the Ford Fusion much as the Chevy SS drivers like theirs.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) NASCAR Cup Ford Fusion - 2016","kg_per_hp":"1.71"},"site-nascar-truck-chevrolet-silverado-2008":{"hp":"625","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 Degree V","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"A monster truck for its time, the 2008 Chevy Silverado can still fight against NASCAR’s current Chevy Silverado model of today. It may be a tad slower but can still shine. While using a OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 Degree V as its engine and weight of 3450 lbs with a 18.5 gallon fuel tank, this older NASCAR Truck can still be a true fighting force come raceday. The 0-60 acceleration time of 4.0 seconds is still on par with NASCAR trucks today though the new NASCAR trucks support advancements in safety, aerodynamics, drafting, fuel efficiency, and much more.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) NASCAR Truck Series Chevrolet Silverado - 2008","kg_per_hp":"2.50"},"site-nascar-truck-series-dirt-chevrolet-silverado":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 degree V","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Ready for dirt racing at a half mile oval, the Silverado takes to the track with special dirt tires. 600 horsepower and weight over 3000 lbs makes this truck difficult to master. The dirt version of the Silverado is one of the most difficult dirt vehicles in all of iRacing. Weighing the most and having high horsepower makes this truck a slick, heavy beast thats hard to control. No matter what the drivers tell you out on those dirt oval tracks, the NASCAR Dirt Trucks are truly the #1 vehicle that gives them a very high rewarding feel.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Camping World Dirt Chevrolet Silverado - 2017","kg_per_hp":"2.41"},"site-nascar-truck-series-dirt-ford-f-150":{"kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 Degree V","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The final dirt oval truck to make its way into iRacing, the Dirt F150 has arrived. Full of slippery and powersliding goodness, this truck has power to keep up with its other powerful rivals. Same power, same weight, and same level of competition as its other competitors from Chevrolet and Toyota, this Ford truck that races around the dirt oval racing scene will need a lot of practice, skill, and taming in order to even put down a quick lap time.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Camping World Dirt Ford F150 - 2020"},"site-nascar-truck-series-dirt-toyota-tundra-trd":{"hp":"650","kg":"1565","lbs":"3450","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"OEM Cast-Iron Block 90 degree V","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Dirt Trucks debuted at Eldora only a couple years ago and popularity soared through the roof. The Dirt Tundra is one of the finest examples of race trucks on the loose stuff at the racing circuit. The other Dirt Truck vehicles to drive, the Dirt Silverado and Dirt F150 remains as challenging as its two other rivals. Many drivers really have a tough time distinguishing the differences between these two trucks since they are the same for the most part. The powersliding that these drivers perform in these vehicles are as comparable as to the Dirt Late Models that do many of the same tasks that these Dirt Trucks do.","wiki_title":"NASCAR Camping World Dirt Toyota Tundra - 2017","kg_per_hp":"2.41"},"site-porsche-mission-r":{"hp":"1088","kg":"1500","lbs":"3307","drivetrain":"4WD","transmission":"Sequential Shift","year":"2022","wiki_type":"Electric Motorsport","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"iRacing's first EV racing machine, the Porsche Mission R is truly a vehicle in its own right and in many categories. The car is powered by 2x oil-cooled PMSM electric motors supplied by a 82 kWh Lithium-Ion battery giving it superfast charging whenever needed. Other features of the car include 18 inch magnesium wheels with central locking in a five twin spoke design, Michelin 30/68 and 31/71 tires with bio-based renewable materials, and even a double wishbone axle with McPherson struts for its suspension. Finally, the car comes with six-piston calipers for its front brakes and four-piston calipers for its rear brakes giving it ample braking power. With electric power steering and a carbon fibre composite exoskeleton cage, this car is truly a modern machine of the contemporary era.","wiki_title":"Porsche Mission R","kg_per_hp":"1.38","released":"2022-09-06"},"site-pro-mazda":{"hp":"240","kg":"494","lbs":"1090","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Mid-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Mazda “Renesis”","year":"2008","wiki_type":"Open Wheel","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The mighty Rotary engines Mazda have been using since the 787B gives the Pro Mazda a speed over 150 mph. The weight is only around half a ton compared to other racing cars in its field. The carbon fibre features the latest safety practices while giving the crew to move the car easily around the paddock and garage area. Its Hewland 6 speed gearbox give the car efficient gear changes at the flick of its paddle shifter while using 98 octane gasoline for faster engine rpm and rotation. Using an electronic fuel injection and naturally aspirated as well, the car and its Cooper Tire & Rubber Company tires give the car maximum grip, traction, and higher capabilities like never before.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Pro Mazda","kg_per_hp":"2.06"},"site-sprint-car":{"hp":"820","kg":"669","lbs":"1475","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"410 Cubic Inch, Stock Block,","year":"2014","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"A real thrill in racing, the Sprint Car has over 800 horsepower and weight under 1500 lbs to ensure thrills and spills for the crowd. Its 410 Cubic Inch Stock Block Push Rod V8 engine makes it the breed of racecar to watch during racing. Its 28 gallon fuel tank with its 1475 lb weight really makes it go since its 0-60 mph acceleration time is 2 seconds even. Being the untamed machine that it is, drivers have had their fair share keeping control of this tough open wheel racecar. Famous drivers like Eddie Sachs, Don Branson, A.J. Foyt, Parnelli Jones, Roger McCluskey, Tony Stewart, and J.J. Yeley had/have always a ball driving this car despite its low stability and noticeable handling.","wiki_title":"Sprint Car","kg_per_hp":"0.82"},"site-street-stock-casino":{"hp":"375","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"One of the two newest street stocks to hit the short track oval racing scene, the Casino M2 is a classic looking car but with modern safety standards and design. The car features the same power rating, engine, fuel capacity, and weight from the old Street Stock - Panther C1 but is on a fiberglass steel body with an OEM frame with an SLA floating leaf spring for its chassis and suspension and 4 pot caliper disk brakes. Besides the old and traditional 4 speed manual transmission, the grassroots that these cars are known for are still going strong even with the new generation of street stock racecars.","wiki_title":"Street Stock - Casino M2","kg_per_hp":"4.11","released":"2024-06-03"},"site-street-stock-eagle":{"hp":"375","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"358 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2024","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Novice","bio":"The other of the two newest street stocks to hit the short track oval racing scene, the Eagle T3 is Ford Thunderbird look-alike but with modern safety standards and design for the modern short track oval racing environment. The car features the same power rating, engine, fuel capacity, and weight from the old Street Stock - Panther C1 but is on a fiberglass steel body with an OEM frame with an SLA floating leaf spring for its chassis and suspension and 4 pot caliper disk brakes. Besides the old and traditional 4 speed manual transmission, the grassroots part of the Eagle T3 car is still known for going strong, a trait also carried by the Casino M2.","wiki_title":"Street Stock - Eagle T3","kg_per_hp":"4.11","released":"2024-06-03"},"site-street-stock-panther":{"hp":"375","kg":"1542","lbs":"3400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"H-Shifter","engine":"Small Block Chevrolet","year":"2010","wiki_type":"Oval","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The rookie car that starts oval careers, the Street Stock - Panther C1 is the grassroots oval car with a 375 horsepower engine. Like any other car, make sure you treat it well. With a Small Block Chevrolet engine with a 22 gallon fuel tank, the car's 3400 lb weight makes it heavy as its 0-60 mph acceleration time is affected to roughly 5 seconds. Being part of JR Motorsports grassroots oval entry series, the Street Stock - Panther C1 is one car that all iRacers started out on the asphalt oval side. Even though they drive the NASCAR Cup, Xfinity, and Trucks of today, they cannot deny that they truly did drive these beginner oval cars and taught them the basics of stock car auto racing.","wiki_title":"Street Stock - Panther C1","kg_per_hp":"4.11"},"site-subaru-wrx-sti":{"hp":"585","kg":"1300","lbs":"2866","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"4 Cylinder Boxer with front-mount turbocharger","year":"2018","wiki_type":"Rallycross","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"The might of the Subaru WRX STI VT17x GRC comes in the form of its engine. Spewing out 560 horsepower, it’s a rallycross car born to win. Failure for this Subaru is never an option at all. The car's transmission powered by a SADEV 6-speed sequential dog-engagement gearbox ensures no mis-shifts at all. The 3-plate carbon racing clutch ensures smooth transmission gear changes while the cars' McPherson strut front with inverted Ohlins TPX struts / Control arm rear with Ohlins TTX damper suspension keep the car fit, stable, and as agile as possible. With the braking system coming from Alcon, their rallycross brakes show that the car ensures maximum stopping power. For tires, the Subaru uses BFGoodrich g-Force RC02 for maximum grip and traction on both asphalt and dirt.","wiki_title":"Subaru WRX STI VT17x GRC","kg_per_hp":"2.22","released":"2018-06-04"},"site-super-dirtcar-big-block-modified":{"hp":"757","kg":"1200","lbs":"2646","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"467 CID Naturally Aspirated V8","year":"2020","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The Dirt Big Block Modified is the big brother to the Dirt 358 Modified. For this car, precision, skill, and a good amount of practice is definitely required to tame this vehicle. With over 750 horsepower coming from its 467 CID Naturally Aspirated V8, this car can definitely get the job done at any dirt oval racetrack. The speeds of this car at nearly 150 mph (242 kmh) makes it one of the fastest dirt oval cars in the sim. With also a good accelerating time to get off the line quick and soar away from other competitors, this car may became a fan favorite to many dirt oval racers on iRacing and maybe to the community as a whole.","wiki_title":"Dirt Big Block Modified","kg_per_hp":"1.59"},"site-ump-modified":{"hp":"750","kg":"1089","lbs":"2400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"410 Cubic Inch Push-Rod V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"Another dirt racer ready to hit the scene, the UMP Modifieds come with lots of horsepower and power sliding action. They are always hungry for attention. Racing in over 19 states and 1 province in Canada, these cars have truly gone global. The design of the car is specifically made for dirt track racing and its 750 horsepower 410 Cubic Inch Push-Rod V8 gives the car fast acceleration and very high dirt track speeds. This is no easy beast to handle and needs taming and great execution of the car to put down a fast lap time.","wiki_title":"Dirt UMP Modified","kg_per_hp":"1.45"},"site-usac-360-sprint-car":{"hp":"720","kg":"624","lbs":"1375","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Stock Block, Push-Rod V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Clubman","bio":"A wingless 360 sprint car, the USAC model has over 700 horsepower and a weight under 1400 lbs to give drivers a new challenge to tackle. With a Stock Block Push Rod V8 engine and a 30 gallon fue ltank, these lightweight cars with 0-60 mph acceleration time of 2.5 seconds makes it a rocket of a car. With no starter inside the vehicle, these guys along with their winged cousins have to be bump started by a bump truck that pushes the car ever so gently to get them going. Famous dirt non-winged sprint car drivers include A.J. Foyt, Al Unser, Mario Andretti, Ken Schrader, Jeff Gordon, and many more that all started out on dirt before transferring to the asphalt giants.","wiki_title":"USAC 360 Sprint Car","kg_per_hp":"0.87"},"site-usac-410-sprint-car":{"hp":"821","kg":"669","lbs":"1475","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Stock Block, Push-Rod V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"More Power, more speed, the USAC 410 is the ultimate non-wingless dirt car. If you don’t drive the car right, it won’t care how you drive it at all. So drive the car like you stole it and make sure you wear a smile on your face. With a Stock Bock Push Rod V8 Engine and over 800 horsepower, these cars that weigh than 1500 lbs shoot off like a rocket thanks to its 0-60 mph acceleration time of 2.2 seconds. Even though it has a big 30 gallon fuel tank for its fuel capacity, these 410 non-winged sprints can really put on a fantastic show for the drivers and fans that love to see action at a high speed pace like never seen before. To many people that drive these monsters, they are hard to tame and as equally as hard to control.","wiki_title":"USAC 410 Sprint Car","kg_per_hp":"0.81"},"site-v8-supercar-ford-falcon-2009":{"kg":"1400","lbs":"3086","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"305 Cubic Inch 5 Liter Push Rod V8","year":"2009","wiki_type":"V8 Supercar","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"An older version of today’s V8 Supercar Falcon, the Falcon V8 2009 is still a competitive racer in the V8 Super Car Championship. The car itself was made by the Ford Australia company on the continent and country of Australia known for making quality vehicles for the Australian and also the left-hand traffic as well. Despite the car being nearly a decade old, it can still pack a lot of punch for its age. With slightly older V8 Supercar aerodynamics, the car's acceleration suffers a little bit while still maintaining its top speed.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Ford Falcon V8 Supercar - 2009"},"site-v8-supercar-ford-fg-falcon-2014":{"kg":"1400","lbs":"3086","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"5.0 Liter Naturally Aspirated V8","year":"2014","wiki_type":"V8 Supercar","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Australian power at its best, the Ford Falcon FG V8 gives Australian cars the muscle it needs to sail to victory with its 644 horses that possess passion and power. Based on the road going Ford Falcon FG, the V8 Supercar version comes with a 6HP26 6 speed transmission that gives the car high top speed and good acceleration. With its Supercharged BOSS 5.0 Liter Naturally Aspirated V8 engine and V8 Supercar style aerodynamics, this V8 car is ready for any track on the Australian V8 Supercar calendar.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Ford Falcon FG V8 - 2014"},"site-v8-supercar-holden-vf-commodore-2014":{"kg":"1400","lbs":"3086","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"5.0 Liter Naturally Aspirated V8","year":"2014","wiki_type":"V8 Supercar","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"Ready to hit the track, the Commodore VF can take on the Falcon with all of its might. It certainly gives the Falcon car a run for its money on the track. Being an improved version of the VE Commodore, the VF Commodore achieved 5 stars on the ANCAP ratings. The car itself was only in production from 2013 to 2017 but is a monster in the V8 Supercar series. While the car has undergone major interior changes, it has also undergone an electronic power steering system that makes the car more fuel efficient for the cost of any ordinary steering feel.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Holden Commodore VF V8 - 2014"},"site-vw-beetle":{"hp":"600","hp_src":"sheet","kg":"1300","lbs":"2999","lbs_src":"sheet","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Straight-Four","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Rallycross","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"A contender to go head to head against the Ford Fiesta GRC, the VW Beetle GRC gives the Fiesta a whole new rival to face off in the world of rallycross racing with over 550 hp. Featuring a Straight Four Turbocharged Engine and a 7.4 gallon fuel tank with a 2866 lb weight, this GRC Beetle is ready for any rallycross track on Earth. With 0-60 mph acceleration speed at 2.2 seconds, its a fast rocket launcher of a racecar and the drivers know it. A plethora of drivers today have driven this high tech Beetle and what they feel is the immense acceleration and power that these little cars possess inside them.","wiki_title":"Volkswagen Beetle GRC","kg_per_hp":"2.17","released":"2017-12-04"},"site-vw-beetle-lite":{"hp":"300","kg":"1300","lbs":"2866","drivetrain":"AWD","engine_loc":"Rear-Engine","transmission":"Paddle Shift","engine":"Straight-Four Turbocharged Engine","year":"2021","wiki_type":"Rallycross","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"The little cousin to the Beetle GRC, the Beetle Lite is a slightly slower but still plenty o' fun car to drive. With a sequential six speed gearbox, and a hydraulically actuated triple-disc sintered metal clutch, this car can breeze through the gears easily. It also has a good 0-60 acceleration time too at 3.8 seconds and has a permament four-wheel drive with multi-plate limited-slip differentials for its final drive that brings out more of the car's technological capabilities. Other features of the car include a McPherson strut and damper suspension system, a servo-assisted rack and pinon steering column, and ventilated disc brakes for good handling and braking power out on the track. The final features on the car include a GRC-conformant reinforced steel body for good durability and toughness while also featuring Yokohama ADVAN A054 tires to ensure its grip and lifespan of those tires securely to the track.","wiki_title":"Volkswagen Beetle - Lite","kg_per_hp":"4.33","released":"2021-06-08"},"site-world-of-outlaws-410-sprint-car":{"hp":"892","kg":"640","lbs":"1400","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"Stock Block, Push-Rod V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The ultimate thrill on dirt, the 410 is ready to deliver its 900 horsepower on the slippery stuff to give you the taste of what driving on the dirt feels like. Hang on tight because this puppy does wheelies with tiny throttle inputs. Using a Stock Block Push Rod V8 engine and a 30 gallon fuel tank, this car eats fuel like no other monster of a car. With a 1400 lb weight and a 0-60 mph acceleration time of a blistering and quick 2.5 seconds, this machine makes the drivers feel its might and grip whenever it goes around any dirt ovals from 1/4 Mile to a full Mile in length. With a top speed of just over 150 mph or just under 250 kmh, the car that pops wheelies seems so much fun to do that drivers sometimes forget what they are truly driving.","wiki_title":"World of Outlaws 410 Sprint Car","kg_per_hp":"0.72"},"site-world-of-outlaws-super-late-model":{"hp":"850","kg":"1021","lbs":"2250","drivetrain":"RWD","engine_loc":"Front-Engine","transmission":"Sequential Shift","engine":"438 Cubic Inch V8","year":"2017","wiki_type":"Dirt Oval","difficulty":"Advanced","bio":"The fastest Dirt Late Models ever, the Super version has over 800 horsepower. It’s also ready to tear up the dirt for excitement and fun. Drive with caution. With a 438 cubic inch V8 engine and a 28 gallon fuel tank, this car and its 2250 lb weight gives it a fascinating 0-60 mph acceleration time of just under 3 seconds. Many people have driven this car many times and have shown that not all can drive it so easily at times. Being one of the most popular dirt racing series out there and under the World of Outlaws banner, it seems that the fan base for this car has grown to new heights like never seen before in dirt racing.","wiki_title":"World of Outlaws Super Late Model","kg_per_hp":"1.20"}},"tracks":{"asphalt-adelaide-street-circuit":{"location":"Adelaide, South Australia","length_mi":"2.0","length_km":"3.2","turns":"14","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"25 mph","owner":"City of Adelaide","opened":"1985","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"The Adelaide Parklands is home to one of the most renowned street circuits in the world, the Adelaide Street Circuit and its jewel event, the Adelaide 500. Famous and talented drivers battle door to door at this legendary 2 mile street circuit through the hustle and bustle of downtown Adelaide and its tight, twisty turns that still attracts well over 200,000 people.","wiki_title":"Adelaide Street Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Australia","released":"2025-12-08"},"asphalt-algarve-international-circuit":{"location":"Portimão, Faro","length_mi":"2.9–2.9","length_km":"4.6–4.7","turns":"15 - 16","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Paulo Pinheiro","opened":"2008","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Portugal's most prestigious racetrack, Portimão has been a fan favorite to many road racing enthusiasts since 2008. The varying challenges of its turns between speed and tightness gives the track a flow that defines its character. To this day, Portimão's capacity of 100,000 people make it a true spectacle of a racetrack.","wiki_title":"Autódromo Internacional do Algarve","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Portugal"},"asphalt-auto-club-speedway":{"location":"Fontana, California","length_mi":"1.5–2.8","length_km":"2.3–4.5","turns":"4 – 21","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"35–55 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1997","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Superspeedway","bio":"Welcome to sunny California and Next Gen in California. It’s going to be rainy weather for racing today. The Next Gen in California was located just east of Los Angeles on the site of an old steel mill. The wide, two mile long D-Shaped oval provides both driver and spectator with a great view of the largest attended sporting event in the state.","wiki_title":"Next Gen in California","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States"},"asphalt-autodromo-internazionale-del-mugello":{"location":"Scarperia e San Piero, Tuscany","length_mi":"1.6–3.3","length_km":"2.6–5.3","turns":"7 – 15","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Scuderia Ferrari","opened":"1974","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"In the Apennines, Mugello remains today as one of Italy's favorite circuits. The well-known track combines high-speed straightaways with chicanes and hairpins to make it a fun and twisty complex. Ever since 1974, this three and a quarter mile road course remains a favorite to many people around the world making Mugello \"The Beautiful Track in the Mountains.\"","wiki_title":"Autodromo Internazionale del Mugello","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Italy","released":"2023-12-05"},"asphalt-autodromo-internazionale-enzo-e-dino-ferrari":{"location":"Imola, Emilia – Romagna","length_mi":"3.1–3.1","length_km":"4.9–4.9","turns":"17 – 22","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Con-Ami","opened":"1953","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located approximately 35 kilometers southeast of Bologna, the historic Circuit Enzo e Dino Ferrari combines short and medium speed straights with a challenging mix of slow turns and varying speed chicanes. Despite numerous revisions in order to improve safety, this circuit renamed in honor of the late Dino Ferrari remains one of Formula One’s classics.","wiki_title":"Autodromo Internazionale Enzo e Dino Ferrari","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Italy"},"asphalt-autodromo-nazionale-monza":{"location":"Monza, Lombardy","length_mi":"1.5–6.2","length_km":"2.4–10.0","turns":"4 – 15","configs_n":"9","pit_speed":"35–70 mph","owner":"Comune di Monza & Milano","opened":"1922","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Superspeedway","bio":"Located just a few kilometers to the north of Milan, the legendary Monza Circuit combines long straights with a mixture of chicanes, fast sweeping, and 90 degree turns. The dedicated motorsports facility is the spiritual home of Italian Motor Racing and a cathedral for Ferrari and their fanatical fans, the Tifosi.","wiki_title":"Autodromo Nazionale Monza","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Italy"},"asphalt-autodromo-hermanos-rodriguez-mexico-city":{"location":"Mexico City, Mexico City District","length_mi":"1.0–2.7","length_km":"1.6–4.3","turns":"4 - 19","configs_n":"7","pit_speed":"31–50 mph","owner":"Inter-American Entertainment Corporation","opened":"1959","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval","bio":"Known for the famous Rodriguez brothers that raced here and its famous landmarks like the Magdalena Mixhuca Sports Complex and the Foro Sol Stadium, Autódromo Hermanos Rodríguez has drawn huge crowds from multiple series from F1 to NASCAR and even the former CART and Champ Car series. To this day, the venue can put on a show with its high altitude of just over 7,000 feet giving the cars more speed leading to more excitement for the fans.","wiki_title":"Autódromo Hermanos Rodríguez","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Mexico","released":"2025-09-08"},"asphalt-autodromo-jose-carlos-pace":{"location":"Sao Paulo, State of Sao Paulo","length_mi":"2.7","length_km":"4.3","turns":"15 – 16","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Luiza Erundina","opened":"1940","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located within the southern suburbs of Sao Paulo, the bumpy Interlagos circuit consists of two very distinct sections. The fast outer section combines two very long straights with fast sweeping turns whilst the technical infield contains some very slow corners that demand absolute precision and leave no room for driver error.","wiki_title":"Autodromo Jose Carlos Pace","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Brazil"},"asphalt-barber-motorsports-park":{"location":"Leeds, Alabama","length_mi":"2.4","length_km":"3.8","turns":"16","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Barber Motorsports","opened":"2003","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located east of Birmingham, Alabama, Barber Motorsports Park is a fantastic race and test track for anyone to use. Its 2.38 mile road course and its 16 turns give drivers challenges as they travel down the track. Used by Skip Barber to test their Formula 2000 cars, this circuit loves races whenever they come to town.","wiki_title":"Barber Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2026-03-09"},"asphalt-brands-hatch-circuit":{"location":"West Kingsdown, Kent","length_mi":"1.2–2.4","length_km":"1.9–3.9","turns":"6 – 9","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"MotorSport Vision","opened":"1950","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in Kent, the Brands Hatch Circuit is a rather unique track. Located not far from Britain’s vast motorways, the track contains some of the trickiest turns in automotive racing. 9 turns in all and a gruesome track makes Brands Hatch a fantastic place to visit.","wiki_title":"Brands Hatch Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom"},"asphalt-bristol-motor-speedway":{"location":"Bristol, Tennessee","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.9","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Type: Short-Track Traditional Bullring Oval","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Are you ready for intensity on wheels? Welcome to Bristol Motor Speedway! Bristol’s 26 degree banked concrete bullring provides some of the sports most exciting fender-banging racing. 146,000 thousand permanent seats and a half mile layout guarantees the crowd is loud and hungry for action.","wiki_title":"Bristol Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-bristol-motor-speedway":{"location":"Bristol, Tennessee","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.9","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Type: Dirt Short-Track Traditional Bullring Oval","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Are you ready for dirt racing on wheels? Welcome to Bristol Motor Speedway! Bristol's 26 degree banked dirt bullring provides dirt racing fans some of the most exciting fender-banging racing. 146,000 thousand permanent seats and a half mile layout guarantees the crowd is loud and hungry for action.","wiki_title":"Bristol Motor Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-bristol-motor-speedway-2021":{"location":"Bristol, Tennessee","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.9","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Type: Dirt Short-Track Traditional Bullring Oval","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Are you ready for dirt racing on wheels? Welcome to Bristol Motor Speedway! Bristol's 26 degree banked dirt bullring provides dirt racing fans some of the most exciting fender-banging racing. 146,000 thousand permanent seats and a half mile layout guarantees the crowd is loud and hungry for action.","wiki_title":"Bristol Motor Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-cadwell-park-circuit":{"location":"Louth, Lincolnshire","length_mi":"0.8–2.2","length_km":"1.4–3.5","turns":"8 – 18","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"31 mph","owner":"MotorSport Vision","opened":"1938","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"The scenic Lincolnshire Wolds National Landscape plays host to a racing circuit that has been around for nearly a whole century. That circuit is the Cadwell Park Circuit and with its varying types of turns and decent length straightaways, a track that is normally used for bike racing can also be a friend to even racecars on any given day.","wiki_title":"Cadwell Park Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom","released":"2024-09-03"},"asphalt-canadian-tire-motorsports-park":{"location":"Bowmanville, Ontario","length_mi":"2.5","length_km":"4.0","turns":"10","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Canadian Motorsports Ventures Ltd.","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"The Canadian Tire Motorsport Park located in Bowmanville, Ontario is one of the true classic road courses. The track is not very complex but many racing series have unlocked the secret emerald to lure fans to the stands. With 10 turns and just under two and a half miles, Canadian Tire reminds drivers how challenging a track can be with minimal turns.","wiki_title":"Canadian Tire Motorsport Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Canada"},"asphalt-charlotte-motor-speedway":{"location":"Concord, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.3–2.4","length_km":"0.5–3.9","turns":"4 - 17","configs_n":"8","pit_speed":"25–45 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1960","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Charlotte Motor Speedway at Concord. Even though it was built more than four decades ago, drivers still love to race at this mile and a half quad oval. If Daytona is the pinnacle of NASCAR Racing, then Charlotte has to be just a bumper behind. Fans flock to the largest sports facility in the southeast, home track to many of NASCAR’s teams.","wiki_title":"Charlotte Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2019-03-04"},"asphalt-chicago-street-course":{"location":"Chicago, Illinois","length_mi":"2.1–2.1","length_km":"3.4–3.4","turns":"12","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Chicago Department of Transportation Type: Street Circuit","opened":"2023","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"Welcome to the newest street course on the circuit located in downtown Chicago. This track that is just over 2 miles in length takes drivers through a breathtaking view of Chicago's Grant Park right alongside Lake Michigan and Lakeshore Drive. Not a very complex and tricky track by any means but this track's 90 degree turns definitely make up for its unique shape.","wiki_title":"Chicago Street Course","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States"},"asphalt-chicagoland-speedway":{"location":"Joliet, Illinois","length_mi":"1.5","length_km":"2.4","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"NASCAR Type: Intermediate Tri-Oval","opened":"2001","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Chicagoland Speedway. Chicagoland’s unique arched backstretch makes it worthy to all drivers and fans. Located on the outskirts of Joliet, action here never sleeps as the cars roar around this one and a half mile tri-oval. Opened less than two decades ago, this unique speedway is becoming one of the drivers' favorite racetracks.","wiki_title":"Chicagoland Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-circuit-de-barcelona-catalunya":{"length_mi":"1.1–2.9","length_km":"1.7–4.7","owner":"Barcelona City Council","opened":"1991","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located just a few kilometers to the north of Barcelona, the superb Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya combines medium speed straights with an interesting selection of slow, medium, and high speed turns. This dedicated motorsports facility is a good example of modern circuit design and is highly rated by most of the teams, both as a race and testing venue.","wiki_title":"Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya","wiki_status":"Open","released":"2019-09-04"},"asphalt-circuit-de-ledenon":{"location":"Lédenon, Occitania","length_mi":"2.0","length_km":"3.2","turns":"15","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"37 mph","opened":"1973","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in southern France in the Occitania region, Circuit de Lédenon is a twisty 2 mile complex with challenging corners and fast straights leading to great road racing competition. For drivers they will have to focus as much as they can at Lédenon as this track will make them twist and turn for nearly 15 turns before coming back to the front straight.","wiki_title":"Circuit de Lédenon","wiki_status":"Open","country":"France","released":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-circuit-de-nevers-magny-cours":{"location":"Magny-Cours, Bourgogne-Franche-Comté","length_mi":"2.7","length_km":"4.4","turns":"17","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Jean Bernigaud Nickname: Magny-Cours","opened":"1960","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located just a few kilometers south of Nevers, the Magny-Cours circuit combines several short straights with an interesting selection of slow to medium speed turns, hairpins, and chicanes. Like the Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya, Magny-Cours is a modern facility built specifically for motor racing.","wiki_title":"Circuit de Nevers Magny-Cours","wiki_status":"Open","country":"France","released":"2022-12-06"},"asphalt-circuit-de-spa-francorchamps":{"location":"Stavelot, Wallonia","length_mi":"4.4","length_km":"7.0","turns":"19 - 21","configs_n":"7","pit_speed":"45–50 mph","owner":"Melchior Wathelet","opened":"1921","difficulty":"Pro","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located approximately 50 kilometers north of Liege near the town of Spa, the exhilarating Spa-Francorchamps circuit comes with a challenging mix of fast turns and chicanes. Winding its way among the forests and the foothills of the Ardennes Mountains, Spa-Francorchamps also has the longest lap of all the current Formula 1 circuits.","wiki_title":"Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Belgium","updated":"2024-09-03"},"asphalt-circuit-des-24-heures-du-mans":{"location":"Le Mans, Pays de la Loire","turns":"31 – 33","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Automobile Club de I'Quest Ville du Mans","opened":"1923","difficulty":"Pro","track_type":"Road Course; Street Circuit","bio":"The Circuit des 24 Heures du Mans is France’s pride and joy when it comes to race tracks. The 24 hour race held here remains traditional and draws in crowds, drivers, teams, spectators, and more from around the world to watch Hypercar and GTE car action here at Le Mans. With over 40 racecars during the 24 hour race, Le Mans is by no means a true classic circuit through and through.","wiki_title":"Circuit des 24 Heures du Mans","wiki_status":"Open","country":"France"},"asphalt-circuit-gilles-villeneuve":{"location":"Montreal, Quebec","length_mi":"2.7","length_km":"4.4","turns":"14","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"City of Montreal","opened":"1978","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course; Street Circuit","bio":"Located on the Île Notre-Dame just minutes away from Downtown Montreal, the Circuit Gilles-Villeneuve combines short straights with an uninspiring selection of slow to medium speed chicanes and one hairpin. Despite being a dedicated motorsports facility, the barriers around Circuit Gilles-Villeneuve are very close to the track, giving the circuit a distinctly street feel.","wiki_title":"Circuit Gilles-Villeneuve","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Canada"},"asphalt-circuit-of-the-americas":{"location":"Austin, Texas","length_mi":"1.5–3.4","length_km":"2.4–5.5","turns":"6 – 20","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"35–50 mph","owner":"Circuit of the Americas LLC","opened":"2012","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"One of the newest road courses in America, COTA features the F1 American Grand Prix and boasts 20 unique, challenging turns. This particular track can wear down a driver, but the crowds love the action at this tight and twisty complex. With state-of-the-art facilities that surrounds the track on all sides, COTA remains as one of the gems in the racing world.","wiki_title":"Circuit of the Americas","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-circuit-zandvoort":{"location":"Zandvoort, North Holland","length_mi":"0.9–2.7","length_km":"1.5–4.3","turns":"6 – 14","configs_n":"9","pit_speed":"37 mph","opened":"1948","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located on the shores of the coast of the Netherlands, Mascot Circuit Zandvoort is a circuit where road course racing in Europe never dwindles. The challenging circuit has banking and tight turns to make the drivers really earn their stripes. Of all the tracks in the Netherlands, Zandvoort is truly the “Diamond Of The Coast”.","wiki_title":"Mascot Circuit Zandvoort","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Netherlands","updated":"2023-09-05"},"asphalt-circuit-zolder":{"location":"Heusden-Zolder, Flanders","length_mi":"2.5","length_km":"4.0","turns":"10","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Antoine Palmers de Terlaemen","opened":"1963","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Home of DTM and no stranger to any road racing series, Circuit Zolder is always a nice stop on the schedule to experience more variety of European Racing Circuits. Many people agree that Zolder is a true racing spectacle that contains multiple turns and tight corners which makes this track a motorsports haven.","wiki_title":"Circuit Zolder","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Belgium","updated":"2024-09-03"},"asphalt-circuito-de-jerez-angel-nieto":{"location":"Jerez de la Frontera, Andalusia","length_mi":"2.7–2.8","length_km":"4.4–4.4","opened":"1985","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Hello and welcome to one of Spain's most well known racetracks, the Circuito de Jerez - Ángel Nieto. This pristine track located in the outskirts of Jerez in Andalusia has been a favorite for both racecars and motorbikes for over 30 years. With challenging turns and fast straightaways, this premier track in Europe pays tribute to Ángel Nieto to this day.","wiki_title":"Circuito de Jerez - Ángel Nieto","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Spain"},"asphalt-circuito-de-navarra":{"location":"Los Arcos, Navarre","length_mi":"0.8–2.4","length_km":"1.3–3.9","owner":"MotorSport Vision","opened":"2010","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in the town of Los Arcos, the Circuito de Navarra is a fairly young circuit consisting of a twisting layout with slow and medium speed turns and a few long straightaways. Being the only circuit in the entire autonomous community of Navarre, the Circuito de Navarra has done well with itself being a fan favorite to many people around the world.","wiki_title":"Circuito de Navarra","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Spain","released":"2024-06-03"},"asphalt-concord-speedway":{"location":"Concord, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.7","turns":"3","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Burton Smith","opened":"1982","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Located not far from the famous Charlotte Motor Speedway, the Concord Speedway was a half-mile triangle that packed lots of action. The drivers that headed to this track stunned the crowds at the skills they possessed. Featuring tight turns, this tri-oval was a whole other beast that definitely needed taming.","wiki_title":"Concord Speedway","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States"},"asphalt-darlington-raceway":{"location":"Darlington, South Carolina","length_mi":"1.4","length_km":"2.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"NASCAR Type: Intermediate Egg-Shaped Oval","opened":"1950","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to NASCAR’s oldest superspeedway, Darlington Raceway in South Carolina. The “Lady in Black”, “The Grand Daddy Of Them All”, call it what you will, The Darlington is always one thing, a challenge. This unique mile and a third egg-shaped oval has well earned the nickname “The Track Too Tough To Tame.”","wiki_title":"Darlington Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-daytona-international-speedway":{"location":"Daytona Beach, Florida","length_mi":"1.0–3.6","length_km":"1.7–5.7","turns":"4 – 14","configs_n":"9","pit_speed":"55–60 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1959","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Superspeedway","bio":"Welcome to the Sunshine State and the birthplace of NASCAR, Daytona Beach, Florida. Since 1959, a drivers career can be made or broken at Daytona International Speedway. The two and a half mile tri-oval has served as a proving ground for some of the greatest names in racing. 31 degrees of banking in the turns, and incredible speeds on the straightaways, have led to the inclusion of restrictor plates here. Aerodynamic drafting has become a must have skill in order to stay with the pack and master Daytona.","wiki_title":"Daytona International Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2019-03-04"},"asphalt-detroit-grand-prix-at-belle-isle":{"location":"Detroit, Michigan","length_mi":"2.4","length_km":"3.8","turns":"14","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"40 mph","owner":"Bud Denker","opened":"1992","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"Commonly known as the Detroit Grand Prix, the Detroit Grand Prix at Belle Isle was one of the most prestigious road courses in all of America. Its tight 14 turns of many 90 degree angles has evolved this track from a easy Sunday drive to a difficult Monday morning Rush Hour. No matter how heavy the traffic, drivers always find a way to keep this track under any green flag conditions.","wiki_title":"Detroit Grand Prix at Belle Isle","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States","released":"2018-06-04"},"asphalt-donington-park-racing-circuit":{"location":"Castle Donington, Leicestershire","length_mi":"2.0–2.5","length_km":"3.2–4.0","turns":"10 – 12","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"MotorSport Vision Nickname: The Heart of British Motorsport","opened":"1931","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to Donington Park, the heart of British motorsport located in Leicestershire, England. With over 2 miles in length and over 10 turns, Donington has become one of the world's most favorite racetracks. Of all the British tracks within the United Kingdom, Donington has been home to fantastic racing action for many years.","wiki_title":"Donington Park Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom"},"asphalt-dover-international-speedway":{"location":"Dover, Delaware","length_mi":"1.0","length_km":"1.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Type: Mile Traditional Oval","opened":"1969","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Dover Motor Speedway in Delaware’s capital. This mile long concrete oval houses some of the most intense racing in NASCAR today. Some of the biggest crowds on the eastern seaboard flock to the “Monster Mile” to see the best drivers in the world battle door to door.","wiki_title":"Dover Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-echopark-speedway-atl":{"location":"Hampton, Georgia","length_mi":"0.3–2.6","length_km":"0.4–4.1","turns":"4 – 12","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"30–50 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1960","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to Hampton, Georgia, home of the EchoPark Speedway. This ultra-modern multi-purpose venue has become one of the fastest tracks on the NASCAR circuit. 24 to 28 degree banking around the mile and a half quad oval serves as a slick, super competitive racetrack.","wiki_title":"EchoPark Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-eldora-speedway":{"location":"Rossburg, Ohio","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Stewart-Haas Racing","opened":"1954","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Both by geography and history, Eldora Speedway stands at the epicenter of dirt track racing. Situated in what was once an Ohio cornfield, the half-mile clay oval lies in the very heart of the Midwest racing scene. Hosting some of the biggest events on the calendar to date, Eldora rightly bills itself as “The World’s Greatest Dirt Track.”","wiki_title":"Eldora Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-fairbury-speedway":{"location":"Fairbury, Illinois","length_mi":"0.3","length_km":"0.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Matt Curl","opened":"1946","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Fairbury American Legion Speedway. This fast, thrilling, quarter-mile dirt track keeps drivers on the steering wheel and the pedals. With a 6,600 seating capacity and roaring competition, you can bet that the Fairbury American Legion Speedway is no laughing matter.","wiki_title":"Fairbury American Legion Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2019-09-04"},"asphalt-federated-auto-parts-raceway-at-i-55":{"location":"Pevely, Missouri","length_mi":"0.3","length_km":"0.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Josh Carroll","opened":"1974","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to \"The Ironman Track\" herself, the I-55 Federated Auto Parts Raceway Park. This high speed, 1/3 mile dirt track makes drivers of all ages rip up the track for some good fun. This facility with banking up to 19 degrees and being home to the Ironman 55 has turned it into one of dirt racing’s fastest tracks.","wiki_title":"I-55 Federated Auto Parts Raceway Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-five-flags-speedway":{"location":"Pensacola, Florida","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","opened":"1953","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"A half mile, paved oval opened in 1953, Five Flags Speedway takes its name from its proximity to Pensacola, Florida, known as the “City of Five Flags.” The race track is one of the fastest short tracks in America, thanks to its 15 degree banking and its wide turns that give the track a nearly circular configuration.","wiki_title":"Five Flags Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-fuji-international-speedway":{"location":"Oyama, Shizuoka Prefecture","length_mi":"2.8–2.8","length_km":"4.5–4.6","turns":"14 - 16","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Toyota Motor Corporation","opened":"1965","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"One of Japan's most challenging circuits, Fuji International Speedway has evolved from a high-speed racetrack into a twisty, technical complex. Featuring tough corners and its long front straightaway, the action that is showcased at Fuji lives long even after over 50 years of existence that makes this track a living legend to this day.","wiki_title":"Fuji International Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Japan","released":"2022-06-06"},"asphalt-hickory-motor-speedway":{"location":"Newton, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Ned Jarrett","opened":"1951","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the Tar Heel State and the Hickory Motor Speedway, known as The Birthplace of the NASCAR Stars. This small but exciting 0.363 mile track contains some of the most exciting fender-banging short track racing there is to date. While the track itself has long said goodbye to its former glory years, it can still give the crowds plenty of action.","wiki_title":"Hickory Motor Speedway","country":"United States","released":"2021-09-07"},"asphalt-hockenheimring-baden-wurttemberg":{"location":"Hockenheim, Baden-Württemburg","turns":"7 - 21","configs_n":"10","pit_speed":"31–50 mph","owner":"Tilke GmbH","opened":"1932","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located near the historic city of Heidelberg, the Hockenheimring Baden-Württemberg consists of three short straights and a really diverse mixture of fast, medium, and slow turns including a hairpin. This circuit was also originally built as a test track for Mercedes-Benz cars. The claustrophobic stadium section is the only feature that designer Hermann Tilke has left intact from the Hockenheim circuit as used in recent years.","wiki_title":"Hockenheimring Baden-Württemberg","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Germany","released":"2021-03-09","updated":"2021-12-06"},"asphalt-homestead-miami-speedway":{"location":"Homestead, Florida","length_mi":"1.5–2.3","length_km":"2.4–3.7","turns":"4 – 14","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"45–50 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1995","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to gorgeous south Florida and the Homestead-Miami Speedway. Known today as The Championship Track and one of the favorites on the NASCAR circuit, Homestead draws huge crowds with its distinctive blend of length at a mile and a half and 20 degrees of banking. This leads to real driving exhibitions for happy fans.","wiki_title":"Homestead-Miami Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-hungaroring":{"location":"Mogyoród, Pest","length_mi":"2.7","length_km":"4.4","turns":"14","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Hungaroring Sport Zrt Type: Road Course","opened":"1986","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located just a few kilometers from Budapest, the Hungaroring combines just one straight of note with a complex selection of slow to medium speed turns. Opinions on this circuit are very much divided but whether you love or hate the venue, it appears to have a long term future in the F1 calendar being the only race hosted by a country from the former Eastern Bloc.","wiki_title":"Hungaroring","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Hungary","released":"2021-09-07"},"dirt-huset-s-speedway":{"location":"Brandon, South Dakota","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Tod Quiring","opened":"1954","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Not far from Sioux Falls, the Huset's Speedway is one of the top visited dirt ovals on the World of Outlaws circuit today and its low banking gives drivers a real challenge. Located near the tri-point of the state borders of South Dakota, Minnesota, and Iowa, fans come here to get down and dirty for some classic racing action.","wiki_title":"Huset's Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-indianapolis-motor-speedway":{"location":"Speedway, Indiana","length_mi":"2.5–2.6","length_km":"4.0–4.2","turns":"4 – 16","configs_n":"7","pit_speed":"40–60 mph","owner":"Penske Entertainment Group","opened":"1909","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Superspeedway","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Indianapolis Motor Speedway. Known as “The Brickyard”, Indy is home to the world famous Indy 500, the biggest and largest motorsports race around the world. Considered relatively flat by American standards, the two and a half mile rectangular oval has been full of automotive excitement for over a century.","wiki_title":"Indianapolis Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2022-09-06"},"asphalt-iowa-speedway":{"location":"Newton, Iowa","length_mi":"0.2–1.3","length_km":"0.2–2.1","turns":"4 – 8","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"30–40 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"2006","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to Newton, Iowa, home to the Iowa Speedway. This high-speed short-track features a 7/8ths mile oval. With a D-Shaped oval patterned after Richmond Raceway and with 14 degrees of banking in the turns, Iowa Speedway makes the fans and drivers here cheer loud and hard for “The Track Out in The Plains.”","wiki_title":"Iowa Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-iracing-superspeedway":{"location":"Bedford, Massachusetts","length_mi":"3.0","length_km":"4.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"65 mph","owner":"iRacing.com Motorsports Simulations, LLC","opened":"2002","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Hyperspeedway","bio":"Welcome to high-speed endurance that’s known to all drivers as the iRacing Superspeedway. This 36 degree banked, 3 mile superspeedway isn’t like any ordinary superspeedway. Instead of being a tri-oval superspeedway type, this track is a traditional oval shape and its length makes it a hyperspeedway which makes it rather unique. The restrictor plates have been taken off at this track to see how fast any racecar in the world can really go. ​","wiki_title":"IRacing Superspeedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-irwindale-speedway":{"location":"Irwindale, California","length_mi":"0.3–0.5","length_km":"0.5–0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Lindom Properties, Arcadia Former Names: Irwindale Speedway (1999 – 2007) Toyota Speedway at Irwindale (2008 – 2011) Irwindale Event Center (2012 - 2017)","opened":"1999","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Heir to the proud tradition of short-track racing, the Irwindale Event Center opened in 1999 and for a quarter of a century, it hosted a variety of local and regional racing series. While it harks back to its old traditions of short-track racing, Irwindale was a modern-filled venue filled with amenities for drivers, crews, fans, and even sponsors as well.","wiki_title":"Irwindale Speedway & Event Center","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States"},"asphalt-kansas-speedway":{"location":"Kansas City, Kansas","length_mi":"0.9–2.4","length_km":"1.4–3.8","turns":"4 – 6","configs_n":"3","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"2001","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"It’s a perfect day for racing at Kansas Speedway in Kansas City, Kansas. This brand new state-of-the-art facility has brought NASCAR to the heartland. Although the tri-oval track design is not unique to Kansas, the slight difference in the banking makes this track truly different.","wiki_title":"Kansas Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-kentucky-speedway":{"location":"Sparta, Kentucky","length_mi":"1.5","length_km":"2.4","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"2000","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to the Kentucky Speedway. Located in the Bluegrass State, Kentucky Speedway is located on 850 acres of land near Sparta, Kentucky. Its one and a half mile tri-oval design, featuring a 1,600 hundred foot long backstretch and turns banked at 17 degrees, makes Kentucky no walk in the park even to NASCAR aficionados. ==","wiki_title":"Kentucky Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2020-06-01"},"asphalt-kentucky-speedway-legacy":{"location":"Sparta, Kentucky","length_mi":"0.3–1.5","length_km":"0.4–2.4","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30–50 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"2000","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to the Kentucky Speedway. Located in the Bluegrass State, Kentucky Speedway is located on 850 acres of land near Sparta, Kentucky. Its one and a half mile tri-oval design, featuring a 1,600 hundred foot long backstretch and turns banked at 17 degrees, makes Kentucky no walk in the park even to NASCAR aficionados.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Kentucky Speedway - 2011","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-kern-county-raceway-park":{"location":"Bakersfield, California","length_mi":"0.1–0.3","length_km":"0.2–0.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"25–35 mph","opened":"2015","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Just located nearby to its bigger paved brother, Bakersfield Speedway at Kevin Harvick's Kern Raceway is a fun dirt oval for many racers and fans alike. While its small layout guarantees some tight fender banging style racing and plenty of cars in traffic, this small dirt oval can surely entertain crowds of all ages.","wiki_title":"Bakersfield Speedway at Kevin Harvick's Kern Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-kevin-harvick-s-kern-raceway":{"location":"Bakersfield, California","length_mi":"0.2–0.5","length_km":"0.4–0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30–35 mph","opened":"2013","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Located along the I-5 corridor near Bakersfield, Kevin Harvick's Kern Raceway is a fantastic half mile oval that features plenty of great racing action and competition. While the track itself is a replacement for Mesa Marin Raceway, both of its oval and dirt oval tracks have plenty of cheering crowds that are hungry for roaring racecars on any raceday.","wiki_title":"Kevin Harvick's Kern Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-knockhill-racing-circuit":{"location":"Dunfermline, Fife","length_mi":"0.3–1.3","length_km":"0.4–2.1","turns":"3 - 10","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Derek Butcher","opened":"1974","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Short Track","bio":"A racetrack that is fun, action, surprises, and more, the Knockhill Racing Circuit is one of the crown racing circuit jewels in the United Kingdom, Located in Scotland, this action packed track with an easy flow of turns and great competition keeps the crowds hungry for more.","wiki_title":"Knockhill Racing Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom","released":"2021-12-06"},"asphalt-la-coliseum-raceway":{"location":"Los Angeles, California","length_mi":"0.3","length_km":"0.4","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"20 mph","opened":"1923","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"A stadium that has been around for nearly a whole century, welcome to the Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum Raceway in downtown Los Angeles. A short quarter mile racetrack gives the crowd plenty of fender banging racing to enjoy. This track's minimal banking gives the drivers a new challenge while also having to battle with other drivers and this track's super tight turns.","wiki_title":"Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum Raceway","wiki_status":"Open (Main Stadium), Closed (Racetrack)","country":"United States"},"asphalt-langley-speedway":{"location":"Hampton, Virginia","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Larry King Law","opened":"1950","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the Langley Speedway in Hampton, Virginia. Immediately adjacent to NASA’s Langley Research Center, the oval has been the launching pad for many NASCAR careers and was the site of nine NASCAR Grand National races. With a length of under 4/10ths of a mile, this track can be tricky to master with under 10 degrees of banking in the turns.","wiki_title":"Larry King Law's Langley Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-lanier-national-speedway":{"location":"Braselton, Georgia","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Bruce Piefke","opened":"1982","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the Lanier Speedway in Braselton, Georgia just across the street from Road Atlanta. The Lanier Speedway is one of the toughest and most brutal short tracks to ever exist in the racing world. With a length of 3/8ths of a mile and 11 degrees of banking in the turns, the drivers practice hard and long since this track does not give you the victory quite so easily.","wiki_title":"Lanier Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-lanier-national-speedway":{"location":"Braselton, Georgia","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Bruce Piefke","opened":"1982","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Returning back to its dirt former glory, the Lanier Speedway Dirt Configuration challenges both car and machine alike. With 11 degrees in its 4 turns and 5 degrees on the straightaways, the fatigue and the skills of the drivers will be pushed to their limits. The hundreds of dealt horsepower on this tiny, dirt oval in Northern Georgia will be no Sunday Drive for the entire field.","wiki_title":"Lanier Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-las-vegas-motor-speedway":{"location":"Las Vegas, Nevada","length_mi":"0.3–2.2","length_km":"0.4–3.5","turns":"4 – 12","configs_n":"6","pit_speed":"30–50 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1996","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to the glamorous Las Vegas Motor Speedway in Las Vegas, Nevada. Home to casino’s and fancy hotels, this one and a half mile tri-oval makes “The Diamond in the Desert” a well deserved racetrack home to the most popular tourist spot in the state.","wiki_title":"Las Vegas Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-lernerville-speedway":{"location":"Sarver, Pennsylvania","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Ted Tomson Track Map ----> Type: Dirt Short-Track D-Shaped Oval","opened":"1967","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome one and all to the Lernerville Speedway. Lernerville is all about high-speed, fast-paced action. Located in Sarver, Pennsylvania, this D-shaped oval is one of the many examples of classic short-track dirt racing. With stiff competition and high banking, this speedway takes no prisoners.","wiki_title":"Lernerville Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2019-12-02"},"dirt-limaland-motorsports-park":{"location":"Elida, Ohio","length_mi":"0.3","length_km":"0.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"University of Northwestern Ohio","opened":"1935","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the Limaland Motorsports Park in Elida, Ohio. This fast 3/10ths mile oval gives thrill and speeds like no other short-track dirt oval. With the fans coming from all over the area to watch the drivers put on a spectacular show, its still known today as Ohio’s “1/4 Mile of Thunder.”","wiki_title":"Limaland Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2018-03-05"},"asphalt-lime-rock-park":{"location":"Lakeville, Connecticut","length_mi":"1.5–1.5","length_km":"2.5–2.5","turns":"7 - 11","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Lime Rock Group, LLC","opened":"1957","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Nestled within the Berkshire Mountains in the northwest corner of Connecticut, Lime Rock Park is as picturesque for visitors as it is challenging for drivers. At a relatively short one and a half miles in length, fans flock from around the eastern seaboard to see great competition at this fantastic circuit.","wiki_title":"Lime Rock Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2019-12-02"},"asphalt-long-beach-street-circuit":{"location":"Long Beach, California","length_mi":"2.0","length_km":"3.2","turns":"11","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"40 mph","owner":"Penske Entertainment Group","opened":"1975","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"From the streets of Los Angeles, welcome to Long Beach. Long Beach is a two mile street circuit with 11 turns winding through the streets of the city's coastline. The location gives the track a downtown feel and with visits from multiple racing series, drivers want to come here to see if they can be victorious in the Golden State.","wiki_title":"Acura Grand Prix of Long Beach","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2020-12-08"},"asphalt-lucas-oil-indianapolis-raceway-park":{"location":"Clermont, Indiana","length_mi":"0.7","length_km":"1.1","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"40 mph","owner":"National Hot Rod Association Nickname: America's Great Race Place","opened":"1960","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"The Lucas Oil Indianapolis Raceway Park is one of America’s premier multiple racing facilities. The track is home to a quarter mile drag strip and its nearly 7/10th mile oval configuration. Finding the fastest line around here has been a daunting challenge to the drivers themselves while still keeping their machine in pristine condition.","wiki_title":"Lucas Oil Indianapolis Raceway Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-lucas-oil-speedway":{"location":"Wheatland, Missouri","length_mi":"0.4–1.1","length_km":"0.6–1.8","turns":"4 - 10","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"25–30 mph","owner":"Lucas Oil Products","opened":"2001","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track; Off-Road","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Lucas Oil Speedway in the heart of the Ozark Highlands. With tight corners but thrilling action giving fans plenty of action on raceday gives this track the nickname, the diamond of dirt tracks.","wiki_title":"Lucas Oil Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-martinsville-speedway":{"location":"Ridgeway, Virginia","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1947","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Hello and welcome to a piece of racing history, the Martinsville Speedway in south central Virginia. Martinsville was opened before NASCAR was even founded. It’s one of the sports original tracks. It’s paperclip shaped half-mile has grown from a dusty pioneer to a beautiful racing facility with personality and unique challenges every time.","wiki_title":"Martinsville Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-miami-international-autodrome":{"location":"Miami, Florida","length_mi":"1.4–3.4","length_km":"2.3–5.4","turns":"13 - 19","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Stephen M. Ross","opened":"2022","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"The Miami International Autodrome is one of America's newest racetracks for grand prix racing and the prowess nature of the facility shows. The modern facilities and grandstands, along with its contemporary look and feel is definitely fitting for America's Monaco. While the racing itself is home to Formula 1's Miami Grand Prix, the track's overall flat nature and tight and twisty complex nature gives drivers a whole new challenge for them to master.","wiki_title":"Miami International Autodrome","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2025-12-08"},"asphalt-michigan-international-speedway":{"location":"Brooklyn, Michigan","length_mi":"2.0","length_km":"3.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"55 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1968","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Superspeedway","bio":"This is the Michigan International Speedway, home to the automobile industry and some great competition. If you like three and four wide racing, then Michigan’s your track. This two mile d-shaped oval allows for great action with its high banks and wide surface. Located just outside the Motor City, drivers are always hoping to put on a great show for the auto industry here.","wiki_title":"Michigan International Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-mid-ohio-sports-car-course":{"location":"Lexington, Ohio","length_mi":"0.5–2.4","length_km":"0.8–3.9","turns":"2 – 15","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"30–45 mph","owner":"Green Savoree Racing Promotions, LLC","opened":"1962","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the Mid-Ohio Sports Car Course in Lexington, Ohio. One of the newest road courses on the NASCAR circuit, competition reigns king here. The full two and a quarter mile road course combines tricky turns and high speeds and with up to 8 degrees of banking in the turns, it has become a classic circuit in all of motorsports.","wiki_title":"Mid-Ohio Sports Car Course","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-misano-world-circuit-marco-simoncelli":{"location":"Misano Adriatico, Emilia-Romagna","length_mi":"0.6–2.6","length_km":"1.0–4.2","turns":"16","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Santa Monica S.p.A","opened":"1972","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Hello and welcome to Misano, one of Italy's top racetracks. Hosting many series to this day, Misano features long straights with chicanes and challenging turns which makes this track a true challenge to any hardened veteran racer. Ever since 1972, this track has always been a stones throw away from the Adriatic Sea making The Adriatic Gem all the more exquisite that pays tribute to the late, great Marco Simoncelli.","wiki_title":"Misano World Circuit Marco Simoncelli","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Italy"},"asphalt-mobility-resort-motegi":{"location":"Motegi, Tochigi Prefecture","length_mi":"0.9–3.0","length_km":"1.4–4.8","turns":"4 – 14","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"37–50 mph","owner":"Honda Motor Co. , Ltd.","opened":"1997","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to Mobility Resort Motegi. An air of anticipation and excitement fills the track as both the cars and stars are set to entertain race fans of all ages. The racetrack is located 60 miles northeast of Tokyo and 100 miles due east of Nagano, home of the 1998 Winter Olympics. This is an exciting track with plenty of room on the straights leading to close, action packed, side-by-side racing.","wiki_title":"Mobility Resort Motegi","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Japan"},"asphalt-motorland-aragon":{"location":"Alcañiz, Aragon","length_mi":"1.6–3.3","length_km":"2.6–5.3","owner":"Marta Gastón","opened":"2009","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to the MotorLand Aragón, Aragón's prestigious road racing circuit. Home to a wide variety of racing ranging from Formula 4's and Touring Cars to the European Le Mans Series and even Motorbikes makes this track both fun and technical that are contained in this tracks challenging turns.","wiki_title":"MotorLand Aragón","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Spain","released":"2023-06-05"},"asphalt-motorsport-arena-oschersleben":{"location":"Oschersleben, Saxony-Anhalt","turns":"8 - 14","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"37 mph","opened":"1997","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in Saxony-Anhalt, Oschersleben is Germany's third permanent motor racing circuit after the Nurburgring and the Hockenheimring. Featuring a multitude of corners, this track has become fast but also tricky to master. With spectator areas above the track, it provides many viewing angles across most of the circuit.","wiki_title":"Motorsport Arena Oschersleben","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Germany"},"asphalt-mount-panorama-circuit":{"location":"Bathurst, New South Wales","length_mi":"3.9","length_km":"6.2","turns":"23","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"31 mph","owner":"National Motor Racing Museum","opened":"1938","difficulty":"Pro","track_type":"Road Course; Street Circuit","bio":"Nestled in Bathurst, Mount Panorama gives fans the thrill of high speeds and tight turns in one package. With over 20 turns, this track is not easy to tame to any pro driver. Known as “The Mountain”, this daunting, dangerous circuit contains high elevation changes and fierce competition that gives \"The Mountain\" its name.","wiki_title":"Mount Panorama Motor Racing Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Australia"},"asphalt-myrtle-beach-speedway":{"location":"Myrtle Beach, South Carolina","length_mi":"0.6","length_km":"0.9","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Speedway Group Inc.","opened":"1958","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Since opening in 1958 and through its transition to pavement in 1974 until its closure in 2020, Myrtle Beach Speedway was not only the scene of great weekly action but, a springboard for stock car racing royalty. The half-mile D-shaped oval is not anything new to the oval racing world but remains quite an adversary to short-track racing. With the track closed since August 2020, this South Carolina racetrack will definitely be missed.","wiki_title":"Myrtle Beach Speedway","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States"},"asphalt-nashville-fairgrounds-speedway":{"location":"Nashville, Tennessee","length_mi":"0.3–0.6","length_km":"0.4–1.0","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"26–35 mph","owner":"Tennessee State Fairgrounds Type: Short-Track Traditional Oval","opened":"1904","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the oldest continually operating track, the Nashville Fairgrounds Speedway in Nashville, Tennessee. Operating since 1904, this 3/5th's mile speedway has been thrilling fans and hosting great competition for well over 100 years. As a matter of fact, this racetrack is older than the famed Indianapolis Motor Speedway by only 5 years and has had 9 name changes, more than any other track in the world today.","wiki_title":"Nashville Fairgrounds Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2020-09-08"},"asphalt-nashville-superspeedway":{"location":"Lebanon, Tennessee","length_mi":"1.3","length_km":"2.1","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Type: Intermediate Tri-Oval","opened":"2001","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Music City and the Nashville Superspeedway. Ever since its opening in 2001, this track has definitely become one of the many oval favorites and still shines on today. With banking ranging from 3 to 14 degrees, this track can still pack a lot of fun for many drivers to please as many spectating fans as possible.","wiki_title":"Nashville Superspeedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2021-06-08"},"asphalt-new-hampshire-motor-speedway":{"location":"Loudon, New Hampshire","length_mi":"0.3–1.6","length_km":"0.4–2.6","turns":"4 – 14","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"30–45 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Nickname: The Magic Mile","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval","bio":"Hello and welcome to Loudon, New Hampshire. At a distance of just over a mile, this squared-off oval has seen some fantastic finishes in its history. Over 70,000 thousand people attend each race, coming from nearby Boston, Providence, and all of New England, to see the action at New Hampshire Motor Speedway.","wiki_title":"New Hampshire Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-new-smyrna-speedway":{"location":"Samsula-Spruce Creek, Florida","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Hart Family","opened":"1967","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Located a few miles down the road from its more celebrated neighbor, New Smyrna Speedway is the place to be for hard-core racers during Speedweeks. The high-banked, half mile oval hosts from stock car racing to open wheel modified cars. Famous NASCAR drivers started their career here and the track has proven to be an increasingly popular test venue among NASCAR’s teams.","wiki_title":"New Smyrna Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-north-wilkesboro-speedway":{"location":"North Wilkesboro, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.6","length_km":"1.0","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1947","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the Appalachian mountains and the North Wilkesboro Speedway. This unique oval is truly one of the NASCAR classics and still is today. With a downhill front straightaway and an uphill back straightaway, no one can deny that the North Wilkesboro Speedway is one of NASCAR’s legendary racetracks.","wiki_title":"North Wilkesboro Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-nurburgring-combined":{"location":"Nürburg, Rhineland-Palatinate","length_mi":"14.8–16.1","length_km":"23.9–25.9","turns":"164 – 170","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Viktor Kharitonin","opened":"1984","difficulty":"World Champion","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"The most fearsome of all racing tracks in the whole world, the Nürburgring Combined is over 14 miles long which features over 160 turns. The famous Karussell turn and the long straight at Döttinger Höhe is one of the highlights of this gruesome race track through the Eifel Mountains in Nurburg, Germany. With many turns here, fowling up results in a drivers race completely shot. Luck and skill are required to master this treacherous circuit known to all drivers around the world as the “Green Hell”.","wiki_title":"Nurburgring Combined","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Germany"},"asphalt-nurburgring-grand-prix-strecke":{"location":"Nürburg, Rhineland-Palatinate","length_mi":"0.9–3.2","length_km":"1.5–5.2","turns":"7 – 16","configs_n":"6","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Viktor Kharitonin","opened":"1984","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located approximately 60 kilometers northwest of Koblenz, the Nurburgring combines short straights with a challenging combination of slow, medium, and fast turns. Whilst the new Nurburgring pales into insignificance compared to the original Nordschleife Circuit, the fatalities of yester year more than justify today’s safety standards which render the old 13 mile loop redundant.","wiki_title":"Nurburgring Grand-Prix-Strecke","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Germany"},"asphalt-nurburgring-nordschleife":{"location":"Nürburg, Rhineland-Palatinate","length_mi":"11.9–12.9","length_km":"19.1–20.8","turns":"154","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Viktor Kharitonin","opened":"1927","difficulty":"Expert","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in the Eifel Mountains in Germany, the Nürburgring Nordschleife is one of the most gruesome race tracks in the world. Skill wins the race here as the track contains over 150 turns and some of the most dangerous corners on any racing circuit in the world. Drivers here must focus on all of these turns and put out their best effort to even put down a decent lap time. The hardest thing they will have to master is being consistent.","wiki_title":"Nurburgring Nordschleife","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Germany"},"asphalt-okayama-international-circuit":{"location":"Mimasaka, Okayama Prefecture","length_mi":"1.3–2.3","length_km":"2.1–3.7","turns":"7 – 11","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Okayama International Circuit Co. , Ltd.","opened":"1990","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Nestled in the mountains of Japan, the Okayama International Circuit is one of the most popular race tracks. Many types of racecars come here to get the thrills of this two and one-thirds mile road course. With variable banking in the turns, one has to be patient in order to be the Senshi at Okayama.","wiki_title":"Okayama International Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Japan","updated":"2023-12-05"},"asphalt-oran-park-raceway":{"location":"Narellan, New South Wales","turns":"6 – 12","configs_n":"6","pit_speed":"20–37 mph","owner":"Singer Car Club","opened":"1962","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Oran Park Raceway, now demolished, was a circuit like no other. With a crossover point that featured a bridge, the tracks 12 turns gave drivers new and exciting corners to get used to. Now part of a housing area, Oran Park Raceway always had a ton of superb racing action for both fans and spectators to enjoy.","wiki_title":"Oran Park Raceway","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"Australia"},"asphalt-oswego-speedway":{"location":"Oswego, New York","length_mi":"0.4–0.6","length_km":"0.6–1.0","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Eric Torrese and John Torrese","opened":"1951","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"The Home of the Super Modified herself, Oswego Speedway is a beautiful 5/8 mile racetrack with a beautiful location right along the Lake Ontario waterfront. Known to many drivers as \"The Big O\" and \"The Steel Palace\", drivers and fans love coming to this racetrack time and time again to experience its well-known cut throat competition and cheering fans.","wiki_title":"Oswego Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-oswego-speedway":{"location":"Oswego, New York","length_mi":"0.6","length_km":"1.0","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Eric Torrese and John Torrese","opened":"1951","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval","bio":"It only happens a few days out of the year, Oswego Speedway's dirt configuration has now become a staple classic for dirt racing fans all over the globe ever since the closure and demolition of the Syracuse Mile. The SuperDIRT week as its known with the tracks usual 4 to 13 degrees of banking in the turns and 6 degrees on the straightaways makes this track quite an exciting place to be. Nearly 10,000 thousand dirt fans cheer loud and proud for their favorite drivers battling for every position during raceday.","wiki_title":"Oswego Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2024-06-03"},"asphalt-oulton-park-circuit":{"location":"Little Budworth, Cheshire","length_mi":"1.7–2.7","length_km":"2.7–4.3","turns":"10 – 17","configs_n":"8","pit_speed":"31 mph","owner":"MotorSport Vision","opened":"1953","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"In Little Budworth, a circuit known as Oulton Park still survives today. Opened in August of 1953, the race track features 17 challenging turns testing drivers skills and patience like never before. With a max length beyond two and a half miles, this track requires a whole new strategy and experience in order to conquer Oulton Park.","wiki_title":"Oulton Park Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom"},"asphalt-oxford-plains-speedway":{"location":"Oxford, Maine","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Tom Mayberry","opened":"1950","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Maine is the northeastern most state of the United States and the 14,000 seat Oxford Plains Speedway is the biggest public facility in the Pine Tree State. Opened in 1950, the facility today features street stocks, legends cars, and more despite the tracks small circular shape. Even though it’s a tiny 3/8ths mile oval, drivers keep coming back to experience its dizzying thrill.","wiki_title":"Oxford Plains Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-phillip-island-circuit":{"location":"Ventnor, Victoria","length_mi":"2.8","length_km":"4.4","turns":"12","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Linfox","opened":"1928","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located on Phillip Island south of Melbourne, the Phillip Island Grand Prix Circuit is home to over two and a half miles of intense road racing. With two tight hairpins and fierce opposition, this track does not play around. With beautiful cliff side edges and spectacular views of the water, this leaves this track in an unique beauty of its own.","wiki_title":"Phillip Island Grand Prix Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Australia"},"asphalt-phoenix-raceway":{"location":"Avondale, Arizona","length_mi":"1.0","length_km":"1.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1964","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to the valley of the sun and the Phoenix Raceway. This gem in the desert has been shining since 1964 with its unique design and beautiful surroundings, its earned its reputation as one of the top visits on the circuit.","wiki_title":"Phoenix Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-pocono-raceway":{"location":"Long Pond, Pennsylvania","length_mi":"2.5","length_km":"4.0","turns":"3","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"55 mph","owner":"Mattco Inc.","opened":"1969","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Superspeedway","bio":"Welcome to the infamous Pocono Raceway in Long Pond, Pennsylvania. This two and a half mile scalene triangular shaped superspeedway features three unique turns with different banking from six to fourteen degrees. With five and six wide racing possible, this track is rightfully known as the “Tricky Triangle.”","wiki_title":"Pocono Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2018-03-05"},"dirt-port-royal-speedway":{"location":"Port Royal, Pennsylvania","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.9","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Juniata County Agricultural Society","opened":"1938","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Port Royal Speedway in the Susquehanna Valley in its namesake town in Pennsylvania. This fast half mile dirt oval known to all dirt oval drivers as The Speed Palace has definitely earned its nickname that plays host to fantastic racing and stiff competition.","wiki_title":"Port Royal Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2022-06-06"},"asphalt-portland-international-raceway":{"location":"Portland, Oregon","length_mi":"2.0–2.0","length_km":"3.1–3.2","turns":"9 - 12","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"40 mph","owner":"City of Portland","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to the Beaver State and the Portland International Raceway. Located within the downtown heart of Oregon's most populated city, Portland features fast straightaways and a short twisty complex that delivers a thrilling two miles full of experience and intense racing action like no other making it the premier road course in the pacific northwest.","wiki_title":"Portland International Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2025-03-10"},"asphalt-qualcomm-circuit-naval-base-coronado":{"location":"San Diego, California","length_mi":"3.4","length_km":"5.5","turns":"16","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"United States Navy","opened":"2026","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"Qualcomm Circuit is NASCAR's newest street circuit built on an active US Navy base near San Diego. The tight and fast sweeping corners here give this track quite a unique feel and character different from other street circuits. The track itself has an interesting scenery of aircraft carriers, fighter jet planes, plane hangars and more which gives The Q a challenge that both fans and drivers all enjoy.","wiki_title":"Qualcomm Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-red-bull-ring":{"location":"Spielberg, Styria","length_mi":"1.1–2.7","length_km":"1.8–4.3","configs_n":"3","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Dietrich Mateschitz Beteiligungs GmbH Type: Road Course","opened":"1969","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located near Knittelfeld in the foothills of the Styrian mountains, the Red Bull Ring combines three long straights with a flowing mix of fast sweeping and slower 90 degree turns. Built on the site of the historic Österreichring, this dedicated motorsports facility is another fine example of modern circuit design.","wiki_title":"Red Bull Ring","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Austria","released":"2021-06-08"},"asphalt-richmond-raceway":{"location":"Richmond, Virginia","length_mi":"0.8","length_km":"1.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"40 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1946","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Whether under the lights or the bright sun of day, the Richmond Raceway is home to excitement. The “Action Track” as its known, combines the best of both worlds, superspeedway speeds and short-track action. At three quarters of a mile on length, it’s not unusual to witness tempers flaring at Richmond.","wiki_title":"Richmond Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-road-america":{"location":"Elkhart Lake, Wisconsin","length_mi":"1.8–4.0","length_km":"2.9–6.5","turns":"6 - 14","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Road America, Inc.","opened":"1955","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located outside the picturesque village of Elkhart Lake, Road America resides. This racetrack is one of the worlds classic road-racing venues and has been hosting a variety of racecars both oval and road spec for over 60 years. At over four miles in length, Road America's challenging turns makes this track demanding even to the most experienced drivers.","wiki_title":"Road America","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-road-atlanta":{"location":"Braselton, Georgia","length_mi":"1.8–2.5","length_km":"2.8–4.1","turns":"10 – 14","configs_n":"3","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"IMSA Holdings, LLC","opened":"1970","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in Braselton, Georgia, the Michelin Raceway Road Atlanta is the hub of the Panoz Motor Sports Group and the American Le Mans Series. With multiple turns, the Michelin Raceway Road Atlanta can decimate a car on raceday. Cars and bikes of all shapes and sizes visit Michelin Raceway Road Atlanta to see what this roller coaster of a race track has in store waiting for them.","wiki_title":"Michelin Raceway Road Atlanta","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-rockingham-speedway":{"location":"Rockingham, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.4–1.6","length_km":"0.6–2.6","turns":"4 – 10","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"15–40 mph","owner":"IHRA","opened":"1965","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval","bio":"Under beautiful Carolina blue skies, welcome to the Rockingham Speedway, also known as “The Rock.” This one mile oval has been thrilling fans for over 30 years with 22 degrees of banking and a “tough on tires” surface, you get fierce competition that gives “The Rock” its name.","wiki_title":"Rockingham Speedway & Entertainment Complex","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-rudskogen-motorsenter":{"location":"Rakkestad, Ostfold","owner":"Mikkelsen Bård Martin","opened":"1990","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"In the most southern part of Norway, the Rudskogen Motorsenter is still around after over 30 years of existence. Featuring a 2 mile road course through Norwegian scenery and rock cuts, this track is definitely the pride and joy of Norwegian racing.","wiki_title":"Rudskogen Motorsenter","wiki_status":"Open","length_mi":"2.0","length_km":"3.3","turns":"14","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"31 mph","country":"Norway"},"asphalt-sachsenring":{"location":"Oberlungwitz, Saxony","length_mi":"2.3","length_km":"3.7","turns":"13","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"31 mph","owner":"HQM Sachsenring GmbH","opened":"1927","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Within the state of Saxony, one of Europe's favorite road courses resides. Hello and welcome to one of Germany's most historic venues, the Sachsenring. Home to mainly MotoGP and DTM races, this twisting 2.281 mile racetrack welcomes road racing vehicles of all shapes and sizes as the drivers battle their way through this technical complex that always remains challenging to rookies and seasoned veterans.","wiki_title":"Sachsenring","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Germany","released":"2024-06-03"},"asphalt-sandown-international-motor-raceway":{"location":"Springvale, Victoria","length_mi":"1.9","length_km":"3.1","turns":"13","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"37 mph","owner":"Melbourne Racing Club","opened":"1962","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Nestled within the bustling suburbs of Melbourne, welcome to the Sandown International Motor Raceway. This bustling 2 mile course is one of the most interesting courses to date combining long straights and some tight turns, which definitely earns this track the nickname \"The Home of Horsepower\".","wiki_title":"Sandown International Motor Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Australia","released":"2022-06-06"},"asphalt-sebring-international-raceway":{"location":"Sebring, Florida","length_mi":"1.8–3.7","length_km":"2.8–6.0","configs_n":"3","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"IMSA Holdings, LLC","opened":"1952","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Laid out on the runways of a former air base and the adjacent roadways, Sebring is the oldest permanent road-racing circuit in the United States. At over three and a half miles, it proves challenging to the drivers to this very day. With an oddly shaped track design and home to the 12 Hour Grand Prix of Endurance, Sebring is still a tough track to master.","wiki_title":"Sebring International Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2022-12-06"},"asphalt-shell-v-power-motorsport-park-at-the-bend":{"location":"Tailem Bend, South Australia","length_mi":"1.1–4.8","length_km":"1.8–7.8","turns":"7 - 35","configs_n":"7","pit_speed":"50–55 mph","owner":"Peregrine Corporation","opened":"2018","difficulty":"Pro","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in Tailem Bend in the state of South Australia, The Bend is one of the world's twistiest tracks. If you like turn-mania, this is definitely the track for you. With many configurations ranging from about a mile to nearly 5 miles in length and total turn count as high as 35 turns, The Bend surely deserves its name home to Supercars, GT Racing, Touring Cars and more gives this track a flashy and fancy feel.","wiki_title":"Shell V-Power Motorsport Park at The Bend","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Australia","released":"2025-06-10"},"asphalt-silverstone-circuit":{"location":"Towcester, Buckinghamshire","length_mi":"1.6–3.7","length_km":"2.6–5.9","turns":"6 – 19","configs_n":"3","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"British Racing Drivers’ Club","opened":"1948","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located just outside Northampton, the fantastic Silverstone Circuit combines two fast straights, slow, medium, and high speed turns. Surrounded by the headquarters of the McLaren Team, this disused airfield in the heart of Formula 1’s so-called Silicon Valley often plays host to one of the most competitive races of the season.","wiki_title":"Silverstone Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom"},"asphalt-silverstone-circuit-2008-legacy":{"location":"Silverstone, Northamptonshire","length_mi":"1.6–3.2","length_km":"2.6–5.1","turns":"6 – 17","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"35–45 mph","owner":"British Racing Drivers' Club Nickname: Home of British Motor Racing","opened":"1948","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located just outside Northampton, the fantastic Silverstone Circuit combines two fast straights, slow, medium, and high speed turns. Surrounded by the headquarters of the McLaren Team, this disused airfield in the heart of Formula 1’s so-called Silicon Valley often plays host to one of the most competitive races of the season.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Silverstone Circuit - 2008","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom"},"asphalt-slinger-speedway":{"location":"Slinger, Wisconsin","length_mi":"0.3–0.3","length_km":"0.4–0.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Todd Thelen","opened":"1948","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Located in southern Wisconsin, the insane but fun Slinger Speedway whirls cars around with high speeds and great action. Not far from the Milwaukee Mile, this track that has been hosting local races since 1948 has been a star shining bright ever since with its steep 33 degrees of banking in the turns and straightaway banking between 6 and 11 degrees has made Slinger a true short track beast in its own right.","wiki_title":"Slinger Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2023-12-05"},"asphalt-snetterton-circuit":{"location":"Norwich, Norfolk","length_mi":"1.0–3.0","length_km":"1.6–4.8","turns":"6 – 13","configs_n":"3","pit_speed":"34 mph","owner":"MotorSport Vision","opened":"1951","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to the Snetterton Circuit in Norwich, Norfolk. Originally part of a Royal Air Force airfield, Snetterton hosts Open Wheel and Sports Cars to create some of the most incredible racing in all of European motorsports. With banking up to three degrees in the tracks’ 13 turns, Snetterton always puts on a great show even to people that do not care about racing.","wiki_title":"Snetterton Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom"},"asphalt-sonoma-raceway":{"location":"Sonoma, California","length_mi":"0.2–2.5","length_km":"0.3–4.1","turns":"12","configs_n":"9","pit_speed":"20–40 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1968","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to the famous Napa Valley of northern California. One of the few road courses on the NASCAR circuit and one of the best in the world, Sonoma Raceway is a beautiful two mile track with multiple turns, testing a drivers skill and patience to the ultimate. The true test for drivers is to try and keep their eyes off the scenery and on the competition at Sonoma.","wiki_title":"Sonoma Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2018-03-05"},"asphalt-south-boston-speedway":{"location":"South Boston, Virginia","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Mattco Inc.","opened":"1957","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"A mecca for Virginian short-track racing for over half a century, South Boston Speedway today bills itself as “America’s Hometown Track.” With a length of just under half a mile, the oval features late models, legends, modifieds, and street stock cars so the fans are never disappointed when race day comes to the South Boston Speedway.","wiki_title":"South Boston Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-southern-national-motorsports-park":{"location":"Lucama, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Michael Diaz","opened":"1993","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"In a little more than two decades, Southern National Motorsports Park has earned a reputation as one of the premier short-tracks in the Carolinas. Opened in 1993, the 17 degree banked 4/10ths mile speedway became part of NASCAR’s Home Tracks program as a host to NASCAR’s Whelen Modified Series. The track may be short on length but, the action still reigns at this tight, impressive oval.","wiki_title":"Southern National Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-st-petersburg-grand-prix":{"location":"St. Petersburg, Florida","length_mi":"1.8","length_km":"2.9","turns":"14","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Green Savoree St. Petersburg, LLC.","opened":"1985","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Street Circuit","bio":"Welcome to St. Petersburg, Florida and its flagship grand prix race sponsored by Firestone. St. Pete is a spectacular 1.8 Mile street circuit weaving in and around the downtown St. Pete area. Home to the IndyCar season opener and more, this facility where a portion of it is on the airport has transformed The Sunshine Race that grew up from troubled times to become a beautiful premier motorsports destination.","wiki_title":"Firestone Grand Prix of St. Petersburg","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2026-03-09"},"asphalt-stafford-motor-speedway":{"location":"Stafford Springs, Connecticut","length_mi":"0.2–0.5","length_km":"0.3–0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"35 mph","opened":"1870","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Built in 1870 for horse racing before automobile racing, Stafford Speedway traces the Modified lineage back to the very beginning of this track and stock car racing. Not as flashy and fancy as the half miles that the Cup Cars go to today, but this busy oval can still put on a fantastic show full of action for the fans and intense competition for the drivers.","wiki_title":"Stafford Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-summit-point-raceway":{"location":"Summit Point, West Virginia","length_mi":"0.6–2.0","length_km":"0.9–3.2","turns":"7 – 10","configs_n":"6","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Bill Scott Racing, Inc.","opened":"1969","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"With the hilly, but high-speed 2 miles of action, Summit Point Motorsports Park offers every challenge a road-racer could desire with tight turns and long straights. All settled in West Virginia’s countryside, it’s still a challenging circuit. The Summit Point Motorsports Park feels like a fast tour over country roads that gives great action for all to see.","wiki_title":"Summit Point Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-suzuka-international-racing-course":{"location":"Suzuka, Mie Prefecture","length_mi":"1.4–3.6","length_km":"2.2–5.8","turns":"9 – 17","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Honda Motor Co. , Ltd.","opened":"1962","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located approximately 70 kilometers southwest of Nagoya, the exciting Suzuka Circuit combines two medium speed straights with a technical arrangement including a hairpin as well as fast sweeping and 90 degree turns. Owned by Honda, Suzuka has a somewhat unique Figure of 8 layout causing the track to cross over itself.","wiki_title":"Suzuka International Racing Course","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Japan"},"asphalt-talladega-superspeedway":{"location":"Lincoln, Alabama","length_mi":"2.7","length_km":"4.3","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"55 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1969","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Superspeedway","bio":"Welcome to the worlds fastest speedway, Talladega Superspeedway in Alabama. Talladega is the biggest, fastest, and most competitive motorsports facility in the world. Speed says it all about this place. Its record breaking two and two-thirds mile tri-oval keeps drivers glued to Earth by virtual 33 degree banking. Freight trains of stock cars in the draft literally caused the Earth to rumble in Alabama.","wiki_title":"Talladega Superspeedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-texas-motor-speedway":{"location":"Fort Worth, Texas","length_mi":"0.2–1.5","length_km":"0.4–2.4","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30–45 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1996","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to Fort Worth and the Texas Motor Speedway. With seating for over 130,000 thousand fans, this motorsports haven represents racing at its finest. Recently repaved, this quad-shaped oval with 20-degree banking has become one of NASCAR’s fastest tracks.","wiki_title":"Texas Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2020-03-02"},"asphalt-texas-motor-speedway-legacy":{"location":"Fort Worth, Texas","length_mi":"0.2–3.4","length_km":"0.4–5.5","turns":"4 – 10","configs_n":"6","pit_speed":"30–50 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1996","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to Fort Worth and the Texas Motor Speedway. With seating for over 150,000 thousand fans, this motorsports haven represents racing at its finest. Recently repaved, this quad-shaped oval with 24-degree banking has become one of NASCAR’s fastest tracks.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Texas Motor Speedway - 2009","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-the-bullring":{"location":"Las Vegas, Nevada","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1985","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"The Bullring at Las Vegas Motor Speedway is racing’s answer to truth in short track action. This little circuit is located a stone’s throw away from the mile and a half tri-oval that is Las Vegas Motor Speedway. With just under 10 degrees of banking, The Bullring is an asphalt oval that’s short on distance, but long on action with great short-track competition.","wiki_title":"The Bullring at Las Vegas Motor Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"dirt-the-dirt-track-at-charlotte":{"location":"Concord, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.7","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc. Type: Dirt Short-Track Traditional Oval","opened":"2000","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Fast, wild, and entertaining, The Dirt Track at Charlotte is one of dirt racing’s highest spectacles. If Eldora is the height of Dirt Oval racing, then The Dirt Track at Charlotte must be a fender behind. Just next door to the famous Charlotte Motor Speedway, this track brings crowds from many parts of the world to see drivers battle for the checkered flag.","wiki_title":"The Dirt Track at Charlotte","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2018-03-05"},"asphalt-the-milwaukee-mile":{"location":"West Allis, Wisconsin","length_mi":"1.0","length_km":"1.6","turns":"4 - 10","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"State of Wisconsin","opened":"1903","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Oval","bio":"Here we are at The Milwaukee Mile, the oldest speedway in the world with auto racing taking place here since 1903. The grandstands offer great views of the track and the one-mile course offers great driving for the competitors.","wiki_title":"Milwaukee Mile Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2026-09-09"},"asphalt-thompson-speedway-motorsports-park":{"location":"Thompson, Connecticut","length_mi":"0.6","length_km":"1.0","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","opened":"1940","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"The terms “Thompson Speedway” and “New England Motorsports” are all but synonymous. The track that became known as the “Indy of the East” was born out of the calamitous hurricane that devastated much of New England in 1938. With the track alive today, this 5/8ths mile that opened in May of 1940 features stock car and open wheel racing like no other. It is a classic circuit for action to endure.","wiki_title":"Thompson Speedway Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-thruxton-circuit":{"location":"Thruxton, Hampshire","length_mi":"2.4","length_km":"3.8","turns":"13","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"50 mph","owner":"Alex Thistlethwayte","opened":"1950","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located in the county of Hampshire, Thruxton Circuit is a well known circuit in the local area that it serves to racing fans both car and bike alike. With turns that are both flowing and sharp, this completely flat circuit with a few elevation changes here and there offer drivers a different kind of strategy and a challenge to go fast with no banking at all.","wiki_title":"Thruxton Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United Kingdom","released":"2024-12-09"},"asphalt-tsukuba-circuit":{"location":"Shimotsuma, Ibaraki Prefecture","length_mi":"0.5–1.3","length_km":"0.8–2.1","turns":"4 – 11","configs_n":"7","pit_speed":"30–37 mph","owner":"Moto Racing JAPAN","opened":"1970","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Tiny and compact, Tsukuba Circuit is one of the most popular road courses in the world. Even though it rarely hosts any major championships these days, Tsukuba is one of the most recognized circuits in all of Japan thanks to being well-known in popular video games. Known as the Home of Time Attack, year round popularity has always soared here.","wiki_title":"Tsukuba Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"Japan","released":"2018-12-03"},"asphalt-usa-international-speedway":{"location":"Lakeland, Florida","length_mi":"0.8","length_km":"1.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Richard Flanzer","opened":"1995","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"A three-quarter mile, semi-banked oval, USA International once hosted a variety of races for a couple of racing series. Located in Lakeland, Florida, it combines long straights and tight turns into a thrilling race track. The track demands a tuned engine and a tough chassis to get around this tracks’ nasty bumps.","wiki_title":"USA International Speedway","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States"},"dirt-usa-international-speedway":{"location":"Lakeland, Florida","length_mi":"0.8","length_km":"1.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"iRacing.com Motorsports Simulations, LLC","opened":"1995","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"A dirt track in Florida to coexist with Volusia Speedway Park, USA International Speedway – Dirt is one of the most fantastic three-quarter mile dirt tracks there is. Even though the dirt cars are more comfortable on shorter dirt race tracks, the competition at USA – Dirt always remains a challenge even to the most experienced.","wiki_title":"USA International Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"asphalt-virginia-international-raceway":{"location":"Alton, Virginia","length_mi":"1.1–4.1","length_km":"1.8–6.6","turns":"10 – 23","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"37–45 mph","owner":"Connie Nyholm","opened":"1957","difficulty":"Advanced","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"A motorsports lazarus, Virginia International Raceway is a race track that came back from the dead after been previously closed in 1974. With the circuit being over three miles long, this road course features elevation change between 350 and 500 feet. The track features multiple turns keeping drivers on their toes making them think twice when viewing the surroundings.","wiki_title":"Virginia International Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2022-12-06"},"asphalt-watkins-glen-international":{"location":"Watkins Glen, New York","length_mi":"2.4–3.5","length_km":"3.9–5.6","turns":"7 – 11","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"40 mph","owner":"NASCAR","opened":"1948","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to the finger lakes region of New York state and Watkins Glen International. This world famous road course leads drivers through a fast, two and a half mile, twisting, twelve turns. With banking ranging from 6 to 10 degrees in the corners and great elevation changes, one always has to be alert in order to conquer Watkins Glen.","wiki_title":"Watkins Glen International","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2021-12-06"},"asphalt-weathertech-raceway-at-laguna-seca":{"location":"Monterey, California","length_mi":"2.2","length_km":"3.6","turns":"11","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"Monterey County","opened":"1957","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca, a classic North American road-racing circuit. This beautiful serpentine ribbon of pavement features the famous Corkscrew turn, the most feared corner in all of the Americas. With 11 turns and nestled in desert highlands, it’s no wonder why the WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca is an automotive gem to many that drive on this legendary circuit.","wiki_title":"WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","updated":"2026-06-09"},"asphalt-willow-springs-international-raceway":{"location":"Rosamond, California","length_mi":"2.5","length_km":"4.0","turns":"9","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"CrossHarbor Capital Partners","opened":"1953","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to the track in the Californian highlands, the Willow Springs Raceway, Willow Springs is a fantastic two and a half mile track with minimal turns and great elevation changes which leads to some great action from the drivers. Located between Los Angeles and Bakersfield, The Big Willow is a great place to race.","wiki_title":"Willow Springs Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2023-06-05"},"asphalt-winton-motor-raceway":{"location":"Benalla, Victoria","turns":"10 - 12","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"34 mph","owner":"Benalla Auto Club","opened":"1961","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Welcome to Australia's action track, the Winton Motor Raceway in Benalla, Victoria. This nearly 2 mile long circuit has been quite the entertainment center for a while in the state. With seating for 30,000 hungry fans and dynamic action, its no wonder why this place is nicknamed \"The Nation's Action Track\".","wiki_title":"Winton Motor Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","length_mi":"1.3–1.9","length_km":"2.0–3.0","country":"Australia","released":"2022-03-08"},"asphalt-world-wide-technology-raceway-gateway":{"location":"Madison, Illinois","length_mi":"1.3–1.6","length_km":"2.0–2.6","turns":"4 – 10","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"45 mph","owner":"Curtis Francois","opened":"1967","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Located in the shadow of the Gateway Arch, the World Wide Technology Raceway lies in the midst of multiple interstate junctions. Once a road course, the track today is now an egg-shaped speedway. This unique track is a fan favorite to all and is literally no stranger with its 10 degrees of banking in the turns.","wiki_title":"World Wide Technology Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-bark-river-international-raceway":{"location":"Bark River, Michigan","length_mi":"1.5","length_km":"2.4","turns":"12","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"The Bark River Lions Club Type: Offroad Truck Dirt Road Course","opened":"1976","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Off-Road","bio":"Home to the annual bark river off-road rumble, the Bark River International Raceway is one of the highlights on any off-road truck series schedule. Featuring tight turns and some curved jumps, this track is definitely a challenging course for all drivers that come here. While this track has to share part of its spotlight with its fellow neighbor, the Crandon International Off-Road Raceway, its a spotlight both will share for many years to come.","wiki_title":"Bark River International Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2021-03-09"},"site-cedar-lake-speedway":{"location":"New Richmond, Wisconsin","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Kaufman Family","opened":"1956","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to Wisconsin and the Cedar Lake Speedway. Fans from around the Midwest gather to see fun and action at this 3/8's mile dirt speedway. Known as “Wisconsin’s Fastest Piece Of Real Estate”, this tricky little track thrills everybody from young children to even the most diehard of fans.","wiki_title":"Cedar Lake Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2020-12-08"},"site-centripetal-circuit":{"location":"Adirondack Mountains, New York","length_mi":"0.1","length_km":"0.2","turns":"1","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"67 mph","owner":"iRacing.com Motorsports Simulations, LLC","opened":"2009","difficulty":"Rookie","bio":"Located in the Adirondack Mountains of New York, the Centripetal Circuit is a large skid pad designed to test cars and their braking, acceleration, handling, and much more. It’s a perfectly flat, perfectly round, circular test track with lane markers placed concentrically every 11 yards or so. It truly is a hidden gem of automotive research and design even to the inexperienced.","wiki_title":"Centripetal Circuit","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-chili-bowl":{"location":"Tulsa, Oklahoma","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Muscogee Nation","opened":"1987","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Welcome to the meanest dirt oval in the country, the Chili Bowl in the heart of Oklahoma. This quarter mile indoor dirt oval has been thrilling fans and entertaining drivers since 1987. Its reputation as being called the “Super Bowl of Midget Racing” still lives on to this very day.","wiki_title":"NOS Energy Drink Chili Bowl Nationals","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-crandon-international-raceway":{"location":"Crandon, Wisconsin","length_mi":"0.8–1.6","length_km":"1.3–2.5","turns":"4 - 8","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Cliff Flannery Type: Offroad Truck Dirt Road Course","opened":"1970","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Off-Road","bio":"Full of land rush excitement and fan surprise, Crandon International Off-Road Raceway in Crandon, Wisconsin provides Lucas Oil trucks with a lot of fender-banging racing. The track itself is full of daring short jumps and a few sharp corners that can definitely be a challenge to any hardcore off-road racer. A one and a half mile layout with 8 turns and variable banking makes The Big House a very known presence in the off-road racing world.","wiki_title":"Crandon International Off-Road Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2020-09-08"},"site-daytona-international-speedway-rallycross":{"location":"Daytona Beach, Florida","length_mi":"0.7–0.9","length_km":"1.1–1.4","turns":"8 - 9","configs_n":"4","owner":"iRacing.com Motorsports Simulations, LLC","opened":"2014","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Rallycross","bio":"Not far from its prestigious speedway, Daytona Rallycross and off-road circuit blends both asphalt and dirt racing to create racing like no other. Its 12 turns and its massive jump on the backstretch makes this track a stranger to inexperience rallycross drivers. At a length of just over three-quarters of a mile, Daytona Rallycross and Dirt Road gives drivers more than enough competition than what they can handle.","wiki_title":"Daytona Rallycross and Dirt Road","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-firebird-motorsports-park":{"location":"Chandler, Arizona","length_mi":"0.7","length_km":"1.1","turns":"5","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","opened":"1983","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Off-Road","bio":"Located in the desert of Arizona, the Firebird Motorsports Park is one of the toughest offroad truck races in the United States. With banking in the turns up to 4 degrees and fast acceleration on the straightaways, the jumps and the action created here makes this track truly fun for both the fans and drivers.","wiki_title":"Firebird Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-knoxville-raceway":{"location":"Knoxville, Iowa","length_mi":"0.6","length_km":"0.9","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Marion County Fair Association","opened":"1954","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Sprint Car Capital of the World, the Knoxville Raceway is one of many dirt track favorites. Located in Knoxville, Iowa, the half mile dirt-clay oval is home to sprint cars and late models. The 7 degrees of banking in the turns make the cars tear up the track for some of the greatest racing in all of dirt competition.","wiki_title":"Knoxville Raceway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2017-12-04"},"site-kokomo-speedway":{"location":"Kokomo, Indiana","length_mi":"0.3","length_km":"0.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"O’Connor Family","opened":"1947","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"It’s a tight dirt oval, but home to fantastic racing. Welcome to the Kokomo Speedway in Kokomo, Indiana. This quarter mile dirt-clay oval that opened in 1947 thrills both the drivers and the fans. With 10 degrees of banking in the turns and 4 degrees on the straightaways, Kokomo Speedway keeps drivers on their feet as they battle for the positions that lead to winning or losing.","wiki_title":"Kokomo Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2018-09-05"},"site-lanier-national-speedway-dirt":{"location":"Braselton, Georgia","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Bruce Piefke","opened":"1982","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Returning back to its dirt former glory, the Lanier Speedway Dirt Configuration challenges both car and machine alike. With 11 degrees in its 4 turns and 5 degrees on the straightaways, the fatigue and the skills of the drivers will be pushed to their limits. The hundreds of dealt horsepower on this tiny, dirt oval in Northern Georgia will be no Sunday Drive for the entire field.","wiki_title":"Lanier Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-lincoln-speedway":{"location":"Abbottstown, Pennsylvania","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"25 mph","owner":"Alan Kreitzer","opened":"1952","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"One of Pennsylvania's most well-known racetracks, Lincoln Speedway sits in the heart of southern Pennsylvania's Pigeon Hills between the towns of York and Gettysburg. With a 3/8's mile layout and over 6,000 roaring fans, dirt racing at this track remains the highlight of southern Pennsylvania racing even after 50 years of racing.","wiki_title":"Lincoln Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2022-12-06"},"site-lankebanen-hellrx":{"location":"Hell, Trøndelag","owner":"Norwegian Automobile Federation","opened":"1987","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Rallycross","bio":"The Lånkebanen is one of Scandinavia’s best known rallycross circuits while also featuring a few gravel sections. Located within the mountainous landscape that defines Norway in its majestic beauty, the Lånkebanen is one of rallycross’ best circuits to date.","wiki_title":"Lånkebanen","wiki_status":"Open","length_mi":"0.5–0.7","length_km":"0.7–1.1","turns":"7 - 8","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"20–35 mph","country":"Norway","released":"2020-03-02"},"site-michigan-international-speedway-2009":{"location":"Brooklyn, Michigan","length_mi":"2.0","length_km":"3.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"55 mph","owner":"International Speedway Corporation","opened":"1968","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Superspeedway","bio":"This is the Michigan International Speedway, home to the automobile industry and some great competition. If you like three and four wide racing, then Michigan’s your track. This two mile d-shaped oval allows for great action with its high banks and wide surface. Located just outside the Motor City, drivers are always hoping to put on a great show for the auto industry here.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Michigan International Speedway - 2009","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-millbridge-speedway":{"location":"Salisbury, North Carolina","length_mi":"0.2","length_km":"0.3","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"20 mph","owner":"The Burnett Family","opened":"1993","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Oval; Short Track","bio":"Just north of the famed Charlotte Motor Speedway, the Millbridge Speedway packs a lot of fun for its small size. While the banking in this track is quite minimal, that doesn't mean the competitors are any less fierce. Home to micro sprints and the like, this track is a fan favorite to the many locals that it serves within the state.","wiki_title":"Millbridge Speedway","country":"United States","released":"2024-03-05"},"site-mount-washington-auto-road":{"location":"Jackson, New Hampshire","length_mi":"7.6","length_km":"12.2","turns":"138","configs_n":"2","owner":"Pacific Group Resorts Inc. Nickname: The Climb To The Clouds Former Names: Mt. Washington by the Auto Road (1861 - 1969) Mt. Washington Auto Road (1970 - 1993, 2002 - Present) Mt. Washington Auto Road at Great Glen (1994 - 2001)","opened":"1861","difficulty":"Expert","track_type":"Rally Stage","bio":"Hello and welcome to the climb to the clouds herself, the Mount Washington Auto Road. Ever since competition began here in 1904, this fierce 7.60 mile hillclimb has been one of the most trickiest tracks in the entire United States. Located in upstate New Hampshire, this tight and twisty complex with 138 turns in all makes sure that drivers pay attention at all times.","wiki_title":"Mount Washington Auto Road","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-new-jersey-motorsports-park":{"location":"Millville, New Jersey","length_mi":"2.3","length_km":"3.6","turns":"14 – 18","configs_n":"4","pit_speed":"35 mph","owner":"N.J. Scott","opened":"2008","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course","bio":"Located adjacent to a former US Army Air Corps fighter pilot training field, New Jersey Motorsports Park pays homage to its legacy by naming its featured circuit “The Thunderbolt.” It’s two and one quarter shaped layout features multiple turns that may throw drivers off their A-Game.","wiki_title":"New Jersey Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-phoenix-raceway-2008":{"location":"Avondale, Arizona","length_mi":"1.0–1.5","length_km":"1.6–2.4","turns":"4 – 13","configs_n":"2","pit_speed":"30–45 mph","owner":"International Speedway Corporation","opened":"1964","difficulty":"Clubman","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval","bio":"Welcome to the valley of the sun and the Phoenix Raceway. This gem in the desert has been shining since 1964 with its unique design and beautiful surroundings, its earned its reputation as one of the top visits on the circuit.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Phoenix Raceway - 2008","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-pocono-raceway-2009":{"location":"Long Pond, Pennsylvania","length_mi":"1.0–2.5","length_km":"1.6–4.0","turns":"3 – 13","configs_n":"5","pit_speed":"35–55 mph","owner":"Mattco Inc.","opened":"1969","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Superspeedway","bio":"Welcome to the infamous Pocono Raceway in Long Pond, Pennsylvania. This two and a half mile scalene-triangular shaped superspeedway features three unique turns with different banking from six to fourteen degrees. With five and six wide racing possible, this track is rightfully known as the “Tricky Triangle.”","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Pocono Raceway - 2009","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-texas-motor-speedway-2009":{"location":"Fort Worth, Texas","length_mi":"0.2–3.4","length_km":"0.4–5.5","turns":"4 – 10","configs_n":"6","pit_speed":"30–50 mph","owner":"Speedway Motorsports, Inc.","opened":"1996","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Road Course; Oval; Roval; Intermediate","bio":"Welcome to Fort Worth and the Texas Motor Speedway. With seating for over 150,000 thousand fans, this motorsports haven represents racing at its finest. Recently repaved, this quad-shaped oval with 24-degree banking has become one of NASCAR’s fastest tracks.","wiki_title":"(Legacy) Texas Motor Speedway - 2009","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-usa-international-speedway-dirt":{"location":"Lakeland, Florida","length_mi":"0.8","length_km":"1.2","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"iRacing.com Motorsports Simulations, LLC","opened":"1995","difficulty":"Rookie","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"A dirt track in Florida to coexist with Volusia Speedway Park, USA International Speedway – Dirt is one of the most fantastic three-quarter mile dirt tracks there is. Even though the dirt cars are more comfortable on shorter dirt race tracks, the competition at USA – Dirt always remains a challenge even to the most experienced.","wiki_title":"USA International Speedway - Dirt","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-volusia-speedway-park":{"location":"Barberville, Florida","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Dean Miracle","opened":"1968","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Known as the “Fastest Dirt Half Mile in the World,” Volusia Speedway Park is a favorite stop on both the World of Outlaws and Super DIRTcar Series calendars. Located in Barberville, Florida, the track has undergone a variety of changes since 1968, but the racing has always stayed competitive to keep the fans’ hunger for action alive. With 10 degrees of banking in the turns, the track and its nickname sells for itself.","wiki_title":"Volusia Speedway Park","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"},"site-weedsport-speedway":{"location":"Weedsport, New York","length_mi":"0.4","length_km":"0.6","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"20 mph","owner":"Al Heinke Former Names: Weedsport Speedway (1955 - 1980, 2013 - Present) Cayuga County Fair Speedway (1981 - 2012)","opened":"1955","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Hello and welcome to the Weedsport Speedway. At over five decades old, drivers that come to Weedsport still love to duke it out at this D-Shaped dirt oval. The 11 degrees of banking in the turns and the fast attainable speeds here makes this track go from a Sunday drive to a champion level. This has resulted in hundreds of fans cheering for their favorite driver.","wiki_title":"Weedsport Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States","released":"2020-09-08"},"site-wild-west-motorsports-park":{"location":"Sparta, Nevada","length_mi":"0.9","length_km":"1.5","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"25 mph","owner":"Norm Dianda","opened":"2012","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Off-Road","bio":"In the dusty desert of Nevada not far from Reno, the Wild West Motorsports Park even after half a decade stands its ground. One of the more exhilarating Offroad Truck Dirt Road Courses within the Western United States, fans from around the area come to visit this action packed race track for some action packed racing featuring tight turns and tall jumps.","wiki_title":"Wild West Motorsports Park","wiki_status":"Defunct","country":"United States","released":"2019-06-03"},"site-williams-grove-speedway":{"location":"Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania","length_mi":"0.5","length_km":"0.8","turns":"4","configs_n":"1","pit_speed":"30 mph","owner":"Kathleen Hughes","opened":"1939","difficulty":"Novice","track_type":"Dirt Oval; Short Track","bio":"Hearkening back to a classic era in American racing, Williams Grove Speedway features history like no other dirt track on the circuit. The long straights and tight turns challenge the dirt drivers to a whole new level. Located just south of Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania, this track has since become woven into the DNA of American racing as we know it today.","wiki_title":"Williams Grove Speedway","wiki_status":"Open","country":"United States"}},"credit":"Specs and descriptions: iRacing Wiki (iracing.fandom.com), community-written."};
